#: dialog/acompu.msg:115
msgid "You find some files containing the keywords \"GECK\" and \"Vault\"."
msgstr "Tu as trouvé des fichiers concernant le J.E.K et les Abris."

#: dialog/acompu.msg:116
msgid "Browse files pertaining to \"GECK\"."
msgstr "[Lire le fichier à propos du J.E.K]"

#: dialog/acompu.msg:117
msgid "Browse files pertaining to \"Vault\"."
msgstr "[Lire le fichier à propos des Abris]"

#: dialog/acompu.msg:118
msgid "The search program seems to be a little too difficult for you."
msgstr "Le programme de recherche semble être un peu trop compliqué pour toi."

#: dialog/acompu.msg:119
msgid ""
"Your eyes widen and your heart quickens as you discover what appears to be "
"an old advertisement for a Garden of Eden\n"
" Creation Kit. The ad depicts a grinning cartoon guy in a vault suit holding "
"up a large case that says, \"Survival Kit\". It's\n"
" almost as if the smiling bastard is taunting you."
msgstr ""
"J.E.K (Jardin d'Eden en Kit) est un kit de survie standard présent dans tous "
"les abris. Il est censé être utilisé après être sorti de l'abri pour créer "
"un nouveau monde."

#: dialog/acompu.msg:120
msgid ""
"You browse over the files, which contain mostly government propaganda for "
"how amazing life in the Vaults would be.\n"
" You learn that in the mid-21st century, the US government commissioned "
"Vault-Tec to construct 122 Vaults across the United States.\n"
" These Vaults were meant to serve as shelters for up to 1,000 US citizens in "
"the event of a nuclear holocaust. Within the safe confines\n"
" of the underground Vaults, the Vault Dwellers could live out a luxurious "
"existence as they await the signal informing them that the\n"
" surface world is once again inhabitable."
msgstr ""
"Les Abris ont été conçus par Vault-Tec au milieu du 21ème siècle. Ils "
"étaient destinés à servir de refuge aux citoyens américains pendant la "
"guerre."

#: dialog/acompu.msg:121
msgid ""
"As you search through the system you find hundreds of digitized books and "
"magazines categorized on the hard drive. You\n"
" wouldn't even know where to begin searching for something of use."
msgstr ""
"Lors de tes recherches, tu trouves des centaines de livres et de magazines "
"au format numérique répertoriés sur le disque dur. Tu ne saurais pas même "
"par où commencer à chercher quelque chose d'utile."

#: dialog/acompu.msg:122
msgid ""
"As you search through the system you find hundreds of digitized books and "
"magazines categorized on the hard drive. Since\n"
" you are skilled in how information is usually stored, perhaps searching by "
"topic would yield something of use."
msgstr ""
"Lors de tes recherches, tu trouves des centaines de livres et de magazines "
"au format numérique répertoriés sur le disque dur. Puisque tu connais les "
"méthodes usuelles de classement de l'information, peut-être qu'une recherche "
"par thème révélera quelque chose d'intéressant."

#: dialog/acompu.msg:124
msgid ""
"According to the ad, the kit includes a \"Base Replicator Unit\", which "
"\"replicates food and basic items needed for building\n"
" your new world\", a \"Holodisc Reader with Library\", which \"includes "
"selections from the Library of Congress, complete set of encyclopedias,\n"
" and other life saving information, all contained on four-hundred and sixty "
"handy holodiscs!\" and it even contains a \"Miniature Pen Flashlight!\"\n"
" Surely, this miracle device is exactly what you need to save your dying "
"village."
msgstr ""
"D'après la pub, le kit comprend une *Unité Support à la Réplication*, "
"laquelle *réplique la nourriture et les objets de base nécessaires pour la "
"construction de votre nouveau monde*, un *Lecteur d'Holodisques avec sa "
"bibliothèque*, qui contient un *assortiment d'encyclopédies de la "
"bibliothèque du Congrès, et d'autres informations vitales, le tout contenu "
"dans 460 holodisques faciles à utiliser !* et il comprend même un *crayon "
"lampe-torche miniature !*. Sans aucun doute, cet appareil prodigieux est "
"exactement ce dont tu as besoin pour sauver ton village mourant."

#: dialog/acompu.msg:125 dialog/acompu.msg:400
msgid "Read more."
msgstr "[En lire plus]"

#: dialog/acompu.msg:126
msgid ""
"You continue browsing the files, but the only mention you find of Vault 13, "
"simply states that it's located in California,\n"
" which doesn't help you much."
msgstr ""
"Tu continues à parcourir les fichiers, mais la seule mention que tu trouves "
