#: dialog/nhmyron.msg:6208 dialog/ocgoris.msg:216 dialog/vcandy.msg:127
#: dialog/vcandy.msg:163 dialog/zidcegrl.msg:2262
msgid "?"
msgstr "?"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:141
msgid "Me ready. "
msgstr "Moi prêt. "

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:142
msgid "Me not ready yet."
msgstr "Pas encore."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:143
msgid "I think so."
msgstr "Je crois que oui."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:144
msgid "No, give me a minute."
msgstr "Non, attends encore une minute."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:145
msgid ""
"Excellent! Your equipment will be kept in the trunk outside of the room.\n"
" You can get it after the fight. Let the fight begin! Good luck to you "
msgstr ""
"Parfait ! Tes affaires vont être placées dans le coffre à l'extérieur de la "
"salle, tu pourras les récupérer après le combat. Que le combat commence ! "
"Bonne chance à toi "

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:147
msgid "It is good to see you again, Chosen One. How may I help you?"
msgstr "Je suis content de te revoir, Etre Elu. Que puis-je faire pour toi ?"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:148
msgid "Me want visit temple again."
msgstr "Moi vouloir visiter temple encore."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:149
msgid "Want fight again?"
msgstr "Vouloir encore combattre ?"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:150
msgid "Just say hello. Me go now."
msgstr "Juste dire bonjour. Moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:151
msgid "I'd like to visit the temple again."
msgstr "J'aimerais visiter le temple à nouveau."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:152
msgid "Hello, Cameron. Ready for another fight?"
msgstr "Bonjour, Dumar. Prêt pour un autre combat ?"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:153
msgid "Just thought I'd say hi. See you later."
msgstr "Je venais juste te dire bonjour. A plus tard."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:154
msgid ""
"Take the path to my left, Chosen One. It leads to the temple proper.\n"
" The cave entrance behind me will return you to the last chamber."
msgstr ""
"Prends le chemin situé à ma gauche. Il mène directement au temple. La grotte "
"constitue l'entrée arrière."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:155 dialog/ccchris.msg:183 dialog/ccmedgrd.msg:120
#: dialog/ccquincy.msg:134
msgid "Okay, me go."
msgstr "Ok, moi partir."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:156 dialog/vcskeeve.msg:117
msgid "All right. Thanks."
msgstr "D'accord. Merci."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:157
msgid ""
"No thank you, Chosen One. I still carry the bruises from our last encounter "
"and will need\n"
" years to recover!"
msgstr ""
"Non merci. J'ai encore les bleus de notre dernière rencontre et il va me "
"falloir des années pour m'en remettre !"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:158
msgid "Go bye, Cameron."
msgstr "Bonne journée, Dumar."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:159
msgid "Ha! Good day to you, Cameron."
msgstr "Ha ! Bonne journée, Dumar."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:160
msgid "Chosen One, my ass. I am going to make you the dead one!"
msgstr "Etre Elu, mon cul ! Je vais te faire ta fête !"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:161
msgid "You have defeated me. You are worthy, Chosen One."
msgstr "Tu m'as vaincu. Tu es digne de respect, Etre Elu."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:165
msgid ""
"I disagree with you. I think that a peaceful solution to any problem is "
"possible."
msgstr ""
"Je ne suis pas d'accord avec toi. Je pense qu'il existe une solution "
"pacifique à tous les problèmes."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:166
msgid "You may be correct, "
msgstr "Tu as peut-être raison, "

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:167
msgid ""
", but not in our current situation. You must defeat me to succeed in your "
"trial."
msgstr ""
", mais pas dans la situation actuelle. Tu dois me vaincre pour réussir ton "
"épreuve."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:168
msgid ""
"Look, I don't know all of your strengths and weaknesses, and you don't know "
"mine.\n"
" Accidents do happen, so what if one of us inadvertently kills the other? "
"Let's just\n"
" end this now rather than take that chance, okay?"
msgstr ""
"Ecoute, je ne connais ni tes forces ni tes faiblesses et tu ne connais pas "
"les miennes. Les accidents sont vite arrivés... et si l'un d'entre nous "
"tuait l'autre par inadvertance... ? Arrêtons tout ceci pour ne pas prendre "
"ce risque, d'accord ?"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:169
msgid ""
"Hmm... I see your point. I wouldn't want to be responsible for\n"
" killing you when all I meant to do was test your mettle. Very well -- you "
"may\n"
" pass, Chosen One."
msgstr ""
"Hum... Je comprends ton point de vue. Je n'aimerais pas être responsable de "
"ta mort alors que je cherchais simplement à tester ton courage. Très bien, "
"tu peux passer, Etre Elu."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:170
msgid ""
"Hmm... I see your point. However, we must still do battle. I will\n"
" simply take care not to hurt you too much."
msgstr ""
"Hum... Je comprends ton point de vue. Mais nous devons quand même nous "
"battre. Je vais juste veiller à ne pas te faire trop mal."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:171
msgid "Thanks! I'll see you back in the village."
msgstr "Merci ! Je te reverrai au village."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:200
msgid ""
"I don't seem to remember our last battle, Chosen One. I will always wonder "
"how you managed\n"
" to get past me."
msgstr ""
"Il ne me semble pas me souvenir de notre dernier combat. Je me demanderai "
"toujours comment tu as réussi à passer."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:201
msgid ""
"You have a tongue of purest silver, Chosen One. Your skill with words will "
"open many doors\n"
" for you."
msgstr ""
"Tes paroles sont d'or, Etre Elu. Ton éloquence t'ouvrira de nombreuses "
"portes."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:300
msgid ""
"And to you as well, Chosen One. May the spirits guide you on your quest."
msgstr ""
"Et pour toi aussi, Etre Elu. Puissent les esprits te guider dans ta quête."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:301
msgid "Thanks, Cameron."
msgstr "Merci, Dumar."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:302
msgid ""
"Chosen One, I could not help but notice that you lack strong combat skills. "
"It has been my experience that you cannot always rely on your wits or words "
"for protection. With your permission I will teach you a few things that I "
"think you will find most useful."
msgstr ""
"Être Elu, j'ai remarqué que tes compétences au combat étaient loin d'être "
"parfaites. Je sais, par expérience, qu'on ne peut pas toujours compter sur "
"son intelligence ou ses paroles pour se protéger. Avec ta permission, je "
"vais t'enseigner quelques choses qui, je pense, te seront très utiles."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:303
msgid "Yes, you teach."
msgstr "Oui, toi apprendre à moi."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:304
msgid "No, me not need."
msgstr "Non, moi pas avoir besoin."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:305
msgid "Yes, please teach me all that you can."
msgstr "Oui, je t'en prie, apprends-moi tout ce que tu sais."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:306
msgid "Thanks, but I think I can handle myself just fine."
msgstr "Merci, mais je crois pouvoir me débrouiller seul."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:307
msgid ""
"You learn well, Chosen One. I think you will be able to handle yourself in a "
"fight now. However, remember that even the strongest of warriors must "
"sometimes retreat. There is no shame in living to fight another day."
msgstr ""
"Tu apprends vite, Être Elu. Je pense que tu devrais savoir te battre "
"maintenant. Cependant, n’oublie pas que même les guerriers les plus "
"puissants doivent parfois battre en retraite. Il n’y a aucune honte à rester "
"en vie pour combattre un autre jour."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:308 dialog/actemvil.msg:311
msgid "Me thank you, Cameron."
msgstr "Moi remercier toi, Dumar."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:309
msgid "Thanks, Cameron. I will remember your words."
msgstr "Merci, Dumar. Je me souviendrai de tes paroles."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:310
msgid "Very well. Return to me if you change your mind."
msgstr "Très bien. Reviens me voir si tu changes d'avis."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:312
msgid "Thanks, Cameron. I will remember your offer."
msgstr "Merci, Dumar. Je me souviendrai de ton offre."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:400
msgid ""
"Do you ever think about stepping down from your position as the Temple's "
"final trial? I mean, it can be pretty risky."
msgstr ""
"T'arrive-t-il de penser à te retirer de ton poste à la dernière épreuve du "
"temple ? Je veux dire, ça peut être assez risqué."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:401
msgid ""
"Life is a constant series of risks, Chosen One. With each new dawn, every "
"one of us takes a risk simply by stepping from our homes to greet the "
"unknown day. Why do you ask?"
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, la vie est une constante prise de risques. A chaque nouvelle "
"aurore, chacun d'entre nous prend un risque simplement en sortant de sa "
"tente pour accueillir le jour nouveau. Pourquoi me demandes-tu ça ?"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:402
msgid "No reason. I'll talk with you later, Cameron."
msgstr "Sans raison. A plus tard, Dumar."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:403
msgid ""
"Well, I was just thinking about what happened to your predecessor, you know, "
"during his battle with... uh, \"He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named\"."
msgstr ""
"Hé bien, j'étais en train de penser à ce qui est arrivé à ton prédécesseur, "
"tu sais, lors de son combat face à... euh, Celui-Qui-Ne-Peut-Etre-Nommé."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:410
msgid ""
"Ah, that was a dark day, indeed, for our tribe lost two good men: one in "
"body, the other in spirit. But the foul deed of that day is no concern of "
"mine. My time will come when the Gods deem it so."
msgstr ""
"Ha, ce fut un jour sombre, en effet, car notre tribu a perdu deux bons "
"éléments : un par le corps et l'autre par l'esprit. Mais l'action vile de ce "
"jour-là ne me concerne pas. Le jour viendra où les Dieux jugeront qu'il doit "
"en être ainsi."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:411
msgid "And may that day be a long time coming. Good day, Cameron."
msgstr "Et puisse ce jour être encore loin. Bonne journée, Dumar."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:412
msgid ""
"Are they even going to have other people attempt the Temple? Hasn't it "
"already been determined that I'm the Chosen One?"
msgstr ""
"Va-t-il y avoir d'autres personnes à tenter l'épreuve du temple ? N'est-il "
"pas déjà établi que je suis l'Etre Elu ?"

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:420
msgid ""
"There will always be a need to test the might of our people. And I take "
"great honor in doing my part."
msgstr ""
"Nous aurons toujours besoin de tester la force de notre peuple. Et c'est un "
"immense honneur pour moi d'y participer."

#: dialog/actemvil.msg:421
msgid "Alright, I'll see you later, Cameron."
msgstr "Bien, à plus tard, Dumar."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:100
msgid "You see a male villager."
msgstr "Tu vois un villageois."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:101
msgid "You see a female villager."
msgstr "Tu vois une villageoise."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:150
msgid "A kindly member of your village."
msgstr "Un gentil membre de ton village."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:152
msgid ""
"Hello! I hear you are the Chosen One. Now, perhaps, our village can be saved."
msgstr ""
"Bonjour ! J'ai entendu dire que tu es l'Etre Elu. Maintenant, notre village "
"va peut-être pouvoir être sauvé."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:153
msgid "Can you tell me where I can find more healing powder?"
msgstr "Peux-tu me dire où trouver plus de poudre de guérison ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:154 dialog/acvillgr.msg:170 dialog/acwarior.msg:154
#: dialog/acwarior.msg:170
msgid "What can you tell me of the traders who trade with us?"
msgstr "Que peux-tu me dire des marchands qui traitent avec nous ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:155
msgid "It is good to see you, but I must be going."
msgstr "Ca fait plaisir de te voir, mais je dois partir."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:156
msgid "Gods protect you on your journey."
msgstr "Que les dieux te protègent au cours de ton voyage."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:157 dialog/acwarior.msg:157
msgid "I do have a question for you."
msgstr "J'ai une question à te poser."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:158 dialog/acwarior.msg:158
msgid "Goodbye, my friend."
msgstr "Au revoir."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:159
msgid "Go see Hakunin in the northern corner of the village. He can help you."
msgstr "Va voir Hakunin au Nord du village. Il peut t'aider."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:161
msgid ""
"Oh, it's not my place to deal with the traders. Talk to Mynoc, the guardian "
"of the\n"
" great bridge. He sees them all."
msgstr ""
"Oh, moi je ne traite pas avec les marchands. Parle à Mynoc, le gardien du "
"grand pont. Il les voit tous."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:163
msgid "Could you tell me where the great bridge is located?"
msgstr "Peux-tu me dire où se trouve le grand pont ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:164 dialog/acvillgr.msg:167 dialog/acvillgr.msg:186
#: dialog/acwarior.msg:164 dialog/acwarior.msg:167 dialog/acwarior.msg:183
msgid "One more question, if I may."
msgstr "Encore une question, si je puis me permettre."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:165
msgid "Good joke, Chosen One! You know where it is. That way -- to the south."
msgstr ""
"La bonne blague, l'Etre Elu ! Tu sais bien où il se trouve. Par là, vers le "
"Sud."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:168 dialog/acwarior.msg:168
msgid "Of course, what is it?"
msgstr "Bien sûr, de quoi s'agit-il ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:169 dialog/acvillgr.msg:184 dialog/acwarior.msg:169
#: dialog/acwarior.msg:181
msgid "Could you tell me where I can find some healing herbs?"
msgstr "Où puis-je trouver des herbes médicinales ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:171 dialog/acwarior.msg:171 dialog/ccdrgrd.msg:111
#: dialog/ccquincy.msg:107 dialog/dcfranki.msg:220 dialog/dcfred.msg:298
#: dialog/dctyler.msg:265 dialog/dctyler.msg:716 dialog/dcvic.msg:2404
#: dialog/ectrappr.msg:109 dialog/fcbadger.msg:217 dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:110
#: dialog/fsface.msg:126 dialog/fsface.msg:133 dialog/gclenny.msg:405
#: dialog/gclenny.msg:415 dialog/gclenny.msg:424 dialog/gclenny.msg:443
#: dialog/gclenny.msg:463 dialog/gclenny.msg:479 dialog/gclenny.msg:493
#: dialog/gclenny.msg:503 dialog/gclenny.msg:513 dialog/gclenny.msg:523
#: dialog/gclenny.msg:533 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:302 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:305
#: dialog/hcmarcus.msg:352 dialog/hcmicky.msg:113 dialog/kcsulik.msg:895
#: dialog/mcjo.msg:264 dialog/ocsandy.msg:109 dialog/scelise.msg:180
#: dialog/scgunthr.msg:136 dialog/scmerk.msg:189 dialog/scrobo.msg:128
#: dialog/vcskeeve.msg:201 dialog/vcwalace.msg:140
msgid "Never mind."
msgstr "Ca ne fait rien."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:172
msgid ""
"Oh gods -- may the spirit of the Founder guide you. If you're the Chosen "
"One, we're\n"
" going to need it."
msgstr ""
"Grands Dieux. Puisse l'esprit du Fondateur te guider. Si tu es l'Etre Elu, "
"nous allons en avoir besoin."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:173
msgid "Uun Ga."
msgstr "Ounga."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:174
msgid "Have a safe journey."
msgstr "Bon voyage."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:175 dialog/acwarior.msg:175
msgid "????"
msgstr "????"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:176
msgid "We're doomed! You have failed your quest."
msgstr "Nous sommes condamnés ! Ta quête a échoué."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:177
msgid "You cannot continue like this."
msgstr "Tu ne peux pas continuer comme ça."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:182
msgid "You are evil. The Chosen One is evil!"
msgstr "Tu es démoniaque. L'Etre Elu est démoniaque !"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:183
msgid "They come to our village from the east, but their goods are poor."
msgstr ""
"Ils viennent au village de l'Est... mais leurs marchandises sont de mauvaise "
"qualité."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:300
msgid ""
"Hello, Chosen One. Nice to see you again. I pray that your holy quest is "
"going well. Is there something I can help you with?"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour, Etre Elu. Quel plaisir de te revoir ! Je prie pour que ta quête "
"aboutisse. Puis-je faire quelque chose pour toi ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:301
msgid ""
"Chosen One, our people are dying. You must hurry your search for the holy "
"GECK. What may I do to aid you in this most holy of quests?"
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, notre peuple se meurt. Tu dois te dépêcher de trouver le saint "
"J.E.K. Que puis-je faire pour t'aider dans cette sainte quête ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:302
msgid ""
"We are running out of time, Chosen One. Please, finish your holy quest soon. "
"We cannot afford to wait much longer. If there's anything I can do to help "
"you to save us, let me know."
msgstr ""
"Le temps nous est compté, Etre Elu. Dépêche-toi de terminer ta quête. Nous "
"ne pouvons pas nous permettre d'attendre plus longtemps. Si je peux faire "
"quelque chose t'aider à nous sauver, dis-le-moi."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:303
msgid ""
"Chosen One, our village is almost dead... you're our only hope. Is there "
"anything\n"
" I could tell you that would aide you in our salvation?"
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, notre village est presque mort... Tu es notre seul espoir. Y a-t-"
"il quelque chose que je puisse te dire pour t'aider à nous sauver ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:400
msgid "Is there anything you could tell me about Kaga?"
msgstr "Y-a-t-il quoi que se soit que tu puisses me dire sur Kaga ?"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:401
msgid ""
"[The villager stares at you, wide-eyed, then slowly steps away from you "
"while glancing around nervously.]"
msgstr ""
"[Le villageois te regarde fixement, les yeux grands ouverts, puis il "
"s'éloigne doucement de toi tout en jetant nerveusement des coups d'oeil "
"autour de lui.]"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:402
msgid "Alright, I guess not."
msgstr "Ok, je suppose que ça veut dire *non*."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:1107 dialog/acvillgr.msg:1108
msgid ""
"He heals us with his herbs and magic. He is in the northern part\n"
" of our village."
msgstr ""
"Il nous guérit avec ses herbes et sa magie. Il habite dans la partie Nord du "
"village."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:1109 dialog/kchild.msg:1109 dialog/kcitizen.msg:1109
msgid ""
"It is a magic powder which will heal you, but will make you\n"
" sleepy."
msgstr "Avec cette poudre magique, tu vas guérir, mais cela te fera somnoler."

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:1111 dialog/acwarior.msg:1111 dialog/kchild.msg:1111
#: dialog/kcitizen.msg:1111
msgid "He guards the bridge leading into our village."
msgstr "Il garde le pont par lequel on pénètre dans notre village."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:100
msgid "You see a tribesman."
msgstr "Tu vois un homme de la tribu."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:101
msgid "You see a tribeswoman."
msgstr "Tu vois une femme de la tribu."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:150
msgid ""
"Before you stands a large warrior of your village, wearing\n"
" pants fashioned from animal hides."
msgstr ""
"Devant toi se trouve un robuste guerrier de ton village, il porte un "
"pantalon en peaux d'animaux."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:152
msgid "Hello, Chosen One, can I help you in your quest?"
msgstr "Bonjour, Etre Elu, que puis-je faire pour toi ?"

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:153
msgid "I'm just looking around the village one last time before I leave."
msgstr ""
"Je faisais juste un tour dans le village une dernière fois avant de partir."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:155
msgid "Could you tell me where I can find more healing powder?"
msgstr "Peux-tu me dire où je peux trouver plus de poudre de guérison ?"

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:156
msgid "Gods give you speed to bring back Eden before it is too late."
msgstr ""
"Que les dieux te confèrent la vitesse pour restaurer l'Eden avant qu'il ne "
"soit trop tard."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:159
msgid ""
"Oh, you're testing me. Go see Hakunin in the northern corner of the village. "
"He makes our\n"
" medicines."
msgstr ""
"Oh, t'essaies de me tester. Va voir Hakunin au Nord du village. Il prépare "
"nos médicaments."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:161
msgid ""
"Well, I've seen them when Mynoc has us guard the bridge, but he does all the "
"dealing.\n"
" Talk to him at the Great Bridge."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, je les ai vus lorsque Mynoc nous a demandé de garder le pont, mais "
"c'est lui qui a eu affaire à eux. Va lui parler, au grand pont."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:163
msgid "Could tell me where the Great Bridge is located?"
msgstr "Peux-tu me dire où se trouve le grand pont ?"

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:165
msgid ""
"Chosen One? The Great Bridge is at the southern end of the village. You know,"
"\n"
" you've been there many times."
msgstr ""
"Le grand pont est situé tout au Sud du village. Tu le sais bien, t'y as déjà "
"été plusieurs fois."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:172
msgid ""
"Ah, dull one. They say you are the Chosen One. I must say the spirit\n"
" of the Founder works in strange ways."
msgstr ""
"Ah, l'être débile. On dit que tu es l'Etre Elu. Je dois avouer que l'esprit "
"du Fondateur agit bizarrement."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:173
msgid "Oon Ga."
msgstr "Ooung Ga."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:174
msgid " Have a safe journey, dull one -- for our sake."
msgstr " Fais un bon voyage, l'Etre Débile... pour notre vie à tous."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:176
msgid "You betray us. You must die."
msgstr "Tu nous as trahis. Tu dois mourir."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:177
msgid "A traitor to your own people!"
msgstr "Tu trahis ton propre peuple !"

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:179
msgid "Death to the evil one!"
msgstr "Mort à l'être démoniaque !"

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:180
msgid ""
"They are nothing to us! They scavenge the dying corpse\n"
" of the wastes to live."
msgstr ""
"Ils ne sont rien pour nous ! Ils dépouillent les cadavres du désert pour "
"survivre."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:300
msgid "Hello again, Chosen One. May the warrior spirits protect and guide you."
msgstr "Rebonjour, Etre Elu. Que l'esprit des guerriers te protège et te guide."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:301
msgid ""
"Are you having difficulties, Chosen One? You must not fail us - please hurry."
msgstr ""
"As-tu des problèmes, Etre Elu ? Tu n'as pas le droit à l'échec, je t'en "
"prie, dépêche-toi."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:302
msgid ""
"Why do you wait so long? We must have the GECK soon. Chosen One, our village "
"is dying."
msgstr ""
"Pourquoi attends-tu si longtemps ? Il nous faut le J.E.K au plus vite. Etre "
"Elu, notre village se meurt."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:303
msgid ""
"Chosen One, our village is almost dead. Why have you not brought the holy "
"GECK to us yet?"
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, notre village est presque mort. Pourquoi ne nous as-tu pas encore "
"ramené le saint J.E.K ?"

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:970 dialog/template.msg:970
msgid "That is my name."
msgstr "C'est mon nom."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:971 dialog/template.msg:971
msgid "You are talking to me."
msgstr "Tu me parles."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:972
msgid "What a silly question. That's me."
msgstr "Quelle question stupide. C'est moi."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:980 dialog/ahmonk.msg:404 dialog/gcharold.msg:293
#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:321 dialog/template.msg:980 dialog/vclynett.msg:823
msgid "I don't know anything about that."
msgstr "J'en sais rien."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:981
msgid "Sorry. No clue."
msgstr "Je regrette, je n'ai pas d'indice."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:982 dialog/template.msg:982
msgid "Never heard of it."
msgstr "Je n'en ai jamais entendu parler."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:1107 dialog/acwarior.msg:1108
msgid ""
"He heals us with his herbs and magic. He is in the northern\n"
" part of our village."
msgstr ""
"Il nous guérit avec ses herbes et sa magie. Il habite dans la partie Nord du "
"village."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:1109
msgid ""
"It is a magic powder which will heal you, but will make\n"
" you sleepy."
msgstr ""
"Avec cette poudre magique, tu vas guérir, mais cela te rendra somnolent."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:100
msgid "You see the Elder of your village."
msgstr "Tu vois la Doyenne de ton village."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:101
msgid "It is the Elder."
msgstr "C'est la doyenne."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:102
msgid ""
"The Elder is just that - old, older than you can remember. Still, she has "
"the\n"
" strength and fire to lead the village through these hard times."
msgstr ""
"La doyenne est très, très vieille, mais elle a toujours la force et "
"l'énergie pour guider le village en ces temps difficiles."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:103
msgctxt "aeld1"
msgid ""
"Congratulations, Chosen One, you have survived the Temple of Trials. Are\n"
" you ready for your quest?"
msgstr ""
"Félicitations, Etre Elu, tu as survécu au Temple des Epreuves. Te sens-tu "
"capable de poursuivre ta quête ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:104
msgid "What were you doing - trying to get me killed in the temple?"
msgstr "Que faisais-tu ? Tu voulais que je me fasse tuer dans le temple ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:105 dialog/dcvic.msg:2505 dialog/hcfrank.msg:129
#: dialog/tribec1.msg:470 dialog/vclynett.msg:828
msgid "Of course."
msgstr "Bien sûr."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:106
msgid "I'd like to think about it some more."
msgstr "J'aimerais encore y réfléchir."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:107
msgctxt "aeld2a"
msgid ""
"I am proud of you, Chosen. You have overcome much. Now. You must go find "
"Vault\n"
" 13. Vault 13. Bring the GECK home. GECK. Here is a shiny bottle. Vic gave "
"us this. Vic.\n"
" He is a trader in Klamath. Klamath. Go to Vic. Find Vault 13. Find GECK. "
"Come home. Do\n"
" your best, child."
msgstr ""
"Tu me combles de fierté, Etre Elu. Tu as surmonté tant d'épreuves... "
"Maintenant, tu dois partir à la recherche de l'Abri 13. L'Abri 13. Ramène le "
"J.E.K. Le J.E.K. Voici une bouteille qui brille. C'est Vic qui me l'a "
"donnée. Vic. C'est un marchand de Klamath. Klamath. Rends-toi chez Vic. "
"Trouve l'Abri 13. Trouve le J.E.K et reviens. Fais de ton mieux, mon enfant."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:112
msgctxt "aeld2b"
msgid "You not find vault. Find vault! Vault 13."
msgstr "Tu n'as pas trouvé l'Abri. Trouve l'Abri ! L'Abri 13."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:113 dialog/ahhakun.msg:225 dialog/dcderek.msg:306
#: dialog/dcfred.msg:363 dialog/dcfred.msg:373 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:328
#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:273 dialog/hcseymor.msg:158 dialog/kcsulik.msg:231
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:751 dialog/kcsulik.msg:792
msgid "Uh."
msgstr "Heu."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:114
msgctxt "aeld3"
msgid "Chosen One, do you wish us all dead? You must find the Vault!"
msgstr "Etre Elu, tu souhaites notre mort à tous ? Tu dois trouver l'Abri !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:115
msgid "I'm sorry, Elder. I will not fail."
msgstr "Pardon, doyenne. Je vais réussir."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:116
msgid "Yeah, yeah. Stop yelling."
msgstr "Ouais, ouais. Arrête de crier."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:117
msgctxt "aeld4"
msgid "Chosen One, why are you here?"
msgstr "Etre Elu, pourquoi es-tu ici ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:118
msgid "I know where Vault 13 is!"
msgstr "Je sais où se trouve l'Abri 13 !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:119
msgid "I am ready for the holy quest."
msgstr "Je veux commencer la sainte quête."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:120 dialog/ahelder.msg:125
msgid "I need some more info."
msgstr "Il me faut d'autres renseignements."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:121 dialog/ahelder.msg:130
msgid "I'm not going to get myself killed!"
msgstr "Je n'ai pas envie de me faire tuer !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:122
msgid "What was I supposed to do again?"
msgstr "Que dois-je faire déjà ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:123
msgid "I'm going now."
msgstr "Je m'en vais maintenant."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:124
msgctxt "aeld5"
msgid ""
"That is good news, but not enough to save us. You must come back soon with "
"the\n"
" GECK or our people will die!"
msgstr ""
"C'est une bonne nouvelle, mais ça n'est pas suffisant pour nous sauver. "
"Trouve le J.E.K ou notre peuple mourra !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:126
msgid "Fine, I'm going now."
msgstr "Très bien, je m'en vais maintenant."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:127
msgctxt "aeld6"
msgid ""
"You survived. The Chosen One cannot be weak or we are all doomed. Are you\n"
" prepared for your quest?"
msgstr ""
"Tu as survécu. L'Etre Elu ne doit pas faillir ou nous serons tous condamnés. "
"Es-tu prêt pour cette quête ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:128
msgid "I've passed the test. Of course, I'm ready."
msgstr "J'ai réussi l'épreuve. Je peux donc commencer."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:129 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:136
msgid "I need to think about this."
msgstr "Je dois y réfléchir."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:131
msgctxt "aeld7"
msgid ""
"Pay attention. Find the holy Vault 13 and bring back the GECK. Vic, the "
"trader\n"
" from Klamath, brought us the flask from the holy Thirteen. Start your "
"search with him.\n"
" The disk will remind you of your task. May the gods of the Vault watch over "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Ecoute bien. Trouve le saint Abri 13 et rapporte le JEK. Vic, le marchand de "
"Klamath, nous a apporté la fiole provenant du Saint-Treize. Commence tes "
"recherches avec lui. Le disque te rappellera ta mission. Que les dieux de "
"l'Abri soient avec toi."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:133
msgid "Before I go, I have some questions."
msgstr "Avant de partir, j'ai quelques questions."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:134
msgid "Goodbye. I will not fail the tribe."
msgstr "La tribu peut compter sur moi. Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:135
msgctxt "aeld8"
msgid "Very well. See me when you decide - but do not wait too long."
msgstr ""
"Très bien. Viens me voir lorsque ta décision sera prise mais n'attends pas "
"trop longtemps."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:137
msgctxt "aeld9"
msgid ""
"I cannot help much. So much has been lost from the Long Ago. What wisdom do "
"you seek?"
msgstr ""
"Je ne peux guère t'aider plus. Tant de choses se sont perdues depuis "
"l'Antan. Quelle sagesse cherches-tu ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:138
msgctxt "aeld9b"
msgid "What do you need?"
msgstr "De quoi as-tu besoin ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:139
msgid "Tell me more about the GECK."
msgstr "Dis-m'en plus sur le J.E.K."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:140
msgid "How do I get to Klamath?"
msgstr "Comment va-t-on à Klamath ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:141
msgid "Where is Vault 13?"
msgstr "Où se trouve l'Abri 13 ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:142
msgid "On second thought, I don't need any help now. Goodbye."
msgstr "Tout bien réfléchi, je ne pense pas avoir besoin d'aide. Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:143
msgctxt "aeld10"
msgid ""
"It is a holy artifact - the Garden of Eden Creation Kit. The disks promise "
"it\n"
" will make our lands green and our village prosperous. It will save us. "
"More, I do not know."
msgstr ""
"C'est un artefact sacré : le Jardin d'Eden en Kit. Les disques disent qu'il "
"rendra nos terres fertiles et notre village prospère. Il nous sauvera. Je ne "
"peux t'en dire plus."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:144
msgid "There's more I want to know."
msgstr "J'aimerais en savoir plus."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:146
msgctxt "aeld11"
msgid "Klamath is to the east."
msgstr "Klamath se trouve à l'Est."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:147
msgid "There are other things I would learn."
msgstr "Je pourrais en apprendre bien plus."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:148
msgid "I am ready. Goodbye."
msgstr "Je suis prêt. Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:149
msgctxt "aeld12"
msgid ""
"The holy Thirteen? I cannot help you. Only the Vault Dweller knew. His tales "
"have\n"
" the sound of a perilous journey. "
msgstr ""
"Le Saint-Treize ? Je ne peux t'aider. Seul l'Habitant de l'Abri savait. Ses "
"contes parlaient d'un périlleux voyage. "

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:150
msgid "I see. There is much I need to know."
msgstr "Je vois. Je dois en savoir plus."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:151
msgid "Goodbye, Elder."
msgstr "Au revoir, doyenne."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:152
msgctxt "aeld13"
msgid ""
"Being a coward will kill us all! Including you. You passed\n"
" the Temple Trials. We have faith in you. We need you."
msgstr ""
"Si tu hésites, nous mourrons tous ! Toi y compris. Tu as réussi à traverser "
"le Temple des Epreuves. Nous croyons en toi. Nous avons besoin de toi."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:153
msgid "Not so fast, old woman. I need time to think about this!"
msgstr "Pas si vite, vieille femme. Je dois y réfléchir !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:154
msgid "As you wish, Elder."
msgstr "Comme tu veux, doyenne."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:155
msgctxt "aeld14a"
msgid "You've betrayed us. You will perish."
msgstr "Tu nous as trahis. Tu dois périr."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:156
msgctxt "aeld14b"
msgid "You are a traitor!"
msgstr "Tu n'es que traîtrise !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:157
msgctxt "aeld14c"
msgid "Why do you do this?"
msgstr "Pourquoi fais-tu cela ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:158
msgctxt "aeld14d"
msgid "I knew you had the soul of darkness!"
msgstr "Je savais que l'esprit du mal était en toi !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:159
msgctxt "aeld15"
msgid ""
"Then take this flask. It is from the holy Vault 13. Vic, a trader in Klamath,"
"\n"
" brought it to us. He may know where the vault is. You may also need some of "
"what they\n"
" call money. Here."
msgstr ""
"Alors prends cette fiole. Elle vient de l'Abri 13. Vic, un marchand de "
"Klamath, nous l'a donnée. Il sait peut-être où se trouve l'Abri. Tu auras "
"sans doute besoin de ce qu'ils appellent de l'argent. Tiens."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:160
msgid "Uh... What was my quest again?"
msgstr "Euh... C'est quoi ma quête déjà ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:161
msgid "Is there more you can tell me?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il autre chose que tu pourrais me dire ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:162
msgid "Wish me luck, Elder, and I will not fail you."
msgstr "Souhaite-moi bonne chance, doyenne. Et compte sur moi."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:163
msgctxt "aeld16"
msgid "Find Vic in Klamath. We are counting on you."
msgstr "Trouve Vic à Klamath. Nous comptons sur toi."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:164
msgctxt "aeld17"
msgid ""
"It's good to see you again, Child. I don't mean to be abrupt but I see you\n"
" haven't completed your quest to find the holy Thirteen. Please, let's not "
"waste time\n"
" talking. The need of our people is great. Go find the Vault!"
msgstr ""
"Ca fait du bien de te revoir, mon enfant. Je ne veux pas te vexer mais... je "
"vois que ta quête du Saint-Treize n'a pas abouti. Je t'en prie, ne perdons "
"pas de temps en bavardages. Le besoin de notre peuple est grand. Va et "
"trouve l'Abri !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:165 dialog/bcdalia.msg:108 dialog/bcjones.msg:129
#: dialog/ccquincy.msg:113 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:114 dialog/ocariel.msg:106
#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:119 dialog/ocgoris.msg:187 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:128
#: dialog/ocjul.msg:114 dialog/ocjul.msg:120 dialog/ockerith.msg:109
#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:111 dialog/ocmatt.msg:150 dialog/octhearn.msg:108
#: dialog/scdocjub.msg:120 dialog/scmira.msg:195 dialog/shtandi.msg:306
msgid "Me go now."
msgstr "Moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:166 dialog/ccgguard.msg:143 dialog/vcstark.msg:129
msgid "All right, I'm going."
msgstr "Très bien, j'y vais."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:167
msgid "I will not fail you elder."
msgstr "Tu peux compter sur moi, doyenne."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:168
msgid "I'm working on it, Ok?"
msgstr "J'm'en occupe, Ok !?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:169
msgctxt "aeld18"
msgid ""
"Once again you return without the GECK. Our crops begin to fail us, Chosen. "
"Our\n"
" need becomes greater with the passage of time. Go find the holy Thirteen!"
msgstr ""
"Une fois de plus tu reviens sans le J.E.K. Nos récoltes commencent à "
"manquer. Le temps passe et nos besoins se font plus pressants. Va et trouve "
"le Saint-Treize !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:170
msgid "Ok, me go now."
msgstr "Ok, moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:171
msgid "Yes, Elder."
msgstr "Oui, doyenne."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:172
msgid "I will not fail you or our people, Elder."
msgstr "Tu peux compter sur moi, doyenne."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:173
msgid "Look. If you think you can do better... "
msgstr "Ecoute. Si tu crois pouvoir faire mieux... "

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:174
msgctxt "aeld19"
msgid ""
"Chosen One, things are not well here. We need the GECK if our village is to\n"
" survive. Our people grow weak with hunger and our food reserves will not "
"last much\n"
" longer. Please, find the holy Thirteen and return to us. Go now."
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, rien ne va plus ici. Nous avons besoin du J.E.K si nous voulons "
"que notre village survive. Notre peuple s'affaiblit. Il a faim. Nos réserves "
"de nourriture diminuent. Je t'en prie, trouve le Saint-Treize et reviens. "
"Pars maintenant."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:176
msgid "Very well. I'm on my way."
msgstr "Très bien. J'y vais."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:177
msgid "I will do my best to find the GECK and save our village."
msgstr ""
"Je vais faire de mon mieux pour trouver le J.E.K et sauver notre village."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:178
msgid "Don't push me, old woman. I'm doing my best."
msgstr "Arrête, vieille femme. Je fais de mon mieux."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:179
msgctxt "aeld20"
msgid ""
"Child, our need is greater than ever before. Our people sicken, the brahmin\n"
" are dying, and our food is all but gone. The blight of the land can only be "
"cured with\n"
" the GECK. Go, find the GECK and save our people."
msgstr ""
"Les temps sont durs, mon enfant. Notre peuple est malade, les Brahmines se "
"meurent et notre nourriture est épuisée. Seul le J.E.K combattra le fléau "
"qui s'est abattu sur nos terres. Va, et trouve-le ! Sauve notre peuple !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:181 dialog/scmerk.msg:262 dialog/vcconnar.msg:153
msgid "I'm on my way."
msgstr "Je m'en vais."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:182
msgid "Forgive me Elder. I will find the GECK without delay."
msgstr "Pardonne-moi, doyenne. Je me mets sur-le-champ à la recherche du J.E.K."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:183
msgid "Yeah, yeah. You're beginning to sound like a broken disk..."
msgstr "Ouais, ouais. Tu commences à radoter..."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:200
msgctxt "eeld1"
msgid "Chosen One! How did you get here?"
msgstr "Etre Elu ! Comment es-tu arrivé ici ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:201
msgid "Uhh... duh?"
msgstr "Euh... Ben ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:202 dialog/tribec7.msg:219
msgid "I've come to rescue you."
msgstr "Je suis venu te sauver."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:203
msgid "What the hell's going on here?"
msgstr "Bon sang, mais que se passe-t-il ici ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:204
msgctxt "eeld2"
msgid "You monster! Have you come to kill me, too?"
msgstr "Monstre ! Tu es là pour me tuer, moi aussi ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:205
msgid "Uhhh?"
msgstr "Euhhh ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:206
msgid "No, it's me, the Chosen One!"
msgstr "Non, c'est moi, l'Etre Elu !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:207
msgid "Oh, shut up, you old bitch! It's me, your Chosen One."
msgstr "Oh, ferme-la, vieille peau ! C'est moi, l'Etre Elu."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:208
msgctxt "eeld3"
msgid ""
"Oh, gods... Listen - go down. Find machine that makes power. Kill machine. "
"Kill bad men. Kill everybody! You kill, we go home. Also, if you not have "
"GECK then look for GECK here. Must have GECK to save village! Freedom is "
"nothing without home to return to. Understand? Oh, gods."
msgstr ""
"Oh, doux Jésus... Ecoute... Descends. Toi trouver machine qui fabrique "
"énergie. Tuer machine. Tuer méchants. Tuer tout le monde ! Si toi tuer, nous "
"rentrer à la maison. Ah oui ! Si toi pas avoir encore J.E.K, toi chercher "
"ici. J.E.K sauver village ! La liberté sert à rien sans une maison où "
"revenir. Compris ? Oh, doux Jésus..."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:209
msgid "Uh -huh!"
msgstr "Euh !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:210
msgctxt "eeld4"
msgid ""
"Careful, do not touch the glow wall. I think the machine that feeds it is "
"beneath us. Destroy it so we may escape. How did you get here?"
msgstr ""
"Attention, ne touche pas au mur rayonnant. A mon avis la machine qui "
"l'alimente est en-dessous de nous. Détruis-la pour qu'on s'échappe. Comment "
"as-tu fait pour venir ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:211
msgid "I have a ship. "
msgstr "J'ai un navire. "

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:212
msgctxt "eeld5"
msgid ""
"Men came to our village in flying machines and took us. There were others, "
"too - from the holy Thirteen! I thought we were saved. I thought we were "
"going to heaven. (sigh)"
msgstr ""
"Des hommes sont venus au village et nous ont emmenés dans leurs machines "
"volantes. Il y avait aussi des gens du Saint-Treize ! Je croyais qu'on était "
"sauvés. J'ai pensé que nous allions au paradis. (soupir)"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:213 dialog/ahhakun.msg:289
msgid "And then?"
msgstr "Et ensuite ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:214
msgctxt "eeld5a"
msgid ""
"Then they brought us here, to hell. They have killed most of us with "
"something they call effeevee. They will kill us all before they are through!"
"\n"
" Do you know what must be done, Chosen One?"
msgstr ""
"Puis, ils nous ont amenés ici, en enfer. Ils ont tué la plupart d'entre nous "
"avec de l'effeuvé. Ils nous tueront, jusqu'au dernier ! Tu sais ce que tu "
"dois faire, Être Elu."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:215
msgid "Effeevee?"
msgstr "Effeuvé ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:218
msgctxt "eeld6"
msgid ""
"If you destroy the machine, we will find the ship. Hurry, there are not many "
"of us left. "
msgstr ""
"Si tu détruis la machine, nous trouverons le navire. Dépêche-toi. Nous ne "
"sommes plus bien nombreux. "

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:219 dialog/ahhakun.msg:249 dialog/kcardin.msg:272
#: dialog/nclabish.msg:736 dialog/tribec4.msg:231
msgid "What happened?"
msgstr "Que s'est-il passé ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:221
msgctxt "eeld7"
msgid ""
"You must destroy the machine and kill the devils in this place. We will meet "
"you outside! And Chosen One, if you have not found the GECK, seek it here. "
"Our freedom is nothing if we cannot save our village. Now go!"
msgstr ""
"Tu dois détruire la machine et tuer tous les démons qui sont ici. On se "
"retrouve dehors ! Etre Elu, si tu n'as pas encore trouvé le J.E.K, cherche "
"ici. Notre liberté ne vaut rien si le village ne peut être sauvé. Vas-y "
"maintenant !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:223
msgctxt "eeld8"
msgid ""
"I am still the Elder. Remember your place! Apologize or I will not help you "
"anymore."
msgstr ""
"N'oublie pas que je suis encore la Doyenne ! Fais-moi des excuses ou je ne "
"t'aiderai pas."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:224
msgid "Sorry, you're not an old bitch. What's going on?"
msgstr "Excuse-moi, tu n'es pas une vieille peau. Que se passe-t-il ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:225
msgid "Like you could help me in there? Fuck off and die."
msgstr "Pff, tu pourrais peut-être m'aider, non ? Va te faire foutre et crève."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:226
msgctxt "eeld9"
msgid ""
"Go away. You are no better than these devils. I weep you were named the "
"Chosen One."
msgstr ""
"Va-t'en. Tu ne vaux guère mieux que ces démons. Tu ne mérites pas d'être "
"l'Etre Elu."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:227
msgctxt "eeld10"
msgid ""
"Why are you here? Every minute you waste another of our people could be "
"killed. And don't forget the GECK! We must have it."
msgstr ""
"Mais que fais-tu ici ? Chaque minute qui s'écoule peut être fatale à notre "
"peuple. Et n'oublie pas le J.E.K ! Il nous le faut."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:228
msgid "Nuh??"
msgstr "Nuh ??"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:229
msgid "Where was I supposed to go?"
msgstr "Où dois-je aller déjà ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:230
msgid "Just wanted to annoy you. I'm on it. Don't worry."
msgstr ""
"Je voulais juste t'embêter un peu. Je contrôle la situation. Ne t'inquiète "
"pas."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:231
msgctxt "eeld11"
msgid "(sigh) Go below. Kill. Smash machines. Go now!"
msgstr "Toi descendre. Tuer. Détruire machines. Maintenant !"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:232
msgctxt "eeld12"
msgid ""
"Listen this time! Go to the levels below us. Find the machine that makes "
"power. Stop it and we can escape. The men here are not true to the Vault "
"dream. They are evil. Also, if you have not yet found the GECK, seek it "
"here. Our freedom is nothing if our village cannot be saved. Now go!"
msgstr ""
"Ecoute cette fois-ci ! Va aux niveaux inférieurs. Trouve la machine qui "
"fabrique l'énergie. Arrête-la pour qu'on s'échappe. Les hommes qui sont ici "
"ne méritent pas l'Abri. Ils sont démoniaques. Et si tu n'as pas encore "
"trouvé le J.E.K, cherche-le ici. Notre liberté ne vaut rien si le village ne "
"peut-être sauvé. Vas-y maintenant !!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:233 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:160 dialog/ccatech.msg:143
#: dialog/cccook.msg:141 dialog/ccdoctor.msg:124 dialog/ccncomp.msg:133
#: dialog/cctech1.msg:143 dialog/cctech2.msg:145 dialog/hcbnkgrd.msg:117
#: dialog/ncmyrgrd.msg:426 dialog/ocdar.msg:119 dialog/ocdar.msg:133
#: dialog/octhearn.msg:118 dialog/ocvaldis.msg:118
msgid "Got it."
msgstr "Compris."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:234
msgctxt "eeld13"
msgid ""
"That is what they call it. They stick needles into our skin, like stimpaks, "
"but then terrible things happen. Then... (chokes up)"
msgstr ""
"C'est comme ça qu'ils l'ont appelé. Ils nous enfoncent des aiguilles sous la "
"peau, tout comme des Stimpaks, puis des choses terribles arrivent. Puis..."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:235 dialog/gcbrain.msg:381 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:139
#: dialog/rcjane.msg:174
msgid "Then what?"
msgstr "Et puis ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:236
msgid "This is going to make me sick, isn't it?"
msgstr "Ca va me rendre malade, pas vrai ?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:237
msgctxt "eeld13a"
msgid ""
"Then the skin bubbles like maggots beneath it. Boils grow and burst. Blood "
"runs from your ears and your tongue swells. Those who are lucky choke to "
"death. Those who are not..."
msgstr ""
"Puis ça se met à grouiller comme s'il y avait des asticots sous la peau. Ces "
"excroissances grossissent et éclatent. Le sang coule par les oreilles et la "
"langue gonfle. Ceux qui ont de la chance, meurent en s'étouffant. Quant aux "
"autres..."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:238
msgid "They'll pay."
msgstr "Ils vont me le payer."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:239
msgid "That certainly was disgusting. What am I supposed to do?"
msgstr "C'était sûrement horrible. Que dois-je faire ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:100
msgid ""
"Before you stands Hakunin, the village shaman. He appraises you with his "
"crazy eyes from somewhere in the world only he inhabits...."
msgstr ""
"Tu as devant toi Hakunin, le shaman. Il te jauge de son regard fou sorti "
"d'un monde connu de lui seul..."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:101
msgid "You see Hakunin lying on the ground. He's badly wounded."
msgstr "Tu vois Hakunin allongé par terre. Il est gravement blessé."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:102
msgid "You see Hakunin. He's very near death."
msgstr "Tu vois Hakunin. Il est sur le point de mourir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:103
msgid ""
"Hakunin is badly burned. He smells like roast chicken, looks like burnt "
"meatloaf, and you don't know how he's managed to stay alive this long."
msgstr ""
"Hakunin est gravement brûlé. Il sent le poulet rôti, il ressemble à du "
"hachis de viande brûlé, et tu te demandes comment il a pu survivre si "
"longtemps."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:104
msgctxt "hak001"
msgid ""
"Greetings, Chosen. Why does the earth before me warm to the touch of your "
"passing?"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour, Etre Elu. Pourquoi la Terre que je contemple se réchauffe sur ton "
"passage ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:105 dialog/ahhakun.msg:112
msgid "Uh? "
msgstr "Euh ? "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:106 dialog/ahhakun.msg:113
msgid "I've come to say goodbye. I'm leaving on my holy quest. "
msgstr "Je suis là pour te dire au revoir. Je vais mener ma sainte quête. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:107 dialog/ahhakun.msg:114
msgid ""
"I'm heading out. I was hoping just this once you'd talk like a real person. "
msgstr ""
"Je m'en vais. J'espérais que pour une fois tu parlerais comme une vraie "
"personne. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:108 dialog/ahhakun.msg:115
msgid "You are doing just way too many drugs. I'm outta here. "
msgstr "Tu prends vraiment beaucoup trop de drogue. Je me tire d'ici. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:109 dialog/ahhakun.msg:178
msgid "I'm hurt. Can you heal me?"
msgstr "J'ai des blessures. Peux-tu me soigner ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:110 dialog/ahhakun.msg:116
msgid ""
"There were some pretty nasty plants infesting your garden- I've taken care "
"of them for you."
msgstr ""
"Ton jardin était envahi de mauvaises herbes. J'en ai pris soin pour toi."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:111
msgctxt "hak001a"
msgid "Please reveal to clouded eyes the purpose of your passage."
msgstr "Je t'en prie, révèle aux yeux voilés le motif de ton passage."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:117
msgctxt "hak002"
msgid ""
"The Earth sings with the news of a champion upon the land.... Perhaps, "
"before you go, you would bestow a kindness?"
msgstr ""
"La Terre chante en apprenant l'arrivée d'un champion dans ces contrées... "
"Peut-être accepteras-tu de m'accorder une faveur ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:118 dialog/epac17.msg:801 dialog/tribec1.msg:532
#: dialog/tribec8.msg:301 dialog/tribec8.msg:319
msgid "Sure. What do you need?"
msgstr "Bien sûr. De quoi as-tu besoin ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:119
msgid "It depends... what'll you give me?"
msgstr "Ca dépend. Que me donnes-tu en échange ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:120
msgctxt "hak002a"
msgid ""
"The views of the world are many - a lesson you will learn soon.... Perhaps, "
"before you reap the experiences of life, you would bestow a kindness?"
msgstr ""
"Les visions du monde sont nombreuses. C'est une leçon que tu apprendras "
"bientôt.... Avant de récolter les fruits de l'expérience, m'accorderas-tu "
"une faveur ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:121
msgid "Did you just ask me to do you a favor? If so, sure, why not?"
msgstr ""
"M'as-tu demandé de te faire une faveur ? Si c'est le cas, certainement, "
"pourquoi pas ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:122
msgid ""
"I'll do something for you, but since I have to work this hard just to "
"understand you, this task will cost."
msgstr ""
"Je veux bien faire quelque chose pour toi mais comme j'ai du mal à te "
"comprendre, ça ne sera pas gratuit."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:123
msgctxt "hak003"
msgid ""
"A blessing on you, for you are truly a child of nature. Would you please use "
"your special talents and rid my garden of the plants of dark soul?"
msgstr ""
"Dieu te bénisse, car tu es un véritable enfant de la nature. Pourrais-tu "
"user de tes talents spéciaux pour débarrasser mon jardin des plantes aux "
"âmes rongées ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:124
msgid "Uh-huh. "
msgstr "Euh, ouais. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:125
msgid "Nuh-uh. Youuu. Giv. Hed hurt."
msgstr "Nuh-uh. Toi... Donner... Mal à tête."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:126
msgctxt "hak004"
msgid ""
"May your aura grace my presence when you are... Oh, come to my door when "
"you're done and I'll give you something good."
msgstr ""
"Que ton aura honore ma présence lorsque tu seras... Viens me voir quand tu "
"auras terminé et je te récompenserai."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:127 dialog/fcdrwong.msg:541
msgid "Urgh."
msgstr "Argh."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:128
msgctxt "hak005"
msgid ""
"The plants of dark soul have infested my garden again. Many seasons have "
"touched my bones and I am too frail for that fight which is eternal in "
"nature. I ask that you be my champion."
msgstr ""
"Les plantes aux âmes rongées ont encore envahi mon jardin. Les nombreuses "
"saisons ont affecté mes os et je suis trop frêle pour ce combat éternel. Je "
"te demande d'être mon champion."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:129
msgid "I don't think so. I need to start my quest right away."
msgstr "Je ne pense pas. Je dois immédiatement commencer ma quête."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:130
msgid ""
"I know you're not a bad guy, but I've got a headache already, so I think "
"I'll have to pass."
msgstr ""
"Je sais que tu n'es pas un mauvais bougre. J'ai déjà mal à la tête et je "
"crois que je vais devoir partir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:131
msgid ""
"Forget it. I'm the future leader of this tribe and it would be undignified "
"for me to do your gardening for you."
msgstr ""
"Laisse tomber. Je serai bientôt à la tête de cette tribu et ce ne serait pas "
"digne de mon rang de m'occuper de ton jardin."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:132
msgid "I'd be honored, holy one."
msgstr "Ce serait un honneur, saint homme."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:133
msgid "Did you just ask me to weed your garden? If that's the case, okay."
msgstr ""
"Tu me demandes simplement de désherber ton jardin ? Si c'est ça, d'accord."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:134
msgid "For a price."
msgstr "Pour un prix."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:135
msgctxt "hak006"
msgid ""
"To ask payment for a gift will bring you less than the gift itself. I will "
"give you such and add the lesson of your self-disappointment at the "
"receiving."
msgstr ""
"Demander le paiement d'un présent t'apportera moins que le présent lui-même. "
"J'accéderai à ta demande et t'enseignerai en outre la leçon de l'auto-"
"déception."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:136
msgid "Good enough. Where's the garden?"
msgstr "Ca me convient. Où est le jardin ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:137
msgid "You know, a nice gift would be to SPEAK ENGLISH!"
msgstr "Tu sais, le plus beau cadeau serait de PARLER FRANCAIS !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:138
msgid "What if I give you a lesson in disappointment and leave right now? Bye."
msgstr ""
"Et que dirais-tu si je te donnais une leçon de déception en partant "
"immédiatement ? Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:139
msgid "Well, if that's your attitude, I don't think I'm interested. Goodbye."
msgstr "Eh bien, si tu réagis comme ça, ça ne m'intéresse pas. Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:140
msgctxt "hak006a"
msgid ""
"If we speak the same words, do we mean the same thing? Do words always carry "
"the same touch of a soul?"
msgstr ""
"Si nous parlons la même langue, signifions-nous la même chose ? Les mots "
"transportent-ils toujours la même note ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:141
msgid ""
"Oh, yeah. Much better. And the lesson I learned is to shut up and just ask "
"where the garden is."
msgstr ""
"Oh, ouais. Encore mieux. Et la leçon que j'ai apprise est de me taire et de "
"juste demander où se trouve le jardin."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:142
msgid "Let's try the word, \"goodbye.\" It means I'm leaving. "
msgstr "Essayons le terme *au revoir*. Ca veut dire que je m'en vais. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:143
msgctxt "hak007"
msgid "Surely you remember it is to the northeast, foolish one."
msgstr "Pauvre créature, tu as oublié qu'il est au Nord-Est ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:144 dialog/dclara.msg:531 dialog/vcmelind.msg:125
#: dialog/vcmelind.msg:132
msgid "Thank you for your help."
msgstr "Merci pour ton aide."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:145
msgid "Thanks. I actually understood that."
msgstr "Merci. J'ai bien compris ça."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:146
msgid ""
"Are you calling me a fool? I don't think I want to help you, after all. "
msgstr "Tu me traites de créature ? Eh bien dans ce cas, je refuse de t'aider. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:147
msgid "I'll be back for my payment soon."
msgstr "Je reviendrai bientôt me faire payer."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:148
msgctxt "hak008"
msgid "The burden you carry now will grow ever heavier."
msgstr "Le fardeau qui te pèse toujours plus te pèsera."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:149
msgctxt "hak009"
msgid ""
"May the gods bless your efforts, Chosen. May your aura grace my presence "
"when the earth breathes clean again."
msgstr ""
"Que les dieux bénissent tes efforts, Etre Elu. Que ton aura honore ma "
"présence le jour où le souffle de la terre sera à nouveau pur."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:150
msgid ""
"I take it you want to see me again when I'm done... You could have just said "
"so, you know."
msgstr ""
"Si je comprends bien, tu veux me revoir lorsque j'aurai terminé... Tu aurais "
"pu le dire plus simplement, tu sais..."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:152
msgctxt "hak010"
msgid ""
"Ha! The founder's spirit lives in you. Focus in to fortify the self to "
"expand the greatness to enable such to touch the world. Of course, the "
"rewards will be more than those of the spirit. "
msgstr ""
"Ah ! L'esprit du fondateur vit en toi. Concentre-toi pour fortifier ton moi "
"intérieur et développer la grandeur afin que celle-ci touche le monde. Bien "
"sûr, les gratifications dépasseront celles de l'esprit. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:153
msgid "Sounds good. I'll be back when I'm done."
msgstr "Ca à l'air bien. Je reviendrai lorsque j'aurai terminé."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:154
msgid "So, I'm getting an actual thing in payment. Good enough. See ya later."
msgstr ""
"Alors, je vais obtenir quelque chose en guise de paiement. Parfait. A plus "
"tard."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:155
msgid ""
"I think you've been playing with those plants way too much. To avoid your "
"fate, I'm staying away from the garden."
msgstr ""
"Je crois que tu as trop joué avec ces plantes. Pour échapper à ton destin, "
"je vais rester hors du jardin."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:156
msgctxt "hak011"
msgid ""
"Time can neither be wasted or saved- it must always be now. The actions "
"create the fabric of your life."
msgstr ""
"Le temps ne peut être ni gaspillé, ni gagné, il doit toujours être au moment "
"présent. Ce sont les actions qui tissent la toile de ta vie."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:157
msgid "Uh, right. Like I said, I've got to go. Goodbye. "
msgstr "Euh, très bien. Comme je l'ai dit, je dois partir. Au revoir. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:158
msgid ""
"You know, talking to you makes me wonder about that time can't be wasted "
"idea. I'm outta here. "
msgstr ""
"Tu sais, en te parlant, je m'interroge sur cette idée de temps gaspillé. Je "
"m'en vais. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:159
msgid ""
"If only I had your wisdom, wise one. Forgive me- of course I'll take care of "
"it for you."
msgstr ""
"Si seulement j'avais ta sagesse, sage homme. Pardonne-moi. Bien sûr, je vais "
"m'en occuper pour toi."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:160
msgctxt "hak012"
msgid ""
"You may bear the mantle of the Chosen, but your dark soul cries from within."
msgstr ""
"Tu as beau porter le manteau de l'Etre Elu, ton âme rongée crie de "
"l'intérieur."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:161
msgid "I beg your forgiveness, holy one. How can I cleanse my soul? "
msgstr "J'implore ton pardon, saint homme. Comment puis-je purifier mon âme ? "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:162
msgid "That's right, Hakunin, and you'd be a real wise man not to forget it."
msgstr ""
"C'est vrai, Hakunin, et tu ferais preuve de grande sagesse en ne l'oubliant "
"pas."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:163
msgid "My head aches from within listening to you. I'm gone."
msgstr "Ma tête me fait mal à force de t'écouter. Je m'en vais."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:164
msgid "Booka!"
msgstr "Booka !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:165
msgctxt "hak013"
msgid "Cleanse your soul as you would banish demons from my garden."
msgstr "Purifie ton âme comme tu bannirais les démons de mon jardin."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:166
msgid ""
"It shall be done, wise one. I will come seek your forgiveness after I have "
"purified your garden."
msgstr ""
"Ca doit être fait, sage homme. Je viendrai implorer ton pardon après avoir "
"purifié ton jardin."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:167
msgid ""
"You're trying to say that weeding your garden will be good for me, right? "
"Well, okay, I'll give it a try."
msgstr ""
"Tu es en train de me dire que le fait de désherber ton jardin me fera le "
"plus grand bien, c'est ça ? Très bien, je vais essayer."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:168
msgid "I kinda like my soul the way it is. Bye."
msgstr "J'aime mon âme telle qu'elle est. Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:169
msgid "I'm not worthy. I'll take my leave now."
msgstr "Je n'en vaux pas la peine. Je m'en vais maintenant."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:170
msgctxt "hak014"
msgid "Chosen, once again the wholeness of your being is like a land blessed."
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, encore une fois ton être tout entier se révèle comme une terre "
"bénie."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:171 dialog/ahhakun.msg:181 dialog/ahhakun.msg:184
#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:211 dialog/ahmonk.msg:422 dialog/ahmonk.msg:702
#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:202 dialog/dcchcgrd.msg:166 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:512
#: dialog/ecfarmer.msg:104 dialog/echomest.msg:104 dialog/generic.msg:200
#: dialog/kcbhcust.msg:208 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:141 dialog/tribec6.msg:132
#: dialog/vclynett.msg:811 dialog/vcvltgrd.msg:131 dialog/vicencom.msg:139
#: dialog/vicencom.msg:165 dialog/vicencom.msg:251
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr "Merci."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:172
msgid "You mean I'm better, right?"
msgstr "Tu veux dire que je vais mieux, c'est ça ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:173
msgctxt "hak015"
msgid ""
"To make one whole instills a sense of fullness that you would be well to "
"understand, Chosen."
msgstr ""
"Guérir autrui instille un sens de plénitude qu'il serait bon que tu "
"comprennes, Etre Elu."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:174
msgid ""
"Wait, don't tell me. I'm better and you felt good doing it, right? Thanks."
msgstr ""
"Attends, ne me le dis pas. Je me sens mieux et ça t'a fait du bien de le "
"faire, pas vrai ? Merci."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:175
msgid "You are wise and kind, Holy One."
msgstr "Tu es sage et aimable, saint homme."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:176
msgctxt "hak017"
msgid "In what way may I touch the chosen soul, Seed of the Dweller?"
msgstr "Comment puis-je toucher l'âme élue, graine de l'Habitant ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:177
msgid "Uh, where exactly is your garden?"
msgstr "Euh, où se trouve exactement ton jardin ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:179
msgid "Oh, nothing. Goodbye."
msgstr "Oh, rien. Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:180
msgctxt "hak018"
msgid ""
"Ahh. You return the spirit of the Dweller to the world and bring a smile to "
"the soul of an old man in passing. For this, I give you powders of healing. "
"Remember, they fog the mind as they cleanse the body."
msgstr ""
"Ahhh. Tu restitues l'esprit de l'Habitant au monde et rends le sourire à "
"l'âme d'un vieil homme. Pour cela, je te donne des poudres de guérison. "
"N'oublie pas, elles purifient le corps mais embrument l'esprit."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:182
msgctxt "hak018a"
msgid ""
"And also, will I mix the broc flower with the xander root together whenever "
"you bring both to me. May your pathways be true and your heart follow suit. "
msgstr ""
"Et aussi vais-je mélanger la fleur de Broc avec la racine de Xandre lorsque "
"tu me les ramèneras. Que tes chemins soient vrais et que ton coeur montre "
"l'exemple. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:183
msgid "Where can I find these things?"
msgstr "Où puis-je trouver ces choses ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:185
msgid "I'm almost sorry to go. I can just about understand you now. Bye."
msgstr ""
"Je regrette presque de partir. Je commence tout juste à te comprendre. Au "
"revoir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:186
msgctxt "hak019"
msgid "Ah, Chosen, my garden is well- how is yours?"
msgstr ""
"Ah, Etre Elu, mon jardin se porte bien. Et le tien, comment se porte-t-il ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:187 dialog/hczaius.msg:126
msgid "I'm all right."
msgstr "Je vais bien."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:188 dialog/fcdrfung.msg:172
msgid "I need healing."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de soins."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:189
msgid "Where did you say the plants were?"
msgstr "Où as-tu dit que se trouvaient les plantes ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:190
msgid "I don't have a garden- what the hell are you talking about this time?"
msgstr "Je n'ai pas de jardin. Bon sang, mais de quoi parles-tu là ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:191
msgid "I'd like you to make some healing powder for me."
msgstr "J'aimerais que tu me prépares de la poudre de guérison."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:192
msgid "Oh, never mind. I've got to go."
msgstr "Oh, tant pis. Je dois partir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:193
msgid "Ow?"
msgstr "Ow ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:194
msgid "Ooog! Bak!"
msgstr "Ooog ! Bak !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:195
msgctxt "hak020"
msgid ""
"The pleasure of these words fills me. Alas, the gods whisper for my ear. "
"Goodbye."
msgstr ""
"Ces mots me remplissent de joie. Hélas, les dieux m'appellent. Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:197
msgid "Still mixing the herbs, huh? See you later."
msgstr "Euh, tu mélanges toujours les herbes ? Au revoir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:198
msgctxt "hak021"
msgid ""
"We all have gardens. May your journeys act as tending. Be well. I must seek "
"audience with the gods now."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons tous un jardin. Puissent tes voyages servir de remède à tes maux. "
"Porte-toi bien, je m'en vais à présent demander audience auprès des dieux."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:199 dialog/dcsheila.msg:210 dialog/dctyler.msg:394
#: dialog/hcencha.msg:141 dialog/hczaius.msg:156
msgid "See ya."
msgstr "A plus."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:200
msgid "I'm betting you carry your audience with you wherever you go. Be well."
msgstr ""
"Je suis sûr que tu attires les foules partout où tu vas. Porte-toi bien."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:201
msgctxt "hak022"
msgid "Look to the north, Chosen, and the way will be open."
msgstr "Regarde vers le Nord, Etre Elu, et la route s'ouvrira."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:202 dialog/ahhakun.msg:208 dialog/cccook.msg:153
#: dialog/sccarkid.msg:116
msgid "Okay. Thanks."
msgstr "Ok. Merci."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:203
msgctxt "hak023"
msgid "I am honored to serve the Chosen."
msgstr "Je suis honoré de servir l'Etre Elu."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:204
msgctxt "hak024"
msgid ""
"Such is life. Two creates a third. You will need both xander root and broc "
"flower for the healing powder."
msgstr ""
"C'est la vie. Deux créent un tiers. Tu auras besoin de racine de Xandre et "
"de fleur de Broc pour la poudre de guérison."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:205
msgid "Oh. Thanks"
msgstr "Oh. Merci."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:206
msgid "Poo."
msgstr "Pouh."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:207
msgctxt "hak025"
msgid "May this be of no use."
msgstr "Puisse ceci ne jamais servir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:209 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:115 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:118
msgid "Uh!"
msgstr "Euh !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:210
msgctxt "hak026"
msgid "You are well."
msgstr "Tu vas bien."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:212
msgid "No lessons? No incomprehensible speeches? You sure you're okay?"
msgstr ""
"Pas de leçons ? Pas de discours incompréhensibles ? Tu es sûr que tu vas "
"bien ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:213
msgctxt "hak027"
msgid ""
"Welcome, Chosen. Bless us with words that the GECK will be found soon. Our "
"village ails, our need is great, our time, short."
msgstr ""
"Bienvenue, Etre Elu. Bénis-nous en nous disant que le J.E.K sera bientôt "
"découvert. Notre village souffre, notre besoin est grand, et le temps nous "
"est compté."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:214 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:116 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:119
#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:111 dialog/kcsulik.msg:324 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:107
msgid "Nuh."
msgstr "Nan."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:215
msgid "And your ability to speak normally, non-existent. I'm still trying."
msgstr "Et ton habilité à parler normalement, inexistante. J'essaie toujours."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:216
msgid "I'm on it. "
msgstr "J'y travaille. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:217
msgid "Get off my back, old man. I'm doing the best I can."
msgstr "Fiche-moi la paix, vieil homme. Je fais de mon mieux."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:218
msgid "I'm still looking, holy one. I hope to have the GECK soon."
msgstr ""
"Je cherche toujours, saint-homme. J'espère pouvoir rapidement me procurer le "
"J.E.K."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:219
msgctxt "hak028a"
msgid "May the Earth cushion the steps you must take."
msgstr "Que la Terre amortisse tes pas."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:220
msgctxt "hak028b"
msgid "May the Waters soothe your journey."
msgstr "Que les eaux apaisent ton voyage."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:221
msgctxt "hak028c"
msgid "May the Wind guide you to your goal."
msgstr "Que le vent te guide vers ton but."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:222
msgctxt "hak028d"
msgid "May the Fire toast your bottom until you get this done."
msgstr ""
"Et que le feu te grille les fesses jusqu'à ce que ta mission soit remplie."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:224
msgid "Say what?!"
msgstr "Qu'as+tu dit ?!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:226
msgid "Huh?!"
msgstr "Euh ?!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:227
msgctxt "hak029"
msgid ""
"Welcome back, Chosen. I see by your face the salvation of the GECK is not "
"yet ours. Be tireless as the ant before our reserves run out. You are our "
"last hope."
msgstr ""
"Bonjour, Etre Elu. Je vois que le J.E.K n'est pas encore à nous. Montre "
"autant de détermination que la fourmi, avant que nos réserves ne s'épuisent. "
"Tu es notre seul espoir."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:228 dialog/ahhakun.msg:234 dialog/ahhakun.msg:239
#: dialog/ecbhead.msg:138 dialog/ecbhead.msg:140 dialog/ecbhead.msg:1138
#: dialog/ecbhead.msg:1140 dialog/kcsulik.msg:114 dialog/kcsulik.msg:120
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:758 dialog/kcsulik.msg:950 dialog/kcsulik.msg:958
#: dialog/ncboxer.msg:207 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:149 dialog/scfelix.msg:112
#: dialog/scwestin.msg:124
msgid "Uh-huh."
msgstr "Euh-euh."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:229
msgid "I'm trying. I'd like to see the ant covering the miles I am."
msgstr ""
"J'essaie. J'aimerais bien voir la fourmi parcourir les kilomètres que je "
"parcours."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:230
msgid "I'm doing my best."
msgstr "Je fais de mon mieux."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:231
msgid "I'll double my efforts, holy one. I will not let you down."
msgstr ""
"Je vais redoubler d'efforts, saint homme. Je ne te laisserai pas tomber."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:232
msgid "Yeah, yeah. I've heard it all before."
msgstr "Ouais, ouais. J'ai déjà entendu ça."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:233
msgctxt "hak030"
msgid ""
"Chosen - the village cries in desperation. The children are weak with "
"hunger. Please, we cannot hold out much longer."
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu. Le village pleure de désespoir. Nous sommes affaiblis par la faim. "
"Je t'en prie. Nous ne pourrons pas tenir encore longtemps."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:235
msgid "I'm trying. I'm trying! Give me a break!"
msgstr "J'essaie. J'essaie ! Donne-moi une seconde chance !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:236
msgid "I'll find the GECK, holy one. You have my word."
msgstr "Je vais trouver le J.E.K, saint homme. Je t'en fais la promesse."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:237
msgid "I'll do my best to find the GECK."
msgstr "Je vais faire de mon mieux pour trouver le J.E.K."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:238
msgctxt "hak031"
msgid ""
"Chosen, the sands of time are but a few grains. Please. Bring the GECK soon "
"and make the future of the village like the beach of the ocean. Quickly, "
"before the last grain falls."
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, les dunes du temps s'égrènent. Trouve le J.E.K et fait du futur de "
"notre village la plage de l'océan. Vite, avant que le dernier grain ne "
"s'écoule."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:240
msgid "All right. I'm off to find it."
msgstr "Très bien, je vais le chercher."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:241
msgid "Life's a beach, huh?"
msgstr "La vie est une plage, hein ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:242
msgid "I will find the GECK, holy one. I will not let our people down."
msgstr ""
"Je trouverai le J.E.K, saint homme. Je ne vais pas laisser tomber notre "
"peuple."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:243
msgctxt "hak032"
msgid ""
"Chosen, the spirits of our ancestors guide me to a world of dreams that I "
"may touch thoughts. Our village suffers without the holy GECK. Your hands "
"hold our lives as a father holds his children."
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, les esprits de nos ancêtres me guident dans un monde de rêves que "
"je peux toucher par la pensée. Notre village souffre sans le saint J.E.K. "
"Nos vies sont entre tes mains."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:244
msgctxt "hak033"
msgid ""
"Once again my spirit touches you from the void, Chosen. Our crops fail, our "
"reserves are meager. Return to us with the GECK. Your failure is our last "
"light."
msgstr ""
"Une fois de plus mon esprit te touche dans le vide, Etre Elu. Nos récoltes "
"manquent, nos réserves sont maigres. Reviens-nous avec le J.E.K. Ton échec "
"est notre..."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:245
msgctxt "hak034"
msgid ""
"Chosen. The village weakens. It is harder to touch your dreams. You must "
"hurry or we will all..."
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu. Le village ne cesse de s'affaiblir. Tes rêves sont de plus en plus "
"inaccessibles. Tu dois te dépêcher sinon nous..."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:246
msgctxt "hak035"
msgid ""
"Chosen? Chosen? Do you hear me? The village dies. All of our futures die, "
"too. We have little left in both time and essence... Hurry. Hurry..."
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu ? Etre Elu ? Tu m'entends ? Le village se meurt. Tous nos avenirs "
"meurent eux aussi. Il ne nous reste plus beaucoup de temps ni beaucoup "
"d'essence. Vite... Vite..."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:247
msgctxt "hak101"
msgid "Chosen - the shadow of darkness arrived before you."
msgstr "Etre Elu. Les ombres des ténèbres sont arrivées avant toi."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:248
msgid "Owwww!"
msgstr "Ooooh !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:250
msgid "You look bad. Let me help."
msgstr "Ca n'a pas l'air d'aller. Laisse-moi t'aider."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:251
msgctxt "hak102"
msgid ""
"Child of Nature, how could we put such a burden on your shoulders? (sigh) "
"Your people have been taken."
msgstr ""
"Enfant de la Nature, comment avons-nous pu mettre un tel fardeau sur tes "
"épaules ? [Soupire...] Ton peuple a été pris."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:252
msgid "Uhh?"
msgstr "Euh ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:253
msgctxt "hak103"
msgid ""
"Yes. Gone. Many dark souls came, riding the metal birds like a flock of "
"hungry chittick bugs, hiding their evil in shiny skins. "
msgstr ""
"Oui. Envolé. Les âmes rongées furent nombreuses à venir, chevauchant les "
"oiseaux de métal comme une armée de tiques. Cachant leur méchanceté sous des "
"peaux dorées. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:254
msgid "Ooo! Shiny Purty!"
msgstr "Ooo ! C'est brillant et joli !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:255
msgctxt "hak104"
msgid ""
"No! Not shiny pretty! They kidnapped our people and took them to the "
"southwest."
msgstr ""
"Non ! Pas belles dorées ! Ils ont enlevé notre peuple et l'ont emmené au Sud-"
"Ouest."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:256 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:346
msgid "Ow."
msgstr "Oh là là !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:257
msgctxt "hak105"
msgid ""
"Yes. Great sadness and pain. I stand between worlds to tell you, Chosen. "
"Save your people."
msgstr ""
"Oui. La tristesse et la douleur sont grandes. Je suis entre les mondes pour "
"te dire ceci, Etre Elu. Sauve ton peuple."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:258 dialog/dcvicgrd.msg:434 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:123
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:105 dialog/kcsulik.msg:118 dialog/kcsulik.msg:323
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:926 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:106 dialog/scvortis.msg:111
msgid "Uh?"
msgstr "Hein ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:259
msgctxt "hak106"
msgid ""
"Chosen, please let my words touch you. Go southwest. South and west. Save "
"our people. Save our people."
msgstr ""
"Etre Elu, laisse mes mots t'atteindre. Va vers le Sud-Ouest. Sauve notre "
"peuple. Sauve notre peuple. Sauve notre peuple."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:260
msgid "Uh-huh.."
msgstr "Euh-euh."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:261
msgctxt "hak107"
msgid ""
"Thank the ancestors. Now my soul may join the eternal song. Safe journey, "
"Chosen."
msgstr ""
"Rends grâce aux ancêtres. A présent mon âme rejoint le chant éternel. Bon "
"voyage, Etre Elu."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:262
msgid "Go?"
msgstr "Partir ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:263
msgctxt "hak108"
msgid "Go!..."
msgstr "Partir... !"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:264 dialog/dcsheila.msg:200 dialog/dcsheila.msg:212
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:232 dialog/rclou.msg:120
msgid "Bye bye."
msgstr "Salut."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:265
msgctxt "hak109"
msgid "Dark souls came. They took everyone."
msgstr "Les âmes rongées sont venues. Elles ont pris tout le monde."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:266
msgid "Dark souls? What do you mean?"
msgstr "Les âmes rongées ? Que veux-tu dire par là ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:267
msgctxt "hak110"
msgid ""
"A rush of wind came. On it were great dragonflies that spat flame. Evil men "
"crawled from the beasts' bellies and brought death to our warriors."
msgstr ""
"Un coup de vent est apparu. Sur son dos, de grandes libellules crachaient "
"des flammes. Des hommes-démons sortirent en rampant des ventres des monstres "
"et semèrent la mort parmi nos guerriers."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:268
msgid "Our warriors couldn't stop them?"
msgstr "Nos guerriers n'ont pas réussi à les arrêter ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:269
msgctxt "hak112"
msgid ""
"The spirit was willing, but the spearheads were weak. The evil ones burned "
"our warriors with the lights of hell."
msgstr ""
"L'esprit était volontaire mais les fers de lance étaient faibles. Les démons "
"ont brûlé nos guerriers avec les flammes de l'enfer."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:270
msgid "They killed everyone?"
msgstr "Ils ont tué tout le monde ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:271
msgctxt "hak113"
msgid ""
"All were dead or taken. My spirit returned to flesh only to reveal the truth "
"to the Chosen."
msgstr ""
"Tous périrent ou furent enlevés. Mon esprit a repris chair uniquement pour "
"révéler à l'Etre Elu ce qui est arrivé."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:272
msgid "What happened to the ones taken?"
msgstr "Qu'est-il arrivé à ceux qui ont été enlevés ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:273
msgctxt "hak114"
msgid "The beasts swallowed all, then took to the winds."
msgstr "Les monstres ont tout avalé, puis se sont enfuis dans les vents."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:274
msgid "Uh, which way were the winds that they followed going?"
msgstr "Euh, quelle était la direction des vents qu'ils ont suivis ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:275
msgctxt "hak115"
msgid ""
"Did you never listen when I taught you the yearly dance of the wind spirits? "
"South, of course."
msgstr ""
"N'as-tu jamais écouté quand je te contais la danse annuelle des esprits du "
"vent ? Vers le Sud bien sûr."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:276
msgid ""
"Your descriptions were so vivid and powerful, great Hakunin, that I was "
"often stricken senseless for the duration of your lessons."
msgstr ""
"Tes descriptions étaient si vivantes et si puissantes, grand Hakunin, que je "
"n'avais parfois plus le contrôle de mes sens pendant tes leçons."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:277
msgid "Oh, those winds. Of course. "
msgstr "Oh, ces vents. Bien sûr. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:278
msgctxt "hak116"
msgid ""
"Yes, they traveled the wind south. I overheard the dark souls speaking. They "
"planned to rest their beasts at a place named Navarro before crossing the "
"great basin of our earth-mother's tears."
msgstr ""
"Ils ont suivi le vent du Sud. J'ai entendu parler les âmes rongées. Elles "
"laisseront reposer leurs monstres dans un lieu appelé Navarro avant de "
"traverser le grand bassin des larmes de notre mère Nature."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:279
msgid "What shall I do?"
msgstr "Que dois-je faire ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:280
msgid "Basin of tears?"
msgstr "Le bassin des larmes ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:281
msgctxt "hak117"
msgid ""
"For me, nothing. Chosen, you must seek the fold of the dark ones and rescue "
"our people."
msgstr ""
"Pour moi, rien. Etre Elu, tu dois lutter contre les âmes rongées et porter "
"secours à notre peuple."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:282 dialog/dccaesar.msg:323
msgid "I will try."
msgstr "Je vais essayer."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:283
msgctxt "hak118"
msgid "You are the Chosen. You must do."
msgstr "Tu es l'Etre Elu. Tu dois."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:284
msgid "Hakunin?"
msgstr "Hakunin ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:285
msgid "First time I understood what you meant."
msgstr "C'est la première fois que j'ai compris ce que tu me disais."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:286
msgctxt "hak120"
msgid "An ocean of tears, cried by a mother for her children."
msgstr "Un océan de larmes, pleuré par une mère pour ses enfants."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:287
msgid "Oh, the ocean. But what shall I do?"
msgstr "Oh, l'océan. Mais que dois-je faire ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:288
msgctxt "hak121"
msgid ""
"A strange mist stole their minds and sent them to the land of Sleep. The "
"evil ones walked among the dreamers, yet did not dream."
msgstr ""
"Une étrange brume a pris leurs esprits et les a expédiés au pays du sommeil. "
"Les démons ont marché parmi les rêveurs, et pourtant n'ont pas rêvé."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:290
msgctxt "hak122"
msgid "Too many seasons and too many wounds, Chosen. Instead, you must listen."
msgstr ""
"Trop de saisons et trop de blessures, Etre Elu. Tu devrais plutôt écouter."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:300
msgid "Those who steal carry a great burden. Remember this, Chosen One."
msgstr "Ceux qui volent portent un lourd fardeau. N'oublie pas cela, Etre Elu."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:301
msgid "You must now pay for your sins, Chosen One."
msgstr "Tu dois maintenant payer pour tes péchés, Etre Elu."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:100
msgid "You see the Abbot, the spiritual leader of the Abbey."
msgstr "Tu vois le Père Supérieur de l'Abbaye."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:101
msgid ""
"There's something about this monk that leads you to believe he's rather "
"important."
msgstr "Ce moine a l'air d'être le chef."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:200 dialog/amonk1.msg:200 dialog/amonk4.msg:200
msgid "Welcome traveler."
msgstr "Bienvenue voyageur."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:202 dialog/amonk1.msg:202
msgid "We are the guardians of knowledge."
msgstr "Nous sommes les gardiens de la connaissance."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:203
msgid "I'm sorry, but knowledge of our books is of no use to you."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolé, mais le savoir que contiennent nos livres ne vous sera "
"d'aucune utilité."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:300
msgid "Welcome to the Abbey, traveler. How can I help you?"
msgstr "Bienvenue à l'Abbaye, voyageur. Comment puis je vous aider ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:301 dialog/amonk4.msg:301
msgid "What can you tell me about your order?"
msgstr "Que peux-tu me dire au sujet de ton ordre ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:302
msgid "Have you ever heard of a device called a GECK?"
msgstr "Avez-vous déjà entendu parler d'un J.E.K ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:303 dialog/amonk5.msg:305
msgid "Do you know where I could find Vault 13?"
msgstr "Sais-tu où se trouve l'Abri 13 ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:401
msgid "Okay. I'd like to know something else."
msgstr "Ok. Je voudrais vous poser une autre question."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:402
msgid ""
"Hmm... that *does* sound familiar. Why, yes, I recall Brother Thomas "
"mentioning something about that recently. I'm sorry, but I don't recall "
"exactly what he said."
msgstr ""
"Hmm... Je crois me rappeler que quelqu'un dans notre Ordre possède ce "
"savoir. Oui, je m'en rappelle maintenant, Frère Thomas a étudié ceci "
"récemment."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:403
msgid "That's fine. Just point me to Brother Thomas and I'll go ask him."
msgstr ""
"Ça me va. Indiquez-moi simplement où trouver frère Thomas et j'irai lui "
"demander."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:405 dialog/vcdrtroy.msg:352
msgid "Well, thanks anyway."
msgstr "Bon, merci quand même."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:406
msgid ""
"I'm afraid I won't be able to do that. You see, I am under the impression "
"that Brother Thomas is no longer among\n"
" the living. But, fortunately for you, he was one of our most reliable "
"transcribers. I'm sure whatever articles he came\n"
" across concerning the information you seek has been transcribed into our "
"computers."
msgstr ""
"J'ai bien peur que Frère Thomas soit le seul à avoir possédé ce savoir. "
"Cependant, nos ordinateurs ont probablement gardé une trace."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:407
msgid ""
"Wait a second, you're \"under the impression\" that Brother Thomas is dead? "
"Where I come from, death is a pretty clear cut thing. So, is he dead, or "
"isn't he?"
msgstr "Il est mort ? Comment est-ce arrivé ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:408
msgid ""
"Brother Thomas has been missing for several days, ever since he went down to "
"the caverns below the Abbey. [He sighs wearily.]\n"
" You see, some of the Abbey's residents claimed to have seen a huge beast "
"lurking down there, and Brother Thomas was quite skeptical.\n"
" He took it upon himself to go dispel these rumors, yet, as it turns out, "
"his disappearance has only further validated them."
msgstr ""
"Une sorte de bête surpuissante qui vit sous notre église l'a tuée, en tout "
"cas, c'est ce que je crois. Il est descendu il y a quelques jours et nous "
"avons trop peur pour aller voir."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:409
msgid ""
"Hmmm. Maybe I should take a look what's down there. *I AM* the chosen one "
"after all..."
msgstr ""
"Hmmm. Peut-être devrais-je aller voir ce qu'il y a là dessous. Je *SUIS* "
"l'Etre Elu après tout..."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:410
msgid "I'm adventurous. I can take a look."
msgstr "J'aime l'aventure. Je vais aller y jeter un coup d'oeil."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:411
msgid ""
"You'd really do that? Perhaps while you're down there, you could look for a "
"certain book. You see, it was last\n"
" known to be in Brother Thomas's possession, and it's very important to us, "
"as it was passed down by our founders.\n"
" If you could retrieve that book, I would be most grateful. In fact, I'd "
"grant you full access to our computers, so you\n"
" can look for whatever you desire."
msgstr ""
"Vous feriez ça ? Frère Thomas avait sur lui un livre très important. Il "
"s'est transmis depuis nos fondateurs jusqu'à nous et j'aimerais le "
"récupérer. Je vous donnerai aussi accès à nos ordinateurs pour vous "
"permettre de chercher ce que vous désirez."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:412
msgid "It's a deal. I'll be back soon."
msgstr "Marché conclu. Je serai bientôt de retour."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:413
msgid "Maybe, let me think about this some more..."
msgstr "Peut-être... J'ai besoin d'un peu de temps pour y réfléchir."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:414
msgid "Thank you. Please let me know if you find the book."
msgstr "Bien. Quand vous aurez récupéré le livre, faites-le-moi savoir."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:415 dialog/ahmonk.msg:426
msgid "Ok, bye."
msgstr "Ok, salut."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:416
msgid "Hello, my friend."
msgstr "Rebonjour, mon ami."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:417
msgid "I've killed your beast, and I've got your book."
msgstr "J'ai tué la bête et récupéré le livre."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:418
msgid "Excellent! Let me have it!"
msgstr "Excellent ! Donnez-le-moi !"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:420
msgid "Not so fast. How much is it worth to you?"
msgstr "Pas si vite ! Combien il vaut, pour vous, ce livre ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:421
msgid ""
"[He takes the book from you and caresses its cover as if to sooth it.] You "
"have done us a great service. You now\n"
" have full access to our computers in the library. Tell Brother Paul I grant "
"you permission to access our files."
msgstr ""
"[Il t'arrache presque le livre des mains.] Vous nous avez rendu un grand "
"service. Vous avez maintenant accès à nos ordinateurs, dans la bibliothèque. "
"Dites au Frère Paul que vous avez la permission d'accéder à nos fichiers."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:423
msgid ""
"You want money for it? Fine, here's $250. Go see Brother Paul for access to "
"the computers."
msgstr ""
"Vous voulez en retirer de l'argent ? Très bien. Voilà $250. Allez voir Frère "
"Paul pour ce qui concerne l'accès à nos fichiers."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:424
msgid "Thanks for the money, bye."
msgstr "Merci pour l'argent, au revoir."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:425
msgid ""
"You should look on a second floor computer, now that you have full access "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Vous devriez allez faire un tour en bas, maintenant que vous y avez accès."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:430
msgid "What is the purpose of your order?"
msgstr "Quels sont les objectifs de votre Ordre ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:431
msgid "What is the history behind the Abbey?"
msgstr "Quelle est l'histoire de l'Abbaye ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:432
msgid "Hmm, I don't have any questions at the moment."
msgstr "Hmm, je n'ai plus de questions pour le moment."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:433
msgid ""
"Our holy mission is to read, copy and take care of our sacred books of "
"knowledge and other relics of the lost age.\n"
" It is our hope that with this knowledge we are able to create a Memorabilia "
"that might one day help humanity emerge from\n"
" its self-imposed Dark Age. Any information that we come across is recorded, "
"lest it be lost like so much was in the\n"
" great Flame Deluge."
msgstr ""
"Notre mission divine consiste à lire, copier et prendre soin des livres "
"sacrés, gardiens de la connaissance. Nous espérons que tout ce savoir "
"emmagasiné permettra un jour à l'humanité de se sortir de cet âge de "
"ténèbres. Toute information qui nous parvient est enregistrée afin qu'elle "
"ne soit pas perdue, comme ce fut le cas pour la plupart d'entre-elles durant "
"le Grand Déluge de Flammes."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:434
msgid ""
"After the Great War, the guiding hands of fate directed our ancestors to "
"this old Abbey in the mountains. Due to\n"
" its remote location, the monastery survived the Flame Deluge mostly "
"unscathed. As our ancestors explored the building,\n"
" they discovered an extensive library of books. And not just religious "
"texts, oh no, this library contained the gamut of\n"
" written works, from literary classics, to scientific encyclopedias."
msgstr ""
"Après la Grande Guerre, nos ancêtres vinrent ici et fondèrent notre Ordre "
"dans cette vieille église. Par chance, elle n'avait pas été endommagée et "
"les radiations étaient assez réduites pour permettre de vivre ici. "
"Lorsqu'ils furent installés, ils découvrirent une assez grande bibliothèque "
"à l'intérieur. De nombreux livres s'y trouvaient et les ordinateurs "
"débordaient d'informations."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:435
msgid "What happened then?"
msgstr "Et ensuite ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:436 dialog/ccmandr.msg:285 dialog/ncrenesc.msg:423
msgid "I've heard enough."
msgstr "J'en ai assez entendu."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:437
msgid ""
"They soon realized the true treasure trove of wisdom stored within those "
"books--especially the scientific tomes.\n"
" Here were the chronicles of a fallen civilization. A lost age. There were a "
"few who thought it might be best to\n"
" destroy this knowledge, for fear that it would once again guide humanity "
"towards apocalypse. But it was eventually\n"
" decided that they would instead dedicate themselves to ensuring the "
"preservation of the books, to be released when,\n"
" and if, the world was ready for it."
msgstr ""
"Peu après, nos ancêtres décidèrent de prendre soin de toutes ces "
"informations. Ils construisirent une petite imprimerie qui leur servit à "
"copier et à préserver les livres. Puis, ils commencèrent à désigner ce lieu "
"comme \"L'Abbaye\". Cependant, je ne connais pas les origines de ce nom."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:438
msgid "(More)"
msgstr "[Plus]"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:439
msgid ""
"And so, utilizing a small printing press, they began making copies of the "
"books, and also transcribing them\n"
" into the Abbey's computers to preserve them digitally, should the physical "
"books ever be destroyed. Over the long years,\n"
" others have come across the Abbey, and some have elected to stay and live "
"out their lives in the tranquil quiet of our mountain home."
msgstr ""
"Au cours des années, de plus en plus de survivants du désert échouèrent en "
"ce lieu par hasard. Ils se rendirent vite compte que c'était un endroit sûr "
"où vivre. Finalement, ils créèrent une petite communauté autour de celle de "
"nos ancêtres. Nous avons vécu en paix durant de nombreuses années et nous "
"espérons que de nombreuses autres suivront."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:440 dialog/dcstory1.msg:162 dialog/epac10.msg:3015
#: dialog/epac10.msg:3042 dialog/scdocjub.msg:151 dialog/scdocjub.msg:157
msgid "Thanks for the story."
msgstr "Merci pour l'histoire."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:441
msgid "Where did your ancestors come from?"
msgstr "D'où venaient vos ancêtres ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:442
msgid ""
"They never told where they originally came from. We suspect that they came "
"here originally from the east."
msgstr ""
"Ils n'ont jamais mentionné d'où ils venaient. Cependant, nous pensons qu'ils "
"venaient de l'Est."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:443
msgid "Well, thanks for the story."
msgstr "Bien... Merci pour l'histoire."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:444
msgid "Do you need any help here at the monastery?"
msgstr "Puis-je vous être utile d'une quelconque manière ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:445
msgid "I found out what's wrong with your water pump."
msgstr "J'ai trouvé quel est le problème avec la pompe à eau."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:446
msgid "Do you know anything about the original founders?"
msgstr "Que savez-vous des fondateurs ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:447
msgid ""
"I do not know all the names of our founders, but the most important one I am "
"aware of is Miller.\n"
" Before the Great War he was an electrical engineer working for the United "
"States government. Shortly thereafter,\n"
" he converted to Catholicism and made an oath with himself that we would "
"spend the rest of his life preserving the\n"
" knowledge of the past. His greatest fear was that this knowledge would be "
"lost forever and thus needed to be preserved\n"
" so that future generations may benefit."
msgstr ""
"Je ne connais pas le nom de tous nos fondateurs mais je connais celui du "
"plus important d'entre eux : Edward Leibowitz. Avant la Grande Guerre, il "
"était ingénieur en électronique pour le gouvernement des Etats-Unis. Peu "
"après, il se convertit au Catholicisme et se fit la promesse de passer le "
"restant de sa vie à mettre en sécurité les connaissances du passé. Sa plus "
"grande peur était que ce savoir fût perdu et, par conséquent, il voulut le "
"préserver afin que les générations futures puissent en bénéficier."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:448
msgid "You must be quite knowledgeable having read so much."
msgstr "Après avoir autant lu, vous devez être particulièrement instruit."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:449
msgid ""
"I have indeed read much in my life. Yet you might be disappointed at the "
"limitations of my knowledge. You see,\n"
" we record and preserve. We are forbidden to act upon the wisdom of these "
"books, therefore our understanding of the text is quite limited."
msgstr ""
"Je me rappelle de la plupart de ce que j'ai lu mais je ne comprends pas tout."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:450
msgid ""
"Wait, you're telling me that you just blindly transcribe these books without "
"even trying to comprehend them?"
msgstr ""
"Attendez, vous êtes en train de me dire que vous recopiez tout aveuglement. "
"Vous n'essayez pas de comprendre ce qui est écrit ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:451
msgid ""
"As I've said, it is our job to preserve this knowledge, not to understand "
"it. Before this knowledge can be\n"
" returned to mankind, he must first prove to have risen above his tendency "
"of mass genocide. That's the only way to\n"
" ensure that history does not repeat itself."
msgstr ""
"Non, notre travail consiste à préserver le savoir, pas à le comprendre. Nos "
"ancêtres n'ont jamais parlé de la compréhension des textes sacrés que nous "
"rassemblons."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:452
msgid ""
"Well, I've got news for you: that day's never going to come. And while "
"you're hoarding all this knowledge in your\n"
" little mountain paradise here, people out in the wasteland are struggling "
"every day to survive. In fact, my entire tribe\n"
" is on the brink of destruction. The knowledge contained in these books "
"could help cure diseases, improve crops, and greatly\n"
" increase the chance of humanity's survival."
msgstr ""
"Alors ce n'est pas de la connaissance. Le vrai savoir ne provient que de la "
"compréhension. La société ne peut pas évoluer si le savoir est aveuglément "
"recopié et mémorisé. Il vous faut agir en conséquence de ce que vous "
"apprenez. Les actes parlent plus que les mots."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:453
msgid ""
"Ah, well I suppose you make a good point. But it just seems like the "
"information stored here could help out a lot\n"
" of people. Even if you don't think the world's ready for this knowledge, I "
"don't see why *you* can't at least try to learn from it.\n"
" Otherwise, what's the point of keeping it?"
msgstr ""
"Ah, eh bien je suppose que vous faites bien de le souligner. Mais il "
"semblerait que les informations contenues ici pourraient aider beaucoup de "
"gens. Même si vous ne pensez pas que le monde soit prêt à obtenir ce savoir, "
"je ne vois pas pourquoi *vous* n'essayez pas d'en apprendre un peu plus. "
"Autrement, quel est l'intérêt de le garder ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:454
msgid ""
"I understand your frustration with our ways, but you must understand that "
"this is the way things have always been\n"
" for us. To alter things now, after so many years... that would be "
"blasphemous against our faith. No, I feel we must continue\n"
" to live by the rules set by our ancestors."
msgstr ""
"Je comprends votre frustration vis-à-vis de nos manières de faire, mais vous "
"devez comprendre que c'est de cette façon que nous avons toujours procédé. "
"Changer les choses maintenant, après tant d'années... Ce serait "
"blasphématoire envers notre foi. Non, mon sentiment est que nous devons "
"continuer de vivre selon les règles établies par nos ancêtres."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:455
msgid ""
"I understand your frustration with our ways, but you must understand that "
"this is the way things have always been\n"
" for us. To alter things now, after so many years... that would be "
"blasphemous against our faith. Still, I shall consider\n"
" your words. I sense great wisdom in you, wanderer. It is a pity I have met "
"very few like you."
msgstr ""
"Je comprends votre scepticisme quant à notre manière de vivre, mais vous "
"devez comprendre que c'est ainsi que nous vivons depuis toujours. Changez "
"les choses maintenant, après tant d'années... Ce serait un blasphème envers "
"notre foi... Malgré tout je devrais prendre en compte votre avis. Je sens "
"une grande sagesse en vous, nomade. Il est bien malheureux que vous soyez si "
"peu nombreux."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:456
msgid "Thanks. I'd like to know something else though."
msgstr "Merci. J'aimerais savoir autre chose..."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:457
msgid "Very well. I'd like to know something else though."
msgstr "Très bien. j'aimerais savoir autre chose."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:501
msgid "You gain %d experience points for bringing back the book."
msgstr "Tu gagnes %d points d'expérience pour avoir ramené le livre."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:600
msgid "I fixed your broken waterpump."
msgstr "J'ai réparé la pompe à eau."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:601
msgid ""
"That is great news, indeed. That waterpump had been acting up for quite some "
"time. Those merchants said they\n"
" could take care of it, but they didn't seem to be making much progress. "
"It's a good thing you came along. Thank you again."
msgstr ""
"C'est une excellente nouvelle. Cette pompe à eau avait toujours bien "
"fonctionné. Ces marchands sont restés ici quelques jours et je ne suis pas "
"sûr qu'ils aient fait beaucoup pour ça. Encore merci."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:602
msgid "I expect some money for this you know. Now cough it up!"
msgstr "J'attends une récompense maintenant. Et ça va casquer !"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:603 dialog/ncftully.msg:2014
msgid "No problem. I have some other questions though."
msgstr "Pas de problème. J'ai d'autres questions."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:604
msgid "I'm glad to be of assistance. Take care."
msgstr "Je suis content d'avoir pu vous aider. Prenez soin de vous."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:605
msgid ""
"[Frowns.] I see. Fine, here, take these coins. Now go, and stop bothering me."
msgstr ""
"[Air surpris.] Quoi ? Vous n'avez donc pas de coeur ? Très bien, prenez ça. "
"Maintenant, partez et arrêtez de me déranger."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:606
msgid "Thank you, *father*."
msgstr "Merci *mon Père*."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:700
msgid "Uhh... no I seem to have misplaced it."
msgstr "Euh... Je crois l'avoir mal placé."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:701
msgid ""
"What!? [He sighs deeply.] It is most unfortunate that you were unable to "
"recover that book. But you say you've\n"
" killed the beast? Hm, then it should be safe to send our own people down to "
"continue searching for it. Anyway, for your\n"
" service, I shall grant you access to our computers. Go see Brother Paul for "
"the access key."
msgstr ""
"Quoi !? [Il pousse un grand soupir.] Eh bien... J'aurais aimé retrouver ce "
"livre. Vous dites avoir tué la bête. C'est déjà ça. Bien sûr, je vous donne "
"quand même accès à nos ordinateurs. Allez voir Frère Paul, il vous donnera "
"la clé."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:800
msgid ""
"Actually, yes. Our main water pump has been acting up for some time, and now "
"it finally seems to have broken down\n"
" completely. If you know anything about machinery, do you think you could "
"take a look and see if something could be done?\n"
" There are a few merchants already working on it. I fear that little "
"progress has been made though."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien... Oui. Notre pompe à eau a fini par céder après quelques années de "
"bons et loyaux services. Pourriez-vous y jeter un coup d'oeil et essayez "
"d'arranger ça ? Il y a quelques marchands qui planchent déjà là-dessus. "
"Cependant, j'ai bien peur qu'ils ne soient pas arrivés à grand-chose."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:801
msgid "I'm happy to help. I'll report back on the progress."
msgstr ""
"Ca me fait plaisir de vous aider. Je vous informerai au fur et à mesure de "
"ce que je fais."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:802
msgid "Sure, I'll be glad to help... for a price of course."
msgstr "Bien sûr, je serais content de vous aider... Si vous y mettez le prix."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:803
msgid "Actually on second thought, let me ask you something else."
msgstr "Finalement, je vais vous poser une autre question."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:804
msgid ""
"What!? Oh, fine. If that's the kind of person you are, then you shall "
"receive payment for your service. Here's\n"
" 25 coins to begin with.  Please let me know if something can be done. [The "
"man sighs as he hands you the coins]"
msgstr ""
"Quoi !? Oh, je vois. Vous êtes comme ça... Dans ce cas-la, vous serez "
"*dédommagé*. Voilà déjà $25 pour commencer. Faites-moi savoir s'il y a "
"encore un problème. [Il soupire en te payant.]"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:805
msgid ""
"Hey, no need for the sighing. You think everything in life comes for free? "
"Now, let me get to work."
msgstr ""
"Hé, pas la peine de soupirer. Vous croyez que tout est gratuit dans la vie ? "
"Maintenant, foutez-moi la paix, que je répare tout ça."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:806
msgid "Really? Please, do tell."
msgstr "Vraiment ? Dites-le-moi s'il vous plaît."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:807
msgid ""
"The motor gave out and fried all the connectors. I'm going to Vault City to "
"get a new part."
msgstr ""
"Il semble que le moteur soit mort et idem pour les connecteurs. Je vais "
"chercher le matos à la Cité de l'Abri."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:808
msgid ""
"Oh thank you. You are indeed a great help. Please report back once you "
"install the new part."
msgstr ""
"Oh merci. Vous nous êtes d'une grande aide. Faites-moi signe lorsque vous "
"aurez fini."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:809
msgid "I will. Be back soon."
msgstr "Je reviendrai. A bientôt."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:900
msgid ""
"You explain to the Abbot that while the information they hold could lead to "
"mankind's annihilation, it could also lead to mankind's salvation."
msgstr ""
"Tu expliques au Père Supérieur, mais en vain, que le progrès ne peut venir "
"que des actes."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:901
msgid "You learn about the original founder of the Abbey."
msgstr "Tu as découvert qui est le fondateur de l'Abbaye."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1000
msgid "I killie scary monster down in cave."
msgstr "Moi avoir tué monstre de caverne."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1010
msgid "Really? That's great. That is very brave of you. You're a big boy."
msgstr ""
"Vraiment ? C'est génial. C'est très courageux de ta part. Tu es un grand "
"garçon."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1011
msgid "Really? That's great. That is very brave of you. You're a big girl."
msgstr ""
"Vraiment ? Excellent. C'est très courageux de ta part. Tu es une grande "
"fille."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1012
msgid "(smile) I know."
msgstr "[Tu souris.] Je sais."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1020
msgid ""
"Did you happen to find a book lying there? A friend of mine had it, and he "
"went missing."
msgstr ""
"As-tu trouvé un livre qui traînait ici ? Un de mes amis l'avait, et il l'a "
"perdu."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1021
msgid "I find book. Here, it heavy and no pitchers inside."
msgstr "Moi trouvé livre. Tiens, ça lourd et compliqué."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1022
msgid "I no find book. Sorree. I go look now."
msgstr "Moi pas trouvé livre. Etre désolé. Moi cherché."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1030
msgid "I find book."
msgstr "J'ai trouvé un livre."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1031
msgid "That's great. Thanks. You're one special guy."
msgstr "C'est très bien. Merci. Tu es vraiment un garçon spécial."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1032
msgid "That's great. Thanks. You're one special gal."
msgstr "C'est très bien. Merci. Tu es vraiment un garçon spécial."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1033
msgid "YAY."
msgstr "Youpi."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1100
msgid ""
"I was down there earlier. I saw a few dead bodies, so I'm guessing one of "
"them belonged to your missing monk. If\n"
" it makes you feel any better, I killed the thing responsible for his death."
msgstr ""
"J'étais là-bas plus tôt, j'ai vu quelques cadavres, je pense que l'un "
"d'entre eux était celui de votre moine disparu. Si ça peut vous consoler, "
"j'ai tué la chose responsable de sa mort."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1110
msgid ""
"Ah... so it's as I feared. Brother Thomas shall be dearly missed. You have "
"my thanks for ridding us of whatever\n"
" wasteland beasts lurked down there. However, I... I don't suppose you found "
"a book while you were down there. It's a very\n"
" important book that was last known to be in Brother Thomas's possession."
msgstr ""
"Ah... C'est bien ce que je craignais. Frère Thomas nous manquera beaucoup. "
"Vous avez mes remerciements pour avoir traqué et éliminé la bête qui "
"sévissait là-bas. Cependant, je... je suppose que vous n'auriez pas trouvé "
"un livre là-bas. C'est un livre très important qui avait été vu pour la "
"dernière fois entre les mains de frère Thomas."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1111
msgid "No, but I suppose I could go back and check."
msgstr "Non mais je suppose que je peux y retourner et vérifier."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1112
msgid "Do you mean this book?"
msgstr "Vous voulez dire ce livre ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1113
msgid "Before I go, let me ask you something else."
msgstr "Avant que j'y aille, laissez-moi vous demander autre chose."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1411
msgid "Very interesting. I have to go now."
msgstr "Trèèès intéressant. Faut que j'y aille."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:4091
msgid ""
"So no one else has even bothered to go down there and check on him? What if "
"he's simply trapped down there somehow, and he's slowly starving to death?"
msgstr ""
"Donc personne d'autre n'a pris la peine de descendre là-bas pour voir "
"comment il va ? Et s'il était simplement coincé, et qu'il mourait doucement "
"de faim ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:4092
msgid ""
"I suppose that's possible, but you must understand. We are a peaceful "
"people. The thought of going up against one of those wasteland monsters is "
"terrifying to us. We're simply not equipped for such confrontations. "
msgstr ""
"J'imagine que c'est possible, mais il faut que vous compreniez. Nous sommes "
"des gens pacifiques. L'idée de devoir affronter un de ces monstres du désert "
"nous terrifie. Nous ne sommes pas préparés à de tels affrontements. "

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:4177
msgid "I've killed the beast."
msgstr "J'ai tué la bête."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:4188
msgid "Excellent! And how about the book; were you able to recover it?"
msgstr "Excellent ! Et pour le livre, l'avez-vous trouvé ?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:6020
msgid ""
"If you truly want to show your gratitude, how about some money for my "
"trouble?"
msgstr ""
"Si vous voulez vraiment me montrer votre gratitude, que pensez-vous d'un peu "
"d'argent ?"

#: dialog/aichest.msg:100 dialog/aivase.msg:100
msgid "You see a simple vase."
msgstr "Tu vois un vase ordinaire."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:101
msgid "You see a small chest."
msgstr "Tu vois un petit coffret."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:102 dialog/aivase.msg:101
msgid "You see a sun-baked clay vase."
msgstr "Tu vois un vase en terre cuite."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:103
msgid "You see a chest for the shaman's herbs."
msgstr "Tu vois un coffret pour les herbes de shaman."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:104
msgid "You deftly steal from the shaman's things."
msgstr "Tu réussis à dérober adroitement des choses dans le coffret de shaman."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:105
msgid "You skillfully lock the chest."
msgstr "Tu fermes habilement le coffre."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:106
msgid "You skillfully unlock the chest."
msgstr "Tu ouvres habilement le coffre."

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:100 dialog/amonk2.msg:100 dialog/amonk3.msg:100
#: dialog/amonk4.msg:100
msgid "You see a monk."
msgstr "Tu vois un moine."

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:101 dialog/amonk2.msg:101 dialog/echlyppl.msg:106
msgid "You see a holy woman."
msgstr "Tu vois une illuminée."

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:103 dialog/amonk2.msg:103
msgid "You see a regular Abbey nun."
msgstr "Tu vois une nonne ordinaire de l'Abbaye."

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:203 dialog/atribal.msg:202 dialog/dccustmr.msg:304
#: dialog/dcg2grd.msg:274 dialog/dcg2grd.msg:300 dialog/dcorphan.msg:271
#: dialog/dcorphan.msg:282 dialog/dcorphan.msg:291 dialog/dcorphan.msg:303
#: dialog/dcpengrd.msg:235 dialog/dcrebdor.msg:213 dialog/dcstory2.msg:115
#: dialog/echomkid.msg:210 dialog/kctorr.msg:276 dialog/ocsandy.msg:139
msgid "Hi."
msgstr "Salut."

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:205
msgid "I hope you enjoy your stay here."
msgstr "J'espère que tu apprécies ton séjour ici."

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:200 dialog/amonk3.msg:202 dialog/atribal.msg:200
#: dialog/atribal.msg:205 dialog/tribec8.msg:104
msgid "Greetings."
msgstr "Salutations."

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:201 dialog/atribal.msg:201
msgid "Welcome to the Abbey."
msgstr "Bienvenue à l'Abbaye."

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:202
msgid "You should talk to our leader if you wish to gain any information."
msgstr ""
"Tu devrais parler à notre meneur si tu souhaites obtenir des informations."

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:203
msgid "Good day... or is it night already?"
msgstr "Bonne journée... Ou est-ce déjà la nuit ?"

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:204
msgid "There's so much work that must be done."
msgstr "Il y a tellement de travail qui doit être fait."

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:205
msgid ""
"Life here at the Abbey is a peaceful one. Something rare in these wretched "
"wastes."
msgstr ""
"La vie ici à l'Abbaye est paisible. Quelque chose de rare dans ces déserts "
"malheureux."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:101
msgid "You see a nun."
msgstr "Tu vois une nonne."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:102
msgid "This monk looks like he knows a thing or two about computers."
msgstr "Ce moine semble connaître une chose ou deux sur les ordinateurs."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:103
msgid "This nun looks like she knows a thing or two about computers."
msgstr "Cette nonne semble connaître une chose ou deux sur les ordinateurs."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:200
msgid "Don't break anything."
msgstr "Ne casse rien."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:201
msgid "Sorry, I'm rather busy at the moment."
msgstr "Désolé, je suis plutôt occupé à l'heure actuelle."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:203
msgid "Feel free to look around."
msgstr "N'hésite pas à regarder autour de toi."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:204
msgid "We copy the knowledge for the future generations."
msgstr "Nous copions nos connaissances pour les futures générations."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:205
msgid "These old books are very fragile."
msgstr "Ces vieux livres sont très fragiles."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:206
msgid "Copying books is pretty hard work."
msgstr "Copier des livres est un travail assez dur."

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:208
msgid "There's much to copy down from these books."
msgstr "Il y a beaucoup à extraire de ces livres."

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:101
msgid "This monk looks like a trader."
msgstr "Ce moine ressemble à un commerçant."

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:203
msgid "Go play somewhere else."
msgstr "Va jouer ailleurs."

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:300
msgid "Hi, how can I help you?"
msgstr "Salut, comment puis je t'aider ?"

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:400
msgid ""
"Our holy mission is to collect and preserve the sacred relics of the "
"forgotten past. Anyone is welcome here, as long as they don't damage "
"anything."
msgstr ""
"Notre sainte mission est de lire, copier et prendre soin de nos bibles de la "
"connaissance. Nous aimons partager nos connaissances avec n'importe qui "
"aussi longtemps qu'ils n'endommagent rien."

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:401
msgid "Who is your leader?"
msgstr "Qui est ton meneur ?"

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:402
msgid "What kind of relics?"
msgstr "Quel genre de connaissance ?"

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:403
msgid ""
"He can be found on the third floor. If you wish to learn more about our "
"order, he is the one to talk to."
msgstr ""
"Il peut être trouvé au troisième étage. Si tu souhaites en apprendre plus au "
"sujet de notre ordre, il est celui à qui parler."

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:404
msgid ""
"All sorts, but most of our Memorabilia consist of ancient tomes. So much "
"information can be obtained from those texts. It is our mission to preserve "
"this knowledge so that a future generation may use it to build a new world "
"of peace and joy."
msgstr ""
"Sous la forme de livres. Tant d'informations peuvent être obtenues de ces "
"textes. C'est notre mission que de les préserver pour les générations "
"futures."

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:406 dialog/amonk5.msg:403 dialog/bckarla.msg:105
#: dialog/ccdrgrd.msg:125 dialog/ccgguard.msg:130 dialog/fctnkbar.msg:115
#: dialog/fctnkbar.msg:121 dialog/fctnkbar.msg:127 dialog/fctnkbar.msg:130
#: dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:115 dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:120 dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:125
#: dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:127 dialog/fctnkmer.msg:115 dialog/fctnkmer.msg:121
#: dialog/fctnkmer.msg:127 dialog/fctnkmer.msg:130 dialog/fsface.msg:130
#: dialog/fsface.msg:135 dialog/fsface.msg:140 dialog/fsface.msg:219
#: dialog/gsterm.msg:740 dialog/kcardin.msg:301 dialog/kcardin.msg:390
#: dialog/kcdunton.msg:520 dialog/kcsally.msg:391 dialog/ocdar.msg:114
#: dialog/ocdar.msg:123 dialog/ocsandy.msg:127 dialog/scelise.msg:147
#: dialog/scelise.msg:172 dialog/scelise.msg:174 dialog/scjohn.msg:109
#: dialog/shtandi.msg:232 dialog/shtandi.msg:283
msgid "Ok."
msgstr "Ok."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:100
msgid "You see a computer monk."
msgstr "Tu vois un moine informaticien."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:101
msgid "You see Brother Paul."
msgstr "Tu vois frère Paul."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:102
msgid "This monk looks like a computer geek."
msgstr "Ce moine à l'air d'un fada d'informatique."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:202
msgid "Now, did I backup those computer files today..."
msgstr "Alors, ai-je sauvegardé ces fichiers informatiques aujourd'hui..."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:203
msgid "I'm sorry, but I don't have time for someone of your intelligence."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolé, mais je n'ai pas de temps à consacrer à quelqu'un de ton "
"intelligence."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:300 dialog/dcrebecc.msg:220 dialog/dctyler.msg:371
#: dialog/epac11.msg:402 dialog/epac12.msg:300 dialog/epac17.msg:120
#: dialog/hceric.msg:131 dialog/ncethwri.msg:431 dialog/nckitty.msg:350
#: dialog/nclabish.msg:260 dialog/ncmcgee.msg:370 dialog/qcgensci.msg:157
#: dialog/scskeete.msg:141 dialog/vcandy.msg:247 dialog/vcandy.msg:281
#: dialog/vcbarcit.msg:151 dialog/vcdrtroy.msg:285 dialog/vcgenfam.msg:157
#: dialog/vckohl.msg:178 dialog/vcwrkcit.msg:151
msgid "Yes?"
msgstr "Oui ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:301
msgid "You guys sure have a lot of computers here."
msgstr "Vous avez plein d'ordinateurs ici les gars."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:303
msgid "Tell me about your leader."
msgstr "Parle-moi de ton chef."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:304
msgid "Do you have any info about a GECK?"
msgstr "Aurais-tu des informations sur le J.E.K ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:307
msgid "I am in need of some specific information."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de quelques informations."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:400
msgid ""
"Yes, we have. Too many, in my opinion. I can't express to you the tedium of "
"having to back up all these files\n"
" each and every day. There's just so much information to preserve, but, of "
"course, it must be done."
msgstr ""
"Oui, nous en avons plein. Trop à mon avis. C'est lourd de sauvegarder toutes "
"ces données tous les jours. Ca fait beaucoup d'informations à préserver, "
"mais c'est pour l'intérêt de tous."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:401
msgid "Of course. Anyway, I have some other questions."
msgstr "Je peux comprendre... J'aurais d'autres questions."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:402
msgid ""
"We are an independent community. Anyone is welcome as long as they behave "
"themselves."
msgstr ""
"Nous sommes une communauté indépendante. Tout le monde est le bienvenu tant "
"qu'on fait attention à son comportement."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:404
msgid ""
"The Abbot is a good spiritual leader, but he's been a little cranky since we "
"lost Brother Thomas to the beast."
msgstr ""
"C'est un bon chef. Il est un peu grincheux depuis que cette bête à tué frère "
"Thomas."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:405
msgid "What kind of beast?"
msgstr "Quel genre de bête ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:406
msgid ""
"I haven't seen it, personally--there's nothing in the world that could get "
"me to go down there and explore those\n"
" caverns--but if I had to guess, I'd say it's probably just some overgrown "
"radscorpion."
msgstr "Je ne l'ai pas vu mais je pense que c'est un grand radscorpion."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:407
msgid "If you haven't seen it, then what makes you think it's a radscorpion?"
msgstr "Pourquoi penses-tu que ce serait un radscorpion ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:408
msgid ""
"Because I've heard sounds echoing up from the caves--the sounds of snapping "
"claws and skittering legs."
msgstr ""
"Parce que j'ai entendu des bruits venant des grottes et on aurait dit ceux "
"qu'émettent les radscorpions."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:409 dialog/dcflick.msg:431 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:196
#: dialog/hcmarcus.msg:317 dialog/tribec2.msg:161 dialog/vclynett.msg:831
msgid "Right."
msgstr "Très bien."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:410
msgid ""
"In fact, we do. Take a look on that computer over there. Here, you can use "
"this card to access our encrypted files. [He hands you an access card.]"
msgstr ""
"Oui nous devons avoir ça, regarde sur cet ordinateur. Tiens, prends cette "
"carte d'accès afin de pouvoir lire les fichiers cryptés. [Il te donne la "
"carte d'accès.]"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:411
msgid "Wow, thanks a lot!"
msgstr "Wahou, merci beaucoup !"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:412
msgid ""
"I don't know anything about Vault 13, but there is Vault City down south. "
"Maybe they have the info you need."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais rien sur l'Abri 13, mais vers le Sud, il y a la Cité de l'Abri. "
"Peut-être qu'ils auront des réponses à tes questions."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:414
msgid ""
"That computer near me should have the information you seek, but you'd need "
"an access card to use it.\n"
" We're very selective with who we give access to, but if you speak to the "
"Abbot, perhaps he'll grant you permission."
msgstr ""
"Cet ordinateur à côté de moi devrait avoir des informations là-dessus. Tu as "
"besoin d'une carte d'accès. Je ne donne pas cette carte d'accès à n'importe "
"qui, tu devrais en parler au chef avant."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:415 dialog/rcjane.msg:231 dialog/scwestin.msg:170
msgid "Ok, thanks."
msgstr "D'accord, merci."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:420
msgid ""
"I'm guessing you've read a lot of books in your time. So I'm curious, what's "
"the most fascinating thing you could tell me?"
msgstr ""
"Tu as lu beaucoup de livres, à la fois techniques et non techniques, dans ta "
"vie ? Y a-t-il un sujet qui t'intéresse plus que les autres ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:421
msgid ""
"Hmm, let's see. Did you know a notch in a tree will remain the same distance "
"from the ground as the tree grows?"
msgstr ""
"Hmm, voyons. Savais-tu qu'une entaille dans un arbre reste toujours à la "
"même distance du sol alors que l'arbre grandit ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:422
msgid ""
"Sure. If I come across anything like that, I'll be sure to let you know."
msgstr ""
"D'accord. Si je trouve quoi que ce soit de ce genre, je te le ferai savoir."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:423
msgid "Right... Well, I have some other questions."
msgstr "Ouais... Euh, j'aurais d'autres questions."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:424
msgid "Would you? I'd appreciate that."
msgstr "Tu ferais ça ? J'apprécie beaucoup."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:425
msgid "No problem. I have some other questions."
msgstr "De rien. J'aurais d'autres questions."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:426
msgid "Any time. Well, see you around."
msgstr "Pas de problème. A plus tard."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:430
msgid "I found some information about Botany that might interest you."
msgstr ""
"J'ai trouvé des informations sur la botanique qui devraient t'intéresser."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:431
msgid "Really?! That's great. Please, do tell immediately."
msgstr "Vraiment ?! C'est génial. S'il te plaît, raconte-moi tout de suite."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:432
msgid ""
"Fascinating! I shall take this holodisk and add it to the computer database "
"immediately. I appreciate you\n"
" taking the time to find this for me. Thank you for collecting this for me."
msgstr ""
"Fascinant ! Je vais récupérer les données de cet holodisque dans "
"l'ordinateur immédiatement. J’apprécie que tu aies pris le temps de le "
"faire. Merci de l'avoir récupéré pour moi."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:433
msgid ""
"Well you see... Understanding habitat destruction and species extinction is "
"dependent on an accurate and complete catalog of plant systematics and "
"taxonomy. And then this means that..."
msgstr ""
"Hum tu vois... La compréhension de la destruction de l'habitat et de "
"l'extinction des espèces dépend de la qualité d'un catalogue précis et "
"complet sur la systémique des plantes et la taxonomie. Cela signifie que..."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:434
msgid "Any time. I have some other questions though."
msgstr "En fait j'aurais encore quelques questions."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:435 dialog/vilann.msg:202
msgid "No problem. See you around."
msgstr "Pas de problème. A plus tard."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:436
msgid ""
"Fascinating! I appreciate you taking the time to find this for me. Please go "
"and upload this information to our computers."
msgstr ""
"Fascinant ! J'apprécie que tu aies pris le temps de faire ça pour moi. S'il "
"te plaît, charge ces données dans l'ordinateur."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:437
msgid "No problem, I'll do that now. See you around."
msgstr "Pas de problème, je le ferai. A plus tard."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:500
msgid "Stop that, moron!"
msgstr "Arrête ça, idiot !"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:550
msgid ""
"That computer near me should have some information about it. You now have "
"access, so take a look for yourself."
msgstr ""
"Cet ordinateur à côté de moi devrait avoir des informations sur ce sujet. Tu "
"as l'accès désormais, tu peux utiliser l'ordinateur si tu le souhaites."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:600
msgid "The Abbot gave me permission to access the computers here."
msgstr "Le chef des moines m'a donné la permission d'accéder à ces ordinateurs."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:601
msgid ""
"Ah yes, I heard about what you did. Thanks for taking care of that "
"situation. Here is the access key. (He hands you the key.) Enjoy!"
msgstr ""
"Ah oui, on m'a raconté ce que tu as fait. Merci d'avoir pris en charge la "
"situation. Tiens voilà la carte d'accès. [Il te donne la carte.] Amuse-toi "
"bien !"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:602 dialog/hcdorgrd.msg:282 dialog/ncbrkmn.msg:307
msgid "Thanks. See you around."
msgstr "Merci. A plus tard."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:650
msgid ""
"Greetings traveler! I am Brother Paul and I am in charge of the collection "
"of information for the Abbey. What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""
"Salutations voyageur ! Je suis frère Paul et je suis en charge du système "
"informatique de l'Abbaye. Que puis-je faire pour toi ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:651
msgid "Nice to meet you, Paul. I have some questions."
msgstr "Heureux de te faire ta connaissance, Paul. J'aurais des questions."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4210
msgid "Uh, no, I can't say I knew that. That's... interesting."
msgstr "Euh, non, je ne peux pas dire que je le savais. C'est... intéressant."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4211
msgid "And did you know a cucumber is 96% water?"
msgstr "Et savais-tu qu'un concombre est constitué de 96% eau ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4212
msgid "Wow, 96%, huh? Fascinating. But, um, what's a cucumber?"
msgstr "Sans blague, 96%, euh ? Fascinant. Mais, euh, c'est quoi un concombre ?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4213
msgid ""
"I've never seen one, but I've read about them. [He looks around nervously "
"and lowers his voice.] I know we're\n"
" not supposed to actually study these books, but when I was transcribing a "
"book on botany, I just couldn't help but get\n"
" sucked into it. The world of plants is simply captivating. Perhaps, if, "
"during your travels, you happen upon some botany\n"
" information, you could bring it to me? I'd be most grateful. Of course, "
"it'd have to be our secret."
msgstr ""
"Je n'en ai jamais vu, mais j'ai lu quelque chose à ce propos. [Il regarde "
"autour de lui nerveusement et baisse la voix.] Je sais que nous ne sommes "
"pas supposés étudier ces livres, mais alors que je transcrivais un livre de "
"botanique, je ne pouvais pas m'empêcher d'être fasciné par celui-ci. Le "
"monde des plantes est tout simplement passionnant. Peut-être que si pendant "
"tes voyages, il arrivait que tu trouves des informations sur la botanique, "
"tu pourrais me les apporter ? Je t'en serais très reconnaissant. Bien "
"entendu, il faudra que cela reste notre secret."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4220
msgid "I don't think I want to contribute to your plant obsession. Sorry."
msgstr "Je ne pense pas vouloir participer à ton obsession des plantes. Désolé."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4221
msgid "Oh, well then. Fine, forget I asked."
msgstr "Oh, très bien dans ce cas. Parfait, oublie ça."

#: dialog/arbridge.msg:100
msgid ""
"You are standing at the Great Bridge, passageway from\n"
" your village to the vast Wasteland."
msgstr ""
"Tu te trouves sur le grand pont séparant ton village de l'immense Désert."

#: dialog/arcaves.msg:100
msgid ""
"You are in a dark, musty temple. The shadows seem to\n"
" play tricks with your eyes, and you can hear the faint sound of movement."
msgstr ""
"Tu entres dans un temple obscur qui sent le renfermé. Les ombres semblent te "
"jouer des tours et tu entends quelque chose bouger devant toi."

#: dialog/arvillag.msg:100
msgid "You are once more in the village of your birth, Arroyo."
msgstr "Te voilà une nouvelle fois dans ton village natal, Arroyo."

#: dialog/aswell.msg:100
msgid "The well has not worked in a while. It needs to be repaired."
msgstr ""
"Le puits n'a pas fonctionné depuis un bon moment. Il a besoin d'être réparé."

#: dialog/aswell.msg:101
msgid "The well is working fine."
msgstr "Le puits fonctionne bien."

#: dialog/atribal.msg:100
msgid "You see a Tribal."
msgstr "Tu vois un tribal."

#: dialog/atribal.msg:101
msgid "You see a strong looking man."
msgstr "Tu vois un homme d'apparence robuste."

#: dialog/atribal.msg:204
msgid "Are you from the Arroyo tribe?"
msgstr "Es-tu de la tribu d'Arroyo ?"

#: dialog/atribal.msg:206
msgid "Nice outfit!"
msgstr "Jolie tenue !"

#: dialog/atribal.msg:207
msgid "Hello, fellow tribal!"
msgstr "Bonjour, frère tribal !"

#: dialog/atribal.msg:500
msgid "Don't mess with my stuff!"
msgstr "Touche pas à mes affaires !"

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:100 dialog/bcjohn.msg:100 dialog/bcrobert.msg:100
#: dialog/bcsara.msg:100 dialog/dcaddct2.msg:100 dialog/fcdocsqa.msg:101
#: dialog/kctrapr.msg:102 dialog/scjohn.msg:100
msgid "You see a squatter."
msgstr "Tu vois un squatteur."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:101
msgid "You see Bill, the squatter."
msgstr "Tu vois Bill, le squatteur."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:102
msgid "You see a middle aged man wearing worn clothing."
msgstr "Tu vois un homme d'âge moyen portant des vêtements usés."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:103
msgid "Sorry, stranger. I don't have time to chat with you."
msgstr "Je regrette mais je n'ai pas le temps de discuter avec toi."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:104
msgid "Hey, I said I don't have time to chat. Please go away."
msgstr "Hé, j'ai dit que j'avais pas le temps de parler. Allez, va-t'en."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:105
msgid "Thanks for helping Rebecca. That was a fine thing you did."
msgstr "Merci d'avoir aidé Elisabeth. Tu as fait quelque chose de bien."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:106
msgid "Leave me alone. I'm no threat to you."
msgstr "Laisse-moi, je ne te veux aucun mal."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:107
msgid "All right, all right. I'm moving."
msgstr "Très bien, très bien, j'me pousse."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:100 dialog/kcattend.msg:106 dialog/kcbgirl.msg:106
#: dialog/vilann.msg:100
msgid "You see a young woman."
msgstr "Tu vois une jeune femme."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:101
msgid "You see Chrissy, Rebecca's daughter."
msgstr "Tu vois Chrissy, la fille d'Elisabeth."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a pretty young woman. She looks confident and able to handle herself "
"in a fight."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois une jolie jeune fille. Elle semble sûre d'elle et capable de se "
"débrouiller en cas de combat."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:103
msgid ""
"If you're here to try and rape me, you're going to be wearing your balls as "
"a bow tie. Get it?"
msgstr ""
"Si tu es ici pour essayer de me violer, je vais te faire bouffer tes bijoux "
"de famille. Compris ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:104
msgid ""
"Let me guess. The guys are tired of me kicking them where it hurts, so they "
"sent you in here to\n"
" do something obscene. Well, I can hurt you just as bad; I just need to kick "
"higher. Get it?"
msgstr ""
"Laisse-moi deviner. Les gars en ont marre de moi, alors ils t'envoient ici "
"pour que tu me fasses des trucs obscènes. Hé bien, accroche-toi parce que "
"j'vais te donner une raclée. Compris ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:105
msgid "Bow tie?"
msgstr "Hein ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:107 dialog/bccrissy.msg:125
msgid "What go on here? Who you?"
msgstr "Quoi se passer ici ? Qui toi être ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:109 dialog/bccrissy.msg:117 dialog/bccrissy.msg:127
msgid "I'd like to know who you are and what is going on here."
msgstr "J'aimerais savoir qui tu es et ce qui se passe ici."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:110
msgid ""
"Yeah. A fancy piece of cloth worn around the neck for decoration. It's like "
"a scarf, but for\n"
" men. Now, just imagine me kicking you SO hard that you end up wearing your "
"dangly about your neck. Get\n"
" it?"
msgstr ""
"Ouais, je vais te donner une raclée. Hein, qu'est-ce que t'en dis ? Imagine "
"que je vais te faire TELLEMENT mal que tu ne pourras plus jamais t'en "
"remettre. T'as compris ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:111
msgid "Me understand. You no hurt me."
msgstr "Moi comprendre. Toi pas faire mal à moi."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:112
msgid "I got the picture; please don't hurt me."
msgstr "J'ai compris. S'te plaît, ne m'fais pas de mal."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:113
msgid "Okay, so why are you here?"
msgstr "Ok, alors pourquoi es-tu ici ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:115
msgid "Me want know what go on here? Who you?"
msgstr "Moi vouloir savoir quoi se passer ici ? Qui toi être ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:118
msgid "Really? Awesome! Let's go."
msgstr "Vraiment ? Génial ! Allons-y."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:120
msgid ""
"In a nutshell, my name is Chrissy and I'm from the Squat. I was out "
"exploring last week when I\n"
" found that entrance out there. I thought it might be an abandoned mine or "
"something, so I decided to\n"
" check it out. Well, it's not a mine; it's a secret entrance into Vault 15. "
"The vault is being\n"
" used as a base for a band of raiders called the Khans. They caught me "
"snooping around and their leader, Darion, had me locked up in here."
msgstr ""
"En bref, je m'appelle Chrissy et je viens du Squat. J'étais en pleine "
"exploration la semaine dernière lorsque j'ai trouvé cette entrée. J'ai pensé "
"qu'il s'agissait d'une mine abandonnée ou quelque chose dans le genre, alors "
"j'ai décidé d'aller voir. Hé bien, ce n'est pas une mine, mais l'entrée "
"secrète de l'Abri 15. Une bande de pillards appelés les Khans utilise l'abri "
"comme base. Ils m'ont capturée et leur chef, Darion, m'a enfermée ici."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:121
msgid "Okay. Me take you home."
msgstr "Ok. Moi ramener toi maison."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:122
msgid "All right, I'll take you home."
msgstr "Très bien, je vais te ramener chez toi."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:123
msgid ""
"Well, I'll be damned. Today must be my lucky day. To what do I owe the "
"pleasure of seeing you\n"
" again?"
msgstr ""
"Elle est bien bonne celle-là ! Ca doit être mon jour de chance. A quoi dois-"
"je le plaisir de te revoir ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:128
msgid "Please take me to my mother, Rebecca."
msgstr "S'il te plaît, parle à ma mère, Elisabeth."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:129
msgid ""
"My knight in shining armor returns. Well, it would shine if you'd clean it "
"every once in a\n"
" while. Oh, and you might want to consider bathing yourself as well. So, "
"what can I do for you?"
msgstr ""
"Mon chevalier à l'armure brillante est de retour. Eh bien, elle brillerait "
"si tu la nettoyais de temps en temps. Et tu pourrais aussi prendre une "
"douche... Bon, qu'est-ce que je peux faire pour toi ?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:130 dialog/ccatech.msg:105 dialog/cccomp2.msg:105
#: dialog/ccomp2.msg:105 dialog/cctech1.msg:105 dialog/cctech2.msg:105
msgid "Me just say hi. Me go now."
msgstr "Moi disais juste bonjour. Moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:131
msgid "Just thought I'd say hello. I'll be going now."
msgstr "Je voulais juste te dire bonjour. Je vais partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:132
msgid ""
"Hey, I know I have a smart mouth, but I want you to know that I'm very "
"grateful for you saving\n"
" my butt. Thanks very much!"
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, je sais que j'ai une grande gueule, mais je veux que tu saches que "
"je te suis très reconnaissante d'avoir sauvé ma carcasse. Merci beaucoup !"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:133 dialog/ccxarn.msg:176 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:194
#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:146
msgid "You welcome."
msgstr "Pas de quoi."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:134 dialog/dcpetey.msg:165 dialog/dcrebecc.msg:402
#: dialog/dcslave.msg:464 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:195 dialog/ocdalia.msg:148
#: dialog/vcconnar.msg:140
msgid "You're welcome."
msgstr "Pas d'quoi."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:135
msgid ""
"The people of the Squat are protecting these guys by helping them keep the "
"vault a secret, but they\n"
" don't know what's really going on here. Darion told us that the vault was "
"being repaired so we could have\n"
" a safe place to live with lots of food and water, but it's all a lie. I've "
"been in there and looked\n"
" around. The vault is dead, and the food and water machines don't work. Our "
"food and water's been coming\n"
" from the spoils\n"
" of raids against caravans."
msgstr ""
"Les gens du Squat protègent ces gars en les aidant à garder l'abri secret. "
"Ils ne savent pas vraiment ce qui se passe ici. Darion nous a dit que l'abri "
"était en cours de réparation et que nous pourrions y vivre en sécurité avec "
"ce qu'il nous faut d'eau et de nourriture, mais tout ça c'est un tissu de "
"mensonges. J'y étais et j'y ai jeté un petit coup d'oeil. L'abri est mort et "
"les systèmes d'eau et de nourriture ne fonctionnent pas. La nourriture et "
"l'eau que nous avons, viennent de ce qui reste des pillages menés contre les "
"caravanes."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:136
msgid ""
"Look, I've got to go home and warn everyone about what's really going on "
"here. We can't help these\n"
" monsters. Will you take me home?"
msgstr ""
"Je dois rentrer à la maison et prévenir tout le monde de ce qui se passe. "
"Nous ne pouvons plus continuer à aider ces monstres. Tu me ramèneras chez "
"moi ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:100
msgid "You see a young woman in tattered clothing."
msgstr "Tu vois une jeune femme vêtue de loques."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:101 dialog/ocdalia.msg:101
msgid "You see Dalia."
msgstr "Tu vois Dalia."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a young woman in tattered clothing. She seems very alert, and "
"watches her surroundings\n"
" carefully."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois une jeune femme vêtue de loques. Elle a l'air sur le qui-vive et "
"regarde avec attention autour d'elle."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:103 dialog/bcdalia.msg:140
msgid "Hi. I'm Dalia. What can I help you with?"
msgstr "Salut. Mon prénom est Dalia. Que puis-je faire pour toi ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:104
msgid "Nothing, just say hi."
msgstr "Rien, moi dire juste bonjour."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:105
msgid "Uh, who you?"
msgstr "Euh, qui toi ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:106 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:119
msgid "What you do here?"
msgstr "Quoi toi faire ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:107
msgid "You look like guard."
msgstr "On dirait toi garde."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:109 dialog/bcjones.msg:113 dialog/ocgordon.msg:176
#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:113
msgid "Just saying hello."
msgstr "Juste dire bonjour."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:111 dialog/dccustmr.msg:204 dialog/ecslaver.msg:108
#: dialog/mcjo.msg:153 dialog/ncmcgee.msg:395 dialog/rcascgrd.msg:187
msgid "What are you doing?"
msgstr "Que fais-tu ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:112
msgid "You look like you're guarding that trail."
msgstr "On dirait que tu gardes le passage."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:113 dialog/echermit.msg:114 dialog/hcghoul.msg:183
#: dialog/ncmyrgrd.msg:458 dialog/ocjul.msg:136 dialog/ocmatt.msg:126
msgid "I'll be going now."
msgstr "Je m'en vais alors."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:114
msgid "Well, hello to you. Now, I'm sorry, but you should go."
msgstr "Eh bien, bonjour. Désolée, mais il faudrait que tu partes."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:115 dialog/cccook.msg:105
msgid "Me want talk."
msgstr "Moi vouloir parler."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:116 dialog/scwesgrd.msg:105
msgid "Ok, me go."
msgstr "Ok, moi partir."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:117
msgid "I want to talk to you."
msgstr "J'aimerais te parler."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:119
msgid ""
"I said I'm Dalia. Look, I don't mean to be rude, but I don't want to talk to "
"anyone right now. Okay?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai dit que je m'appelais Dalia. Ecoute, je ne veux pas être impolie mais "
"je ne veux parler à personne. Compris ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:120 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:283 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:334
#: dialog/dcvicgrd.msg:333 dialog/dcvicgrd.msg:463 dialog/ocgordon.msg:141
msgid "Okay, bye."
msgstr "D'accord, salut."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:121
msgid "Just little more."
msgstr "Encore un peu."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:122
msgid "Then I'll leave."
msgstr "Ensuite, je partirai."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:123
msgid "I just want to ask you a question."
msgstr "Je veux juste te poser une question."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:124
msgid ""
"I like the fresh air, I like the trees, so I'm standing here. Do you have a "
"problem with that?"
msgstr ""
"J'aime l'air frais, j'aime les arbres. C'est pour ça que je reste ici. Ca te "
"pose un problème ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:125 dialog/bcjones.msg:108 dialog/ocdave.msg:139
#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:108
msgid "Sorry, me go."
msgstr "Pardon, moi partir."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:126
msgid "No, not problem. Me ask you something."
msgstr "Non, pas problème. Moi demander quelque chose à toi."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:127
msgid "I don't have a problem, but I am curious about something."
msgstr "Ca ne me pose pas de problème, mais quelque chose m'intrigue."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:128
msgid "Sorry, I'll be going then."
msgstr "Pardon, je vais donc m'en aller."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:129
msgid ""
"No, I'm not guarding the trail. There's nothing in this hole worth guarding. "
"I told you, I'm\n"
" enjoying the fresh air. Now go away."
msgstr ""
"Non, je ne garde pas le passage. Rien dans ce trou ne mérite d'être gardé. "
"Je t'ai dit que je profitais de l'air pur. Maintenant, va-t'en."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:130
msgid "You nice talk to. Me talk more."
msgstr "Moi aimer parler avec toi. Moi parler encore."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:131
msgid "Sorry me bother. Me go."
msgstr "Pardon, moi déranger toi. Moi partir."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:132
msgid "But we're having such a nice conversation, why stop?"
msgstr "Mais pourquoi partirais-je ? Notre conversation est si agréable..."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:133
msgid "I guess it's time to leave."
msgstr "Je crois qu'il est temps de partir."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:134
msgid ""
"Oh no, it's the pest again. Look, I have nothing to say to you. Go away!"
msgstr "Oh non, encore cette plaie. Ecoute, je n'ai rien à te dire. Va-t'en !"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:137
msgid "I have no quarrel with you. Leave me be."
msgstr "Je ne veux pas me disputer avec toi. Laisse-moi."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:141
msgid "Person go by here? In hurry?"
msgstr "Quelqu'un aller par là ? Très pressé ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:142 dialog/bcdalia.msg:143 dialog/ccquincy.msg:105
#: dialog/dcderek.msg:314 dialog/dctyler.msg:443 dialog/fcronmey.msg:110
#: dialog/hcliz.msg:112 dialog/hcmanson.msg:140 dialog/hcminers.msg:143
#: dialog/hcminers.msg:147 dialog/hcphil.msg:118 dialog/hcrsuper.msg:111
#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:124 dialog/hcrsuper.msg:129 dialog/hcsuper.msg:111
#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:124 dialog/hcsuper.msg:129 dialog/ncwriply.msg:434
#: dialog/nhmyron.msg:530 dialog/rccshtnd.msg:104 dialog/scelise.msg:123
#: dialog/scggcap.msg:111 dialog/scgunthr.msg:154
msgid "Nothing."
msgstr "Rien."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:144
msgid "Did you see someone go by here in a hurry?"
msgstr "As-tu vu quelqu'un passer par ici d'un pas pressé ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:145
msgid ""
"I see people go by here every day. I really don't pay much attention to them."
msgstr ""
"Je vois tous les jours des gens passer par ici. Je n'y prête pas vraiment "
"attention."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:146
msgid "Me not have time for you crap."
msgstr "Moi pas avoir temps pour tes trucs."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:148
msgid "Girl life at stake. Young girl. Someone daughter. You please help?"
msgstr ""
"Vie d'une fille en jeu. Jeune fille. Fille de quelqu'un. Toi aider moi ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:149
msgid "I don't have time for your crap."
msgstr "J'ai pas le temps de m'occuper de tes conneries."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:150
msgid "Fine, bye."
msgstr "Très bien, au revoir."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:151
msgid ""
"Look, a young girl's life is at stake here. The daughter of a worried "
"mother. Can you please\n"
" help me out?"
msgstr ""
"Ecoute, la vie d'une jeune fille est en jeu. La fille d'une mère inquiète. "
"Peux-tu m'aider ?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:152
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I don't give a radrat's ass... I'm sorry. I'm just a gun who was hired to "
"stand here and guard\n"
" this trail. Other than that, I don't know what's going on around here. I "
"had a daughter once, though,\n"
" and... yeah, some guy went by here. I let him through because he knew the "
"proper sign... just like the\n"
" sign you gave me. Go on. I'm outta here. "
msgstr ""
"J'en ai rien à foutre... Désolé. Je suis juste engagé pour rester ici et "
"garder ce passage. À part ça, je sais pas ce qui se passe dans le coin. "
"J'avais une fille, autrefois, et... ouais, un type est passé par ici. Je "
"l'ai laissé passer parce qu'il connaissait le code... comme celui que tu "
"m'as donné. Allez, vas-y. Je me tire d'ici. "

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:153
msgid "Thanks. Me no forget this, Dalia."
msgstr "Merci, moi pas oublier ça, Dalia."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:154
msgid "Thanks. I won't forget this, Dalia."
msgstr "Merci, je ne l'oublierai pas, Dalia."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:155 dialog/bcdalia.msg:157
msgid "Then go the hell away and leave me be!"
msgstr "Alors va au diable et lâche-moi !"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:156 dialog/bcdalia.msg:158 dialog/bcdarion.msg:104
#: dialog/bcjones.msg:167 dialog/bczeke.msg:109 dialog/bczeke.msg:111
#: dialog/bczeke.msg:149 dialog/bczeke.msg:153 dialog/bczeke.msg:155
#: dialog/bscomp2.msg:105 dialog/bscomp2.msg:107 dialog/bscomp3.msg:107
#: dialog/bscomp3.msg:109 dialog/bscomp3.msg:111 dialog/bscomp4.msg:107
#: dialog/bscomp4.msg:110 dialog/bscomp4.msg:113 dialog/bscomp5.msg:105
#: dialog/bspower.msg:110 dialog/ccncomp.msg:141 dialog/ccxarn.msg:141
#: dialog/ncstulit.msg:472 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:170 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:175
#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:228 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:230 dialog/oscomptr.msg:122
#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:123 dialog/oscomptr.msg:126 dialog/shtandi.msg:137
msgid "Done."
msgstr "Terminé."

#: dialog/bcdardog.msg:100
msgid "You see a dog."
msgstr "Tu vois un chien."

#: dialog/bcdardog.msg:101
msgid "You see Darion's dog."
msgstr "Tu vois le chien de Darion."

#: dialog/bcdardog.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see an animal with a lot of fur and four legs. If a dog could grin "
"evilly, you would swear\n"
" this one is doing it."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois un animal avec une épaisse fourrure et quatre pattes. Si les chiens "
"pouvaient ricaner, tu jurerais que c'est le cas de celui-là."

#: dialog/bcdargrd.msg:101
msgid "You see one of Darion's personal guards."
msgstr "Tu vois l'un des gardes personnels de Darion."

#: dialog/bcdargrd.msg:102
msgid ""
"He has armor, weapons, and a bad attitude - not the type of guy who likes "
"your company."
msgstr ""
"Il a une armure, des armes et un air mauvais. Ce n'est pas le genre de type "
"qui apprécie ta compagnie."

#: dialog/bcdarion.msg:100
msgid "You see an older man."
msgstr "Tu vois un vieil homme."

#: dialog/bcdarion.msg:101
msgid "You see Darion, leader of the New Khans."
msgstr "Tu vois Darion, le chef des nouveaux Khans."

#: dialog/bcdarion.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see an older man with thin, gray hair. He seems to be in good shape for "
"his age."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois un vieil homme aux cheveux fins et blancs. Il a l'air en forme pour "
"son âge."

#: dialog/bcdarion.msg:103
msgid ""
"So, here you are at last. The savior of the downtrodden, the righter of "
"wrongs, the icon of\n"
" hope for humanity. What a dumb-ass! Well, before you start any boring "
"speeches, I'd just like to say\n"
" that I'm not fucking interested. Let's just cut to the chase and get this "
"over with. Baddog, kill!"
msgstr ""
"Ah, te voilà enfin ! Le sauveur des opprimés, celui qui fait le bien, le "
"symbole de l'espoir de l'humanité. Quelle ordure ! Hé bien, avant que tu ne "
"te lances dans des discours ennuyeux, je tiens à te dire que tes conneries "
"ne m'intéressent pas. Allez, finissons-en. Sale chien, à mort !"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:100 dialog/bcgengrd.msg:101 dialog/bckarla.msg:100
#: dialog/bcphil.msg:100
msgid "You see a Khan raider."
msgstr "Tu vois un membre des Khans."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a tough looking person with armor, weapons, and a bad attitude. It "
"must be a Khan."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois une personne robuste dotée d'une armure, d'armes et d'un air "
"mauvais. Sûrement un Khan."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:103
msgid "What the... I don't think I know you. Who the hell are you?"
msgstr "Hé... Je ne crois pas qu'on se connaisse. Bon sang, mais qui es-tu ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:104
msgid "I got my ID right here! Let me show ya."
msgstr "J'ai mes papiers ! Laisse-moi te les montrer."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:105
msgid "The name's... umm... Pat, and I'm new here."
msgstr "Je m'appelle... Pat et ça fait pas longtemps que je suis ici."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:106
msgid "All right, wise-ass. Take your best shot."
msgstr "Très bien, l'intello, tu vas dérouiller."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:107
msgid ""
"Oh yeah. Sorry. Didn't recognize you at first. Go on about your business."
msgstr ""
"Oh ouais, pardon. J'avais pas reconnu que c'était toi. Tu peux continuer."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:108
msgid "Hey, I'm not as stupid as you look."
msgstr "Hé, j'suis pas aussi stupide que t'en as l'air."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:109
msgid "You're not dead yet? Shit."
msgstr "T'es encore en vie. Merde."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:110
msgid "Man, Darion doesn't pay me enough to stand around here and do nothing."
msgstr "Hé, Darion ne me paie pas assez pour rester ici à rien faire."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:111
msgid "Sometimes I sit and think about absolutely nothing."
msgstr "Parfois, je m'assois et je ne pense à rien."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:112
msgid "I generally don't care what anyone else thinks."
msgstr "En général, je ne me soucie pas de ce que les autres pensent."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:113
msgid "Ignorance is bliss... I think."
msgstr "L'ignorance est synonyme de félicité... Je pense."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:114
msgid "When's the next caravan passing through? I could use some action."
msgstr ""
"Quand est prévue la prochaine caravane ? Ca ferait du bien un peu d'action."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:115
msgid "I could use a break."
msgstr "Ca me ferait du bien de faire une pause."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:116
msgid "Damn, I still hurt from that bitch Chrissy kicking me."
msgstr ""
"Bon sang, j'ai toujours mal après le coup de pied que m'a donné cette salope "
"de Chrissy."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:117
msgid "Hey, we never get any new blood around here."
msgstr "Hé, on a jamais de sang neuf ici."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:118
msgid "So when are we going to get out of this stupid place?"
msgstr "Alors, quand est-ce qu'on quitte ce fichu endroit ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:119
msgid "I don't know about you, but I think this sucks."
msgstr ""
"J'sais pas ce que tu en dis, mais je trouve que c'est vraiment merdique."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:120
msgid "There ain't nothin' to kill around here."
msgstr "Y'a rien à tuer dans le coin."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:121
msgid "Where's the damn bathroom?"
msgstr "Où sont les chiottes ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:122
msgid ""
"Hey, we never get a break around here. Isn't there some law or something?"
msgstr "Hé, ça n'arrête jamais ici. N'y a-t-il pas une loi ou quelque chose ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:123
msgid "We should start up a government like in the old days."
msgstr "On devrait mettre en place un gouvernement, comme autrefois."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:124
msgid "Man, I wonder what it was like to be President back then?"
msgstr "J'me demande comment c'était d'être président à l'époque."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:125
msgid "I bet you could do anything you wanted if you were President."
msgstr "Je parie que tu pourrais faire ce que tu veux si t'étais président."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:126
msgid "I think my father would be proud of me today. Too bad I killed him."
msgstr ""
"Je pense que mon père serait fier de moi aujourd'hui. Dommage que je l'aie "
"tué..."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:127
msgid "I HATE RATS! HATE HATE HATE!"
msgstr "JE DETESTE LES RATS, JE LES DETESTE, JE LES DETESTE, JE LES DETESTE !"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:128
msgid "Hey, is that new armor you have on? How do you rate getting new armor?"
msgstr ""
"Hé, c'est une nouvelle armure que tu portes là ? Comment t'as fait pour "
"avoir une nouvelle armure ?!"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:129
msgid "This damn vault smells. Don't you hate it?"
msgstr "Ce foutu abri pue à mort. T'en as pas marre toi ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:130
msgid "Hey, who is it we're supposed to be keeping an eye open for?"
msgstr "Hé, qui doit-on surveiller de près ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:131
msgid "All I do is stand, stand, stand."
msgstr "Je ne fais qu'attendre, attendre, attendre."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:132
msgid ""
"I think we should just waste everyone upstairs and say to hell with this "
"place."
msgstr ""
"Je crois qu'on devrait liquider tout le monde là-haut et plus remettre les "
"pieds ici."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:133
msgid "What the hell is your problem with rats?"
msgstr "Bon sang, c'est quoi ton problème avec les rats ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:134
msgid "Have you ever pulled one of the legs off of a rat?"
msgstr "As-tu déjà arraché une patte à un rat ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:135
msgid "I like guns, yeah! GUNS I LIKE! GUNS: I REALLY, REALLY LIKE THEM!"
msgstr "J'aime les flingues, ouais ! J'AIME LES FLINGUES, JE LES ADORE !"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:136
msgid "Hey, is anyone listening to me?"
msgstr "Hé, est-ce que quelqu'un m'écoute ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:137
msgid "Oh well, I just talk to keep myself sane anyway."
msgstr "Oh, de toute façon, je parle juste pour ne pas perdre la tête."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:138
msgid "Hey, anyone remember what was in a Long Island Ice Tea?"
msgstr "Hé, quelqu'un sait-il ce qu'il y avait dans le thé de Long Island ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:139
msgid "Yeah, vodka, rum, tequila, triple sec, lime, and Nuka."
msgstr ""
"Ouais, de la vodka, du rhum, de la tequila, du triple-sec, du citron et du "
"Nuka-Cola."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:140
msgid "Hey, look -- the lights came on. What the..."
msgstr "Hé, regarde, les lumières s'allument. Hé..."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:141
msgid "Darion said he'd get the damn lights fixed. I guess he came through."
msgstr ""
"Darion a dit qu'il allait réparer ces foutues lumières. Il a réussi "
"visiblement."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:142
msgid "I don't think the generator just fixes itself, does it?"
msgstr "Je ne pense pas que le générateur se soit réparé tout seul, pas vrai ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:143
msgid ""
"That was kind of weird; now I can see. Jesus, this place looks like shit!"
msgstr ""
"C'était bizarre, maintenant je vois. Mon dieu, c'est endroit est vraiment "
"merdique !"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:144
msgid "Wow, it's bright in here. Where's the dimmer control?"
msgstr "Oh la la, c'est clair ici. Où est le variateur pour la lumière ?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:145 dialog/ccqmstr.msg:106 dialog/dcatkslv.msg:307
#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:200 dialog/mcprotec.msg:152 game/cmbatai2.msg:2347
#: game/cmbatai2.msg:2548 game/cmbatai2.msg:3148 game/cmbatai2.msg:12148
#: game/cmbatai2.msg:32646 game/cmbatai2.msg:36147 game/cmbatai2.msg:36248
#: game/cmbatai2.msg:36347 game/cmbatai2.msg:36448 game/cmbatai2.msg:36547
#: game/combatai.msg:2347 game/combatai.msg:2548 game/combatai.msg:3148
#: game/combatai.msg:12148 game/combatai.msg:32646 game/combatai.msg:36147
#: game/combatai.msg:36248 game/combatai.msg:36347 game/combatai.msg:36448
#: game/combatai.msg:36547 game/combatai.msg:36854
msgid "Die!"
msgstr "Crève !"

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:101
msgid "You see John, the squatter."
msgstr "Tu vois John, le squatteur."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:102
msgid "You see a middle-aged man wearing worn clothing."
msgstr "Tu vois un homme d'âge moyen portant des vêtements usés."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:103
msgid "Sorry, stranger, I don't have time to chat with you."
msgstr "Désolé mais j'ai pas le temps de discuter avec toi."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:104 dialog/scjohn.msg:104
msgid "Why no talk?"
msgstr "Pas parler ? Pourquoi ?"

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:105
msgid "Okay, wavy."
msgstr "Ok, salut."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:106 dialog/scjohn.msg:106
msgid "All right, see ya."
msgstr "Bon, alors à une prochaine."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:107 dialog/scjohn.msg:107
msgid "Wait a minute. Why won't you talk to me?"
msgstr "Attends une minute. Pourquoi ne veux-tu pas me parler ?"

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:108
msgid ""
"We're a very private community here, and we don't want any trouble or "
"interference from outside\n"
" sources. Please just leave us be."
msgstr ""
"Nous formons une communauté très fermée et nous ne voulons pas de problèmes "
"ou de contacts avec l'extérieur. Laisse-nous s'il te plaît."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:110 dialog/scjohn.msg:110
msgid "Hello... and good bye."
msgstr "Bonjour... Et au revoir."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:111
msgid ""
"Thank you for all that you've done. I apologize for the cold shoulder "
"earlier."
msgstr ""
"Merci pour tout ce que tu as fait. Excuse-moi d'avoir fait preuve de tant de "
"froideur."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:112
msgid "Screw you, asshole!"
msgstr "Va te faire voir, enflure !"

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:113
msgid "Damn, I hate it when that happens."
msgstr "Merde, je déteste quand ce genre de chose arrive."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:114
msgid "Take that! Yeah, that'll show ya."
msgstr "Prends ça ! Ouais, ça t'apprendra."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:100 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:100
msgid "You see a short man carrying a book in his hands."
msgstr "Tu vois un petit homme tenant un livre dans les mains."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:101
msgid "You see Doc Jones, the doctor."
msgstr "Tu vois le Dr Jones, le médecin."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:102
msgid "You see a short man with a book called \"So, You Want to be a Doctor.\""
msgstr ""
"Tu vois un petit homme tenant un livre intitulé « Alors, tu veux devenir "
"médecin ? »."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:103
msgid "Hello, I'm Doc Jones. You can call me Doc. What can I help you with?"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour, je suis le docteur Jones. Tu peux m'appeler Doc. Que puis-je faire "
"pour toi ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:104 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:104
msgid "Got owie. You fix?"
msgstr "Moi avoir bobos. Toi soigner ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:105 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:105
msgid "Feel icky. You fix?"
msgstr "Moi malade. Toi soigner ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:106 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:106
msgid "Me gimp, you fix?"
msgstr "Moi cassé, toi soigner ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:107 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:107
msgid "Got questions. Okay?"
msgstr "Avoir questions. D'accord ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:109 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:109
msgid "I'm injured. Can you help me?"
msgstr "Peux-tu soigner mes blessures ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:110 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:110
msgid "I feel ill. Can you help me?"
msgstr "Je suis malade, peux-tu m'aider ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:111 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:111
msgid "I'm crippled. Can you help me?"
msgstr "Je suis estropié, peux-tu m'aider ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:112 dialog/ccdoctor.msg:201 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:112
msgid "I wanted to ask you some questions."
msgstr "Je voulais te poser quelques questions."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:114
msgid ""
"Why, certainly. Here, we'll give you a shot of this -- this'll sting a bit --"
" now a bandage,\n"
" and there, you're all set."
msgstr ""
"Mais, certainement. Allez, on va te donner ça - ça va piquer un peu - "
"maintenant un bandage - voilà, tout ira bien."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:115 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:115
msgid "Me thank. Bye."
msgstr "Moi dire merci. Au revoir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:116 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:116
msgid "Thanks, Doc. I feel much better."
msgstr "Merci Doc. Je me sens beaucoup mieux."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:117
msgid ""
"Why, certainly. Here, you'll need to drink this -- all of it, I know it "
"tastes foul. Now, just\n"
" lie down on the bed over there, and I'll wake you in the morning."
msgstr ""
"Mais, certainement. Tiens, bois ça, entièrement... je sais, c'est infect. "
"Maintenant, allonge-toi sur le lit, je te réveillerai dans la matinée."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:118 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:118
msgid "Me feel good. Bye."
msgstr "Moi sentir bien. Au revoir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:119
msgid "Thanks Doc, that did the trick."
msgstr "Merci Doc, ça aura été efficace."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:120
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, but I don't have the proper facilities to perform surgery. I'd "
"suggest you go to one\n"
" of the bigger cities and see a surgeon. Try Vault City. It's north of here."
msgstr ""
"Je regrette mais je n'ai pas ce qu'il faut pour opérer. Je te conseille "
"d'aller dans une grande ville pour consulter un chirurgien. Essaie la Cité "
"de l'Abri, au Nord d'ici."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:121
msgid "Okay. Bye"
msgstr "D'accord. Au revoir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:122 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:122
msgid "All right. Thanks anyway."
msgstr "Très bien. Merci quand même."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:123 dialog/dccaesar.msg:182 dialog/dcmaggie.msg:173
#: dialog/dcrebecc.msg:241 dialog/dctubby.msg:171 dialog/kcjenny.msg:290
#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:114 dialog/ocgoris.msg:122 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:118
#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:123 dialog/qcmartin.msg:126 dialog/rcdrjohn.msg:154
msgid "What would you like to know?"
msgstr "Que veux-tu savoir ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:124
msgid "You work Darion?"
msgstr "Toi travailler Darion ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:125 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:125
msgid "You leave here when want?"
msgstr "Toi peux partir quand vouloir ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:126
msgid "What you know about Darion?"
msgstr "Quoi toi savoir sur Darion ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:127 dialog/ocdalia.msg:117 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:127
msgid "How you be here?"
msgstr "Comment toi arriver ici ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:128
msgid "You say Darion got doggie?"
msgstr "Toi dire que Darion avoir toutou ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:130 dialog/bczeke.msg:123
msgid "Do you work for Darion?"
msgstr "Travailles-tu pour Darion ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:131 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:130
msgid "Can you leave here if you want?"
msgstr "Es-tu libre de partir d'ici si tu le souhaites ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:132
msgid "What can you tell me about Darion?"
msgstr "Que peux-tu me dire sur Darion ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:133 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:132
msgid "How did you come to be here in the first place?"
msgstr "Comment es-tu arrivé ici ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:134
msgid "You mentioned Darion has a dog?"
msgstr "Tu as dit que Darion avait un chien ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:135 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:133
msgid "Thanks for the information. I'll be heading out now."
msgstr "Merci du renseignement. Je m'en vais maintenant."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:136
msgid ""
"Well, yes and no. It's not by choice. I'm a prisoner here. Darion is getting "
"up there in years\n"
" and he needs a dedicated physician to look after him. The Khans keep me "
"here for his needs. I'd rather\n"
" be here for the people in the town above. They have no medical help at all, "
"and there is a lot I can\n"
" do to aid them."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, oui et non. Ce n'est pas par choix. Je suis prisonnier ici. Darion "
"commence à se faire vieux et il a besoin d'un médecin pour s'occuper de lui "
"jour et nuit. C'est pour ça que les Khans m'ont gardé. Je préférerais "
"m'occuper des gens de la ville là-haut. Ils ne disposent d'aucune aide "
"médicale et je pourrais faire beaucoup pour eux."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:137 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:135
msgid "Okay. Need know more."
msgstr "Ok. Besoin savoir plus."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:139 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:137
msgid "That's very commendable of you."
msgstr "C'est vraiment louable de ta part."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:140 dialog/ocmatt.msg:153
msgid "I see. I'll be going now."
msgstr "Je vois. Je vais partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:141
msgid "They're squatters! Let 'em die. Get on with your life."
msgstr "Ce sont des squatteurs ! Laisse-les crever et vis ta vie !"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:142
msgid ""
"No, I'm pretty much trapped here. I can't even leave to refill my medical "
"supplies. Darion\n"
" sends out for anything I need."
msgstr ""
"Non, je suis prisonnier ici. Je ne peux même pas partir pour me ravitailler "
"en médicaments. Darion envoie des gars chercher tout ce dont j'ai besoin."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:143 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:141
msgid "Me got it. Go now."
msgstr "Moi comprendre. Partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:144 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:142
msgid "Need ask more."
msgstr "Besoin demander plus."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:145
msgid ""
"I guess you just aren't a trustworthy enough person to be allowed freedom."
msgstr ""
"Tu ne dois pas être une personne assez digne de confiance pour avoir le "
"droit de connaître la liberté."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:146
msgid "All right. I'm sorry, but I have to get going."
msgstr "Très bien. Je regrette mais je dois partir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:147 dialog/bcjones.msg:158
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that."
msgstr "Ca m'désole d'entendre ça."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:148
msgid ""
"Darion is a mental case, plain and simple. He's got more spooks in his head "
"than his dog has\n"
" fleas. As far as I can figure it, he was a member of another gang called "
"the Khans. They kidnapped\n"
" this girl, Tandi, and held her for ransom. Her father didn't take kindly to "
"that, and hired some merc\n"
" to get her back. Darion was the only one to come out alive."
msgstr ""
"Darion est un malade mental, c'est tout. Il a plus d'apparitions dans sa "
"tête que son chien n'a de puces. D'après ce que je sais, il faisait partie "
"d'un autre gang appelé les Khans. Ils ont enlevé une fille, Tandi, et ont "
"demandé une rançon. Son père ne l'a pas pris à la légère et a engagé des "
"mercenaires pour la retrouver. Darion a été le seul à s'en sortir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:149 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:149 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:147
msgid "Uh... what you said."
msgstr "Euh... Quoi toi dire ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:150 dialog/ocariel.msg:133 dialog/ocgordon.msg:134
#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:148
msgid "Got go now."
msgstr "Moi devoir partir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:151
msgid "Uh-huh. Well, I'll be leaving now."
msgstr "Euh. Eh bien, je vais y aller maintenant."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:152
msgid "Wow; I'm impressed with your knowledge."
msgstr "Oh là là, tes connaissances m'impressionnent beaucoup."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:153
msgid "Sounds like my kind of guy."
msgstr "J'aime ce genre de type."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:154
msgid ""
"I was kidnapped. I was traveling from Vault City to New Reno for a well-"
"deserved vacation. Went\n"
" to bed one night and woke up bound and gagged the next morning. A week or "
"so later, I was here. Been\n"
" here ever since."
msgstr ""
"On m'a enlevé alors que j'effectuais le trajet entre la Cité de l'Abri et "
"New Reno pour des vacances bien méritées. Un soir, j'suis allé me coucher et "
"le lendemain matin je me suis réveillé attaché et bâillonné. Environ une "
"semaine plus tard, j'débarquais ici et tu vois, j'suis toujours là."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:155 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:632 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:153
msgid "Ugh."
msgstr "Pouah !"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:156 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:154
msgid "Thanks. Me be leave now."
msgstr "Merci. Moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:157
msgid "The weak are often the prey of the strong."
msgstr "Les faibles sont souvent la proie des plus forts."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:159
msgid "Interesting, but I need to get going."
msgstr "Intéressant, mais je dois partir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:160
msgid ""
"Yeah, he's got a dog. Personally, I think it's the meanest, most vile "
"creature on the face of\n"
" the earth. It seems to love Darion, though, so I guess it can't be all that "
"bad."
msgstr ""
"Ouais, il a un chien. Personnellement, j'trouve que c'est la créature la "
"plus mauvaise et la plus vile de la terre. Mais bon apparemment il aime "
"Darion, alors il ne doit pas être si mauvais que ça."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:161 dialog/shtandi.msg:204
msgid "Me ask more."
msgstr "Moi demander plus."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:162
msgid "Uh, bye."
msgstr "Euh, au revoir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:163
msgid "I see. Well, thanks for the warning."
msgstr "Je vois. Eh bien, merci de me prévenir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:164
msgid "Ah. Well, I've got to go."
msgstr "Ah. Eh bien, je dois partir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:165 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:158
msgid "I'll not help someone like you. Go away."
msgstr "Je n'aiderai pas quelqu'un comme toi. Va-t'en."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:166
msgid "Okay, well, you take care, and come back if you need anything."
msgstr ""
"Ok, prends bien soin de toi et reviens si tu as besoin de quoi que ce soit."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:168
msgid ""
"Now he's paranoid. He believes that Tandi is out to get him. He's obsessed "
"with revenge, and he\n"
" wants Tandi dead. He's riddled with guilt 'cause he hid and lived, rather "
"than dying with his\n"
" gang... and the list goes on and on."
msgstr ""
"Il est devenu parano et il croit que Tandi est à sa recherche. La revanche "
"l'obsède et il veut la mort de Tandi. Il se sent coupable d'avoir survécu "
"alors que tous les membres de son gang sont morts... et ce n'est pas tout..."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:200
msgid "Darion is dead."
msgstr "Darion est mort."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:201
msgid "Dar-e-on dead."
msgstr "Dar-i-on mort."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:202
msgid "He is!? Oh, this is wonderful news."
msgstr "Vraiment !? Oh, c'est assurément une nouvelle merveilleuse."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:203 dialog/epac12.msg:250
msgid "What are you going to do now?"
msgstr "Que comptes-tu faire maintenant ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:204
msgid "What yoo do?"
msgstr "Toi quoi faire ?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:205
msgid ""
"Well, I see no reason to return to my old life. The town above us doesn't "
"have any medical assistance, so I think\n"
" I will go up and help them. Thank you again for freeing me."
msgstr ""
"Hé bien, rien ne m'oblige à retrouver mon ancienne vie. De plus, le village "
"au-dessus ne dispose d'aucune structure médicale, je pense donc remonter et "
"proposer mon aide. Merci encore de m'avoir libéré."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:206
msgid "Of course. See you later."
msgstr "Sans problème. A plus tard."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:210
msgid "I still need to pack a few things. I'll see you on the outside."
msgstr "J'ai deux-trois paquets à finir. Je te verrai à l'extérieur."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:220
msgid ""
"Hey there, good to see you again! Everyone here really appreciates what you "
"have done. I personally am glad\n"
" to be out of there. Working for Darion was a nightmare."
msgstr ""
"Hé ! Bonjour, c'est bon de te revoir ! Tout le monde a apprécié ton "
"intervention. Moi le premier, je suis content d'en être sorti. Travailler "
"pour Darion était un cauchemar."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:221
msgid "Glad I could help. So, tell me a little bit more about yourself."
msgstr "Heureux d'avoir rendu service. Alors, parle-moi un peu plus de toi."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:222
msgid "Alright, see you around."
msgstr "Génial, à bientôt."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:230
msgid ""
"Well you see, I'm originally from the New California Republic, but I "
"realized I had a gift for medical practices.\n"
" So I trained as much as I could under the NCR medical staff, and once I had "
"learned all I could, I decided to try and\n"
" learn more by making my way to Vault City. I was lucky enough to meet Dr. "
"Troy while he was tending an injured citizen\n"
" outside the vault, and long story short, he agreed to finalize my training "
"in Vault City. I had just finished my training\n"
" and was heading out when Darion captured me."
msgstr ""
"Hé bien, vois-tu, je suis originaire de la République de la Nouvelle "
"Californie, et j'ai vite réalisé que j'avais des dispositions particulières "
"pour la médecine. J'ai donc appris tout ce que je pouvais sous la direction "
"de l'équipe médicale de la RNC, puis j'ai décidé d'approfondir mes "
"connaissances en me rendant à la Cité de l'Abri. J'ai eu la chance de "
"rencontrer le Dr. Troy lors de mon voyage, alors qu'il tentait de soigner un "
"citoyen en dehors de l'Abri, et pour faire court, il fut d'accord pour "
"parfaire mon entraînement. Mon apprentissage se terminant, je décidais alors "
"de reprendre la route lorsque Darion me captura."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:231
msgid "That's terrible. Well, I hope everything works out for you now."
msgstr ""
"C'est terrible. Hé bien, j'espère que tout se passera bien pour toi à "
"l'avenir."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:240
msgid "I hope so too. I think I can put my medical skills to good use here."
msgstr ""
"Je l'espère également. Et je pense que mes compétences médicales seront "
"d'une certaine aide ici."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:250
msgid "Thanks again for everything."
msgstr "Merci encore pour tout."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:251
msgid "It feels good to be helping civilized people again."
msgstr "C'est toujours gratifiant d'aider des personnes civilisées."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:101
msgid "You see Karla, a Khan."
msgstr "Tu vois Karla, la Khan."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a tough-looking woman in metal armor. She would be pretty, if it "
"were not for the scars\n"
" that line her face."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois une femme robuste dotée d'une armure métallique. Elle serait très "
"mignonne sans toutes ces cicatrices sur son visage."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:103
msgid "Talk to Phil, shit head."
msgstr "Parle à Phil, tête de noeud."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:104
msgid "Talk to Phil, bitch."
msgstr "Parle à Phil, garce."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:106
msgid "That little bitch is dead."
msgstr "Cette petite garce est morte."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:101
msgid "You see Phil, a Khan guard."
msgstr "Tu vois Phil, un garde Khan."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:102
msgid "You see a tough-looking young man in metal armor. He is heavily armed."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois un jeune homme robuste doté d'une armure métallique. Il est très "
"lourdement armé."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:103
msgid ""
"I should shoot you dead, but I'm kind of curious about what you could "
"possibly have to say to\n"
" me."
msgstr ""
"Je devrais te tuer sur le champ, mais j'ai envie de savoir ce que tu peux "
"bien avoir à me dire."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:104
msgid "Me look for spy. Go this way."
msgstr "Moi chercher espion. Aller par là."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:105
msgid "Me look for missing girl. You know where find?"
msgstr "Moi chercher fille disparue. Toi savoir où trouver ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:106
msgid "Me come here accident. Go now."
msgstr "Moi venir ici par hasard. Partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:107
#, fuzzy
msgid "Screw you. Me shoot you dead."
msgstr "Va te faire. Moi tirer toi mort."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:108
msgid "Uh, we talk this out?"
msgstr "Euh, on met les choses au clair ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:109
msgid "I'm looking for an eavesdropper who came this way."
msgstr "Je cherche une oreille indiscrète qui a dû passer par ici."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:110
msgid "I'm looking for a missing girl. Seen her?"
msgstr "Je cherche une fille disparue. Tu l'aurais pas vue par hasard ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:111
msgid "Sorry, took the wrong trail by accident. Gotta go."
msgstr "Pardon. J'ai pris le mauvais chemin. Faut que j'y aille."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:112
#, fuzzy
msgid "Up yours and have a bullet breakfast, asshole."
msgstr "Va te faire foutre et avale-moi ça au petit-déj, connard."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:113
msgid "I think we can talk this out like two civilized beings."
msgstr ""
"Je pense que nous pouvons en parler sans s'énerver, comme deux personnes "
"civilisées."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:114
msgid "Ah, that would be me. Now that you've found me, what's next?"
msgstr "Ah, ce serait moi. Et maintenant, que va-t-il se passer ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:115
msgid "Why you spy Rebecca?"
msgstr "Pourquoi t'espionnes Elisabeth ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:116
msgid "Now me know not be shooting wrong person. Thanks!"
msgstr "Maintenant moi savoir quelle personne tuer. Merci !"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:117
msgid "Nothing, me go now."
msgstr "Rien, moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:118
msgid "Why are you spying on Rebecca?"
msgstr "Pourquoi espionnes-tu Elisabeth ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:119
msgid ""
"Just wanted to make sure I'm shooting the right person. Thanks, and have a "
"nice day!"
msgstr ""
"Je voulais juste m'assurer que j'tire sur la bonne personne. Merci et bonne "
"journée !"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:120
msgid "Hmm. Nothing, I guess I'll be going now."
msgstr "Hum. Rien, je pense que je vais y aller maintenant."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:121
msgid ""
"I can't believe that you think you can just waltz in here and get answers to "
"your questions!\n"
" Oh, what the hell, you're about to die anyway and I feel generous. We've "
"got her kid locked in the\n"
" back room and have been having some fun with her. That bitch, Rebecca, has "
"been trying to find her, so\n"
" we've been keeping an eye open to make sure she doesn't get too close."
msgstr ""
"Tu t'imagines que tu peux venir ici et qu'on va répondre à tes questions ! "
"C'est incroyable ça ! De toute façon, tu vas mourir... et je suis généreux. "
"On garde sa gamine prisonnière dans l'arrière-salle... on s'est bien amusés "
"avec elle... Cette conne d'Elisabeth a essayé de la retrouver, alors on doit "
"garder l'oeil pour ne pas qu'elle s'approche de trop."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:122 dialog/bcphil.msg:148
msgid "You sicky in head. Me fix by remove head."
msgstr "Toi malade dans ta tête ! Moi enlever ta tête pour soigner."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:123 dialog/bcphil.msg:149
msgid "What you mean have fun with girl?"
msgstr "Que veux-tu dire par s'amuser avec la fille ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:124
msgid "Oh, that explain. Me leave now."
msgstr "Oh, moi comprendre. Moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:125 dialog/bcphil.msg:151
msgid "You are one sick puppy. I think I'll put you to sleep now."
msgstr ""
"Espèce de sale mioche, je vais te mettre au lit pour de bon maintenant !"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:126 dialog/bcphil.msg:152
msgid "Fine, have fun and I'll be going now."
msgstr "Très bien. Amuse-toi bien, je m'en vais maintenant."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:127 dialog/bcphil.msg:153
msgid "Hand over the girl and we can all leave here alive."
msgstr "Rends la fille et on pourra tous sortir vivants d'ici."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:128
msgid "Think about it as you die, stupid."
msgstr "Penses-y au moment de mourir, imbécile."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:131
msgid "Why in the hell should I do that?"
msgstr "Mais bon sang, pourquoi je ferais ça ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:132
msgid "It's good for your eternal soul."
msgstr "C'est bon pour ton âme éternelle."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:133
msgid ""
"Because I'm the worst thing that you could ever fear happening to you. Hand "
"her over or feel\n"
" the pain."
msgstr ""
"Parce que je suis la pire chose qui pourrait t'arriver. Rends-la ou prépare-"
"toi à souffrir !"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:134
msgid ""
"Because if we fight, one of us will die. I don't want to die any more than "
"you do, so let's end\n"
" this peacefully. Okay?"
msgstr ""
"Parce que si on se bat, l'un de nous mourra. Je ne veux pas plus mourir que "
"toi, alors trouvons une issue pacifique. D'accord ?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:135
msgid "Screw that noise."
msgstr "Laisse tomber."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:138
msgid "That sounds like a challenge. I'll take it."
msgstr "Ca a tout l'air d'un défi. J'accepte."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:141
msgid ""
"Hmm... I... Yeah, Okay. Here's the key to her cell; she's in the back room "
"of the shack. Take her\n"
" and get out, but don't come back. If I see you again, we'll see who lives "
"and who dies."
msgstr ""
"Hm... Je... Ouais, Ok. Tiens, voilà la clé de sa cellule. Elle se trouve "
"dans la pièce au fond de la cabane. Prends-la et va-t'en, mais ne t'avise "
"pas de revenir. Si je te revois, l'un d'entre nous devra mourir !"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:142
msgid "Let's see who comes out of this alive."
msgstr "Voyons un peu qui de nous deux va s'en sortir vivant."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:143
msgid "Thanks, you did the right thing."
msgstr "Sage décision. Merci."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:144
msgid "The only way you're leaving here is feet first, in a box."
msgstr "Tu quitteras cet endroit les pieds devant, entre quatre planches."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:147
msgid ""
"You mean the one locked up in back that we've been having fun with? No, I "
"haven't seen her."
msgstr ""
"Tu veux parler de cette fille enfermée là-bas derrière avec qui on s'est "
"bien amusés ? Non, je ne l'ai pas vue."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:150
msgid "Oh. Me leave now."
msgstr "Oh. Moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:154
msgid "So, you've returned. Let's see who comes out on top."
msgstr "Alors, te revoilà. On va voir qui s'en sort le mieux."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:155
msgid "We killed that bitch Chrissy, and now it's your turn to die!"
msgstr "On a tué cette garce de Chrissy et maintenant c'est ton tour !"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:100
msgid "You see an older woman."
msgstr "Tu vois une vieille femme."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:101 dialog/dcrebecc.msg:101
msgid "You see Rebecca."
msgstr "Tu vois Elisabeth."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see an older woman. Although she appears to have lived a hard life, she "
"has not lost any of\n"
" her natural beauty."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois une vieille femme. Même si la vie semble ne pas l'avoir épargnée, "
"elle n'a rien perdu de sa beauté naturelle."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:103
msgid "Hi, I'm Rebecca. Can we talk privately, please?"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour, je m'appelle Elisabeth. Pouvons-nous parler en privé, s'il te plaît "
"?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:104
msgid "What talk about?"
msgstr "Parler de quoi ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:105 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:114
msgid "Why need talk private?"
msgstr "Pourquoi parler en privé ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:107
msgid "No. Me leave."
msgstr "Non. Moi partir."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:108 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:135
msgid "Sorry, not interested."
msgstr "Ca m'intéresse pas."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:109
msgid "What do you want to talk to me about?"
msgstr "De quoi veux-tu me parler ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:110
msgid "Sure, where can we go for privacy?"
msgstr "Très bien, où pouvons-nous aller pour parler en privé ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:111 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:117
msgid "Why the need for privacy?"
msgstr "Pourquoi en privé ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:112
msgid ""
"(whispering) My daughter is missing and I need help finding her. I can't "
"talk about it here,\n"
" though. Can we go somewhere private?"
msgstr ""
"(en chuchotant) Ma fille a disparu et j'ai besoin d'aide pour la retrouver. "
"Je ne peux pas en parler ici. Pouvons-nous aller ailleurs ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:115 dialog/fctnkbar.msg:106 dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:107
#: dialog/fctnkmer.msg:106
msgid "No, me go."
msgstr "Moi partir."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:116
msgid "All right, let's go."
msgstr "Très bien, allons-y."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:118
msgid "No thanks, I don't want to get involved."
msgstr "Non, je ne veux pas m'en mêler."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:119
msgid ""
"(whispering) You may think I'm crazy but I get the feeling I'm being watched "
"all the time. It's\n"
" rather disturbing, and I'm a bit on edge because of it."
msgstr ""
"(en chuchotant) Tu vas penser que je suis folle mais j'ai l'impression "
"d'être constamment sous surveillance. C'est inquiétant et ça me tape sur les "
"nerfs."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:120
msgid "Okay, we go private."
msgstr "Très bien, parlons en privé."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:121
msgid "No time for sicky in head."
msgstr "Pas le temps pour les fous."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:122
msgid "All right; where can we go to talk?"
msgstr "Très bien, où pouvons-nous aller ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:123
msgid "Sorry, I don't like the sound of this."
msgstr "Je regrette, mais ça ne me dit rien qui vaille."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:124
msgid "Thanks; we can go to my tent."
msgstr "Merci, nous pouvons aller dans ma tente."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:126
msgid "We should be able to talk here."
msgstr "On devrait pouvoir parler ici."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:127
msgid "Okay, what problem?"
msgstr "Ok, quoi problème ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:128
msgid "Me got questions first."
msgstr "Moi avoir questions d'abord."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:129
msgid "Okay, so what's so important?"
msgstr "Alors, qu'y a-t-il de si important ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:130
msgid "I have some questions for you, first."
msgstr "Je dois d'abord te poser quelques questions."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:131
msgid ""
"I have a daughter named Chrissy who's a bit of a tomboy. She likes to run "
"around, explore,\n"
" and pretty much stick her nose into things. Chrissy's a good kid, though. "
"She doesn't\n"
" cause trouble, she's always home on time and she's shown herself to be a "
"very responsible young lady.\n"
" I let her do as she pleases most of the time. Last week Chrissy didn't come "
"home. I've asked\n"
" around, and nobody's seen or heard from her. I tried to find her myself, "
"but Zeke, he's... sort of the\n"
" mayor here... stopped me. He said it wasn't safe for me to go out looking "
"on my own; he'd have some of\n"
" his men do it. They couldn't find her, either, and said that maybe the "
"slavers got her."
msgstr ""
"J'ai une fille nommée Chrissy qui est un peu garçon manqué. Elle aime courir "
"par monts et par vaux, explorer les environs et mettre le nez un peu "
"partout. Chrissy est une gamine adorable. Elle ne cause pas de problèmes, "
"elle rentre toujours à la maison à l'heure et c'est une jeune fille qui "
"s'est toujours montrée très responsable. C'est pour ça qu'en général, je la "
"laisse faire ce qu'elle veut. Mais, la semaine dernière, Chrissy n'est pas "
"rentrée. J'ai interrogé le voisinage, mais personne ne l'a vue, ni n'a "
"entendu parler d'elle. J'ai essayé de la retrouver par moi-même, mais "
"Zeke... - c'est un peu le maire ici -, m'en a empêchée. Il m'a dit que je ne "
"devais pas m'en occuper moi-même et il a demandé à certains de ses hommes de "
"s'en charger. Ils ne l'ont pas retrouvée et ils ont dit que les "
"esclavagistes l'avaient peut-être enlevée."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:132
msgid "No, not get involved."
msgstr "Non, moi pas me mêler de ça."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:133
msgid "Need think before decide."
msgstr "Moi réfléchir avant décider."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:134
msgid "Ok, me seem be hero type lately."
msgstr "Ok, moi être apparemment très héroïque ces temps-ci."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:137
msgid "All right, Rebecca. I'll try to help you."
msgstr "Très bien, Elisabeth. Je vais essayer de t'aider."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:138 dialog/tribec1.msg:364
msgid "If I help you, what's in it for me?"
msgstr "Quel intérêt aurais-je à t'aider ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:140 dialog/cccook.msg:115
msgid "What go on here?"
msgstr "Que se passe-t-il ici ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:141
msgid "Who boss?"
msgstr "Qui chef ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:142
msgid "Me try find Vault 13. You know where is?"
msgstr "Moi essayer trouver Abri 13. Toi savoir où c'est ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:143
msgid "Tell about vault."
msgstr "Parler de l'abri."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:144
msgid "Tell about Darion."
msgstr "Parler de Darion."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:145
msgid "Thanks. We talk you problem?"
msgstr "Merci. Nous parler de ton problème ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:146 dialog/cccook.msg:120 dialog/vcmacrae.msg:117
#: dialog/vcmacrae.msg:135
msgid "What's going on around here?"
msgstr "Que se passe-t-il ici ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:147
msgid "Who's in charge around here?"
msgstr "Qui c'est qui commande ici ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:148
msgid "I'm looking for Vault 13. Do you know anything about it?"
msgstr "Je cherche l'Abri 13. Peux-tu m'en parler ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:149
msgid "Tell me about the vault."
msgstr "Parle-moi de l'abri."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:150
msgid "So tell me about Darion."
msgstr "Alors, parle-moi de Darion."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:151
msgid "Thanks Rebecca. Let's talk about your problem now."
msgstr "Merci Elisabeth. Parlons de ton problème maintenant."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:152
msgid ""
"We call this place the 'Squat' because it was settled by the homeless of "
"many cities. It's not\n"
" much, but it's all we have. To the west is a city called the NCR. They've "
"known about us for quite some\n"
" time, and never offered us any kind of help or hindrance. Now, they are "
"suddenly claiming this area as their\n"
" ancestral home, and they want it back."
msgstr ""
"Nous appelons cet endroit le « Squat » parce qu'il a été créé par des sans "
"abris de différentes villes. C'est pas grand-chose, mais c'est tout ce que "
"nous avons. A l'Ouest, il y a une ville appelée RNC. Ils nous connaissent "
"depuis un moment et ils nous ont toujours ignorés. Et voilà que subitement, "
"ils décrètent que cette zone est leur foyer ancestral et qu'ils veulent la "
"récupérer."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:154
msgid "What here they want?"
msgstr "Que veulent-ils ici ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:156
msgid "What is here that they want so badly?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui pourrait les intéresser tant que ça ici ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:157
msgid ""
"Well... there is a vault here; I think it's number 15. They want to loot it "
"for any of the old\n"
" technology that may still be there."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien... Il y a un abri ici. Je pense qu'il s'agit du numéro 15. Ils "
"veulent le piller pour retrouver l'ancienne technologie qui pourrait y être "
"enfouie."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:158
msgid "Ah. Me understand."
msgstr "Ah. Moi comprendre."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:159
msgid ""
"I knew there had to be something here other than the waste-of-flesh "
"inhabitants."
msgstr "Je me disais bien qu'il devait y avoir autre chose pour les motiver."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:161
msgid ""
"That explains a lot. You've been very helpful. I need to ask some more "
"questions, though."
msgstr ""
"Ca explique beaucoup de choses. Merci pour ton aide. J'ai encore quelques "
"questions à te poser."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:162
msgid ""
"That would be Zeke. He runs everything up here. You can find him in the "
"building over there.\n"
" ::points north-east::"
msgstr ""
"Ce serait Zeke. Il dirige tout ici. Tu peux le trouver dans le bâtiment là-"
"bas. *désigne le Nord-Est*"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:163
msgid "Thanks. Ask more."
msgstr "Merci. Demander plus."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:164
msgid "Thank you. I need to ask you some more questions."
msgstr "Merci. Je dois encore te poser quelques questions."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:165
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, I have no idea. I would ask about it in NCR. They've taken a "
"great interest in\n"
" vaults lately."
msgstr ""
"Je regrette, je n'en ai aucune idée. Si j'étais toi, je me renseignerais en "
"RNC. Ils s'intéressent beaucoup aux abris ces temps-ci."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:166 dialog/ccxarn.msg:116
msgid "Okay, me do."
msgstr "Ok, moi faire ça."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:167
msgid "All right, I will."
msgstr "Très bien, je le ferai."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:168
msgid ""
"Well... we're not supposed to talk about it, but since I need your help... "
"The vault is being\n"
" repaired by Darion. He's our benefactor. When it's fully functional, we're "
"all supposed to move in\n"
" where we'll be safe from raiders, slavers, and such. So far he has the food "
"and water systems up, but\n"
" that's about it."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien... Nous ne sommes pas censés en parler, mais comme j'ai besoin de "
"ton aide... Darion répare l'abri. C'est notre bienfaiteur. Lorsqu'il sera "
"totalement réparé, nous nous y installerons pour échapper aux pillards, aux "
"esclavagistes et à tous les autres. Pour le moment, il a réparé les systèmes "
"d'eau et de nourriture, c'est tout ce que je peux te dire."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:169
msgid "Me see. Need know more."
msgstr "Moi comprendre. Besoin savoir plus."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:170
msgid "I need to know more."
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'en savoir plus."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:171
msgid ""
"There's not much to say, really. Darion keeps to himself and never leaves "
"the vault. If he has\n"
" anything to say, he says it through Zeke. I've only met him once, and he "
"seemed like a nice guy."
msgstr ""
"Il n'y a pas grand-chose à dire, en fait. Darion garde tout pour lui et ne "
"quitte jamais l'abri. S'il a quelque chose à dire, il nous le communique par "
"le biais de Zeke. Je ne l'ai rencontré qu'une fois et il a l'air d'un type "
"bien."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:173
msgid "Nice guys finish last. I wonder what he's up to?"
msgstr ""
"Les gentils finissent toujours derniers. Je me demande ce qu'il mijote ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:175
msgid "That's okay. You are very helpful."
msgstr "C'est bien, tu m'aides beaucoup."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:176
msgid "I have nothing to give you other than my undying gratitude."
msgstr "Je n'ai rien à t'offrir hormis mon éternelle gratitude."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:177
msgid "That's more than enough. I'll help you."
msgstr "C'est plus que suffisant. Je vais t'aider."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:178
msgid "It'll take more than that to buy my help."
msgstr "Mon aide va te coûter bien plus que ça."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:179
msgid "What the hell, I'll help you."
msgstr "Allez va, je vais t'aider."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:180
msgid ""
"Thank you so much. I'll never be able to repay you for this. I'll wait here "
"until you bring...\n"
" Hey, there was someone outside listening to us! I saw their shadow on the "
"tent wall. They just ran off\n"
" that way! ::points north-east:: They must have heard everything!"
msgstr ""
"Merci beaucoup. Je ne pourrai jamais te dédommager pour ça. Je t'attendrai "
"ici jusqu'à ce que tu apportes... Hé, il y avait des gens qui nous "
"écoutaient dehors ! J'ai vu des ombres sur la toile de la tente. (Désignant "
"le Nord-Est) Ils viennent de s'enfuir par là ! Ils ont dû tout entendre !"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:181
msgid "Me stop, no get away!"
msgstr "Moi arrêter, pas partir !"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:182
msgid "You no worry, me find girl."
msgstr "Toi pas souci, moi trouver fille."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:183 dialog/ccquincy.msg:130
msgid "Ooops."
msgstr "Ouups !"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:184
msgid "I'll try and stop them."
msgstr "Je vais essayer de les arrêter."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:185
msgid "They won't stop me from finding your daughter."
msgstr "Ils ne vont pas m'empêcher de retrouver ta fille."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:186
msgid "Oh well. Shit happens."
msgstr "Bah, tant pis. Ça arrive."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:187
msgid "Please, just go away."
msgstr "S'il te plaît, va-t'en."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:188
msgid "Have you thought things through?"
msgstr "T'as réfléchi à tout ça ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:189
msgid "Me ask questions."
msgstr "Moi poser question."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:190
msgid "No, still think."
msgstr "Non, moi réfléchir encore."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:191
msgid "No, I'm still considering everything."
msgstr "Non, j'y réfléchis encore."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:192
msgid "I want to ask you some questions."
msgstr "J'aimerais te poser quelques questions."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:193
msgid "Have you changed your mind? Will you help me?"
msgstr "As-tu changé d'avis ? Vas-tu m'aider ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:194
msgid "Sorry, no."
msgstr "Je regrette, mais c'est non."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:195
msgid "Me help."
msgstr "Moi aider."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:196
msgid "Yes, I'll help you."
msgstr "Oui, je vais t'aider."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:197
msgid ""
"You must be the person who saved my daughter. I can never repay you for your "
"kindness. Thank you.\n"
" Please wait here, I need to talk to Chrissy and then I'd like to talk to "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Tu dois être la personne qui a sauvé ma fille. Merci, je ne pourrai jamais "
"te dédommager pour ça ! Merci ! Je dois parler à Chrissy. S'il te plaît, "
"attends ici, je veux te parler après."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:198
msgid ""
"You saved my daughter. I can never repay you for your kindness. Thank you.\n"
" Please wait here, I need to talk to Chrissy and then I'd like to talk to "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Tu as sauvé ma fille. Je ne pourrai jamais te dédommager pour ça. Merci. Je "
"dois parler à Chrissy. S'il te plaît, attends ici, je veux te parler après."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:200
msgid ""
"My daughter has told me everything. I find it hard to believe that Darion is "
"such a monster\n"
" after all he's been doing for us. And to think, we've been helping him hide "
"his operations as a raider.\n"
" I can guarantee you we won't stand for it any longer. I've already talked "
"to Zeke, and he wants to see\n"
" you. You should go see him now."
msgstr ""
"Ma fille m'a tout dit. J'ai du mal à croire que Darion soit un tel monstre "
"après tout ce qu'il fait pour nous. Et quand je pense que nous l'avons aidé "
"à camoufler ses opérations de pillage. Je peux t'assurer que tout ceci est "
"définitivement terminé. J'ai déjà parlé à Zeke et il veut te voir. Tu "
"devrais aller lui parler tout de suite."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:201
msgid ""
"I find it hard to believe that Darion is such a monster after all he's been "
"doing for us. And to\n"
" think, we've been helping him hide his operations as a raider. I can "
"guarantee you we won't stand for\n"
" it any longer. I'll talk to Zeke and explain everything. I'm sure he'll "
"want to see you. You should go\n"
" talk to him later."
msgstr ""
"J'ai du mal à croire que Darion soit un tel monstre après tout ce qu'il a "
"fait pour nous. Et quand je pense que nous l'avons aidé à camoufler ses "
"opérations de pillage. Je peux t'assurer que tout ceci est définitivement "
"terminé. Je vais parler à Zeke et tout lui expliquer. A mon avis, il voudra "
"te voir. Tu devrais aller lui parler après."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:203
msgid "I hope you find Chrissy soon."
msgstr "J'espère que tu vas très vite trouver Chrissy."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:204
msgid "Me looking."
msgstr "Moi chercher."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:205
msgid "I'll continue to search for her."
msgstr "Je continuerai de la chercher."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:206
msgid "Thanks for everything you've done for me."
msgstr "Merci pour tout ce que tu as fait pour moi."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:207
msgid ""
"I can't explain why, but I don't believe the slavers took her. I've an "
"uneasy feeling that\n"
" something else is going on. And then there's this feeling that I'm being "
"followed. I've had it ever\n"
" since I talked to Zeke about Chrissy. I need someone to help me find my "
"daughter. Will you help me,\n"
" please?"
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas pourquoi, mais je ne crois pas que les esclavagistes l'aient "
"enlevée. Je pense qu'il se passe quelque chose d'autre. J'ai aussi "
"l'impression qu'on me suit depuis que j'ai parlé à Zeke au sujet de Chrissy. "
"J'ai besoin que quelqu'un m'aide à retrouver ma fille. Veux-tu bien m'aider "
"? S'il te plaît ?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:208
msgid ""
"They keep sending people here to try and talk us out of our home, but they "
"don't understand\n"
" that we have nowhere else to go. We don't have the skills necessary to "
"survive on our own if we leave\n"
" here."
msgstr ""
"Ils continuent à envoyer des gens ici pour essayer de négocier notre départ, "
"mais ils ne comprennent pas que nous n'avons nulle part ailleurs où aller. "
"Nous ne pourrons pas survivre si nous quittons cet endroit."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:209
msgid ""
"You know, it's kind of funny that they managed to get something that complex "
"fixed, but not the\n"
" lights. The damn place is lit by torches. Anyway, Darion doesn't want "
"anyone to know what's going on\n"
" with the vault. He's afraid that someone will take it all away from us if "
"they find out. So, we're told\n"
" to drive off anyone who shows up here -- especially the NCR."
msgstr ""
"Tu sais, c'est marrant qu'ils aient réussi à réparer un truc aussi complexe, "
"alors qu'ils n'ont pas réparé l'éclairage. Ce fichu endroit est éclairé par "
"des torches. De toute façon, Darion veut que personne ne sache ce qui se "
"passe dans l'abri. Il craint que quelqu'un nous le prenne si on découvrait "
"ce qui s'y passe. C'est pour ça que nous devons renvoyer toutes les "
"personnes qui se présentent ici. Notamment, les gens de la RNC."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:101
msgid "You see Roberta, a squatter."
msgstr "Voici Roberta, la squatteuse."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:102 dialog/bcsara.msg:102
msgid "You see a middle aged woman wearing worn clothing."
msgstr "Tu vois une femme d'âge moyen portant des vêtements usés."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:103
msgid "Oh, my. I'm sorry, but I have nothing to say to you. Please go away."
msgstr ""
"Ca par exemple ! Je regrette, j'ai rien à te dire. Je t'en prie, va-t'en."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:104
msgid "Please go away. I don't want to be bothered."
msgstr "Je t'en prie, va-t'en. Je ne veux pas qu'on me dérange."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:105
msgid "Thanks for helping out Rebecca. I was wrong about you."
msgstr "Merci d'avoir aidé Elisabeth. J'm'étais trompée sur ton compte."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:106 dialog/bcsara.msg:106
msgid "I'm no threat to you. Please don't kill me."
msgstr "Je ne te veux pas de mal. Je t'en prie, ne me tue pas."

#: dialog/bcsara.msg:101
msgid "You see Sara, a squatter."
msgstr "Tu vois Sara, la squatteuse."

#: dialog/bcsara.msg:103
msgid "Please don't bother me; I'm really busy right now."
msgstr "Laisse-moi tranquille, j'ai beaucoup à faire."

#: dialog/bcsara.msg:104
msgid "Please go away. There's nothing here for you."
msgstr "Je t'en prie, va-t'en. Il n'y a rien ici pour toi."

#: dialog/bcsara.msg:105
msgid ""
"Thanks for helping out Rebecca. It was a wonderful thing for you to do for a "
"stranger."
msgstr ""
"Merci d'avoir aidé Elisabeth. Tu as fait quelque chose de formidable pour "
"quelqu'un que tu ne connaissais pas."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:100
msgid "You see an older squatter."
msgstr "Tu vois un vieux squatteur."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:101
msgid "You see Zeke, a squatter."
msgstr "Tu vois Zeke, un squatteur."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:102
msgid "You see an older man with thinning, white hair."
msgstr "Tu vois un vieil homme aux cheveux fins et blancs."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:103
msgid ""
"My name's Zeke, stranger. I'm sorry, but I don't have time to talk to you -- "
"and I don't think\n"
" there's anything in this town for you, anyway. You should move on."
msgstr ""
"Je m'appelle Zeke. Je m'excuse, mais je n'ai pas le temps de te parler - et "
"je ne pense pas qu'il y ait quoi que ce soit dans cette ville pour toi. Tu "
"devrais t'en aller."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:104 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:752 dialog/gcbrain.msg:501
#: dialog/ncwriply.msg:631 dialog/ocariel.msg:141 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:234
#: dialog/ockerith.msg:124 dialog/vcgatgrd.msg:188
msgid "Uh, okay."
msgstr "Uh, Ok."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:106
msgid "All right, I'll leave."
msgstr "Très bien, je m'en vais."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:107
msgid "I just wanted to ask a couple of questions."
msgstr "Je voulais juste te poser quelques questions."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:108
msgid ""
"Well, I think you'll find that we're all out of answers here. Why don't you "
"come back when we\n"
" get a shipment in?"
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, je pense que tu vas te rendre compte qu'on a pas de réponses ici. "
"Pourquoi ne reviens-tu pas quand on aura reçu une nouvelle cargaison ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:110
msgid ""
"Hello, again. I still don't have any answers for you, stranger. Why don't "
"you take a hint and\n"
" get the duck out of fodge?"
msgstr ""
"Rebonjour. Je n'ai toujours pas de réponses pour toi. Tu ne comprends pas ou "
"quoi ? Pourquoi tu vas pas voir ailleurs si j'y suis ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:112
msgid ""
"Rebecca has told me what you did for her. I want to apologize for the "
"treatment you received\n"
" here. You certainly didn't deserve it. What can I help you with?"
msgstr ""
"Elisabeth m'a dit ce que tu avais fait pour elle. Je tiens à m'excuser pour "
"l'accueil que tu as reçu ici. Tu ne l'as certainement pas mérité. Que puis-"
"je faire pour toi ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:114
msgid "Nothing. Wavy."
msgstr "Rien. Salut."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:115
msgid "I've got some questions for you."
msgstr "J'ai quelques questions à te poser."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:116
msgid "Nothing for now, thanks."
msgstr "Rien pour le moment, merci."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:118
msgid "You work for Darion?"
msgstr "Toi travailler pour Darion ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:119
msgid "What you do about raiders?"
msgstr "Quoi toi faire contre pillards ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:120
msgid "Where vault door?"
msgstr "Où porte abri ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:121
msgid "Anything else go on here?"
msgstr "Se passer rien d'autre ici ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:122 dialog/ocsandy.msg:114
msgid "Me leave now."
msgstr "Moi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:124
msgid "What do you intend to do about the raiders?"
msgstr "Qu'as-tu l'intention de faire au sujet des pillards ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:125
msgid "Where is the vault entrance?"
msgstr "Où se trouve l'entrée de l'abri ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:126
msgid "Is there anything else going on around here?"
msgstr "Se passe-t-il autre chose dans le coin ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:127
msgid "I guess that's it. I'll be going now."
msgstr "Je pense que c'est tout. Je vais m'en aller maintenant."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:128
msgid ""
"Yes, I do. I act as the middle man between him and the people up here. I'm "
"not very happy about\n"
" the fact, now that I know what he's up to."
msgstr ""
"Oui. Je sers d'intermédiaire entre lui et la population d'ici. Ca ne me "
"réjouit guère, maintenant que je sais ce qu'il mijote."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:131
msgid ""
"Nothing. They have the guns, they control the water, and they control the "
"food. That means\n"
" they are in charge. Period. We have no skills and no means of support "
"without the backing of Darion.\n"
" How can we turn against him? We're at his mercy."
msgstr ""
"Rien. Ils ont les armes, ils contrôlent l'eau et la nourriture. Bref, ils "
"s'occupent de tout. Point. Sans Darion, on n'a ni les capacités, ni les "
"moyens de survivre. Comment pourrait-on se retourner contre lui ? On est à "
"sa merci."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:132
msgid "Hmm. Me think me understand."
msgstr "Hum. Moi croire comprendre."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:133
msgid "Hmm. I see."
msgstr "Hum. Je vois."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:134
msgid ""
"It's behind that door over there, but it's locked from the other side and "
"trapped, too. I don't have\n"
" any means of opening it... Wait a minute. I found this key card some time "
"ago, and I have no idea what\n"
" it is for. Rebecca says that you found some sort of door where they were "
"holding Chrissy. Maybe this\n"
" card will open it. Here, take it."
msgstr ""
"C'est derrière cette porte, là-bas, mais elle est piégée et fermée de "
"l'intérieur. Je n'ai aucun moyen de l'ouvrir... Attends une minute. J'ai "
"trouvé cette carte d'accès il y a quelque temps et je ne sais vraiment pas à "
"quoi elle sert. Elisabeth dit que tu as trouvé une sorte de porte derrière "
"laquelle ils détenaient Chrissy. Cette carte permet peut-être de l'ouvrir. "
"Tiens, prends-la."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:135 dialog/scwesgrd.msg:132
msgid "Me thank you."
msgstr "Moi dire merci toi."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:136
msgid "Thanks. I'll give it a try."
msgstr "Merci. Je vais essayer."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:137
msgid ""
"There's a city west of here called NCR. They claim Vault 15 is their "
"ancestral home and they want it\n"
" back. They've been sending people here trying to talk us into leaving but "
"we aren't going for it. This is the only home we know."
msgstr ""
"Ouais, il y a une ville à l'Ouest d'ici appelée RNC. Ils soutiennent que "
"l'abri 15 est leur foyer ancestral et ils veulent le récupérer. Ils ont "
"envoyé des gens ici pour essayer de négocier notre départ, mais ce n'est pas "
"facile. C'est le seul foyer que nous connaissons."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:138
msgid "You maybe make deal NCR?"
msgstr "Toi peut-être faire marché avec RNC ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:139
msgid "Would you consider making a deal with NCR?"
msgstr "Que dirais-tu de conclure un marché avec la RNC ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:140
msgid "That all depends. What did you have in mind?"
msgstr "Ca dépend. A quoi penses-tu ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:141
msgid ""
"Join NCR tribe. Learn from elders. Give NCR you permission enter vault. Both "
"happy."
msgstr ""
"Rejoindre tribu RNC. Apprendre des anciens. Donner RNC permission entrer "
"dans abri. Tout le monde content."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:142
msgid ""
"Join NCR, let them annex your territory, and give them access to the vault. "
"In return, they can teach you all the skills\n"
" you need to survive on your own and offer you their protection."
msgstr ""
"Rejoignez la RNC, laissez-les annexer votre territoire et donnez leur accès "
"à l'abri. En échange, ils peuvent vous enseigner tout ce que vous devez "
"savoir pour survivre et vous offrir leur protection."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:143
msgid ""
"Not bad... I like it. You've got yourself a deal if you can get NCR to agree "
"to it as well. But...\n"
" Look, someone has to take care of Darion and his cronies. It should be done "
"now before they realize what has happened\n"
" and have time to prepare for an attack. Why not get this over with and take "
"Darion out now?\n"
" You'll have the element of surprise on your side."
msgstr ""
"Pas mal... Ca me plaît. Ca marche, mais à une condition : tu dois réussir à "
"entrer en RNC. Mais... Ecoute, quelqu'un doit s'occuper de Darion et de ses "
"amis. Ca doit être fait avant qu'ils se rendent compte de ce que tu as fait "
"et qu'ils aient le temps de préparer une attaque. Pourquoi ne pas le faire "
"maintenant et évincer Darion ? Tu bénéficieras de l'effet de surprise."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:144
msgid "You right, me take care of."
msgstr "Toi avoir raison, moi m'occuper ça."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:145
msgid "Me not sure."
msgstr "Moi pas vraiment savoir."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:146
msgid "Yeah, I guess it has to be done."
msgstr "Ouais, je pense qu'il faut le faire."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:147 dialog/ccmaster.msg:150 dialog/gcharold.msg:289
#: dialog/ncorvill.msg:673 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:334 dialog/scofjack.msg:147
#: dialog/vclynett.msg:824
msgid "I don't know."
msgstr "Je n'sais pas."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:148
msgid "Excellent. Good luck to you, and thank you."
msgstr "Parfait. Bonne chance à toi et merci."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:150
msgid ""
"Well, take the time to think about it, but know this -- until Darion is out "
"of the picture, I\n"
" have no choice but to maintain things around here as they are. It's for the "
"safety of everyone\n"
" concerned. That means no deal and you are still persona non grata. "
"Understand?"
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, prends le temps d'y réfléchir, mais sache que tant que Darion sera "
"dans les parages, je n'ai pas d'autre choix que de veiller à ce que rien ne "
"change ici. C'est pour la sécurité de tous. Ce qui signifie aucun marché et "
"tu es toujours persona non grata. Compris ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:152
msgid ""
"Hi. I'm still waiting for a final resolution to our troubles. In other "
"words, kick Darion's ass!"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour. J'attends toujours que nos problèmes soient définitivement réglés. "
"En d'autres termes, j'attends de jeter Darion dehors à coups de pieds au cul "
"!"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:154
msgid ""
"You've done it, friend! We're no longer under Darion's yoke. Thank you! I'm "
"ready to accept your deal with NCR now.\n"
" Just have them send one of their reps by and I'll seal the deal."
msgstr ""
"Tu as réussi. Nous ne sommes plus commandés par Darion. Merci. Je suis prêt "
"à accepter ton pacte avec la RNC. Dis leur d'envoyer un de leurs "
"représentants et c'est un marché conclu."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:156
msgid "Thanks for the chance of a new life. We all owe you."
msgstr "Merci pour cette nouvelle vie ! Nous te sommes très reconnaissants."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:157
msgid "Just go away. I have nothing to say to you."
msgstr "Va-t'en. Je n'ai rien à te dire."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:158
msgid ""
"Wait, before you go... I found this key card some time ago, and I have no "
"idea what it's for.\n"
" Rebecca says that you found some sort of entrance where they were holding "
"Chrissy. Maybe this card will\n"
" open it. Here, take it."
msgstr ""
"Attends, avant que tu t'en ailles... J'ai trouvé cette carte d'accès il y a "
"quelque temps et je ne sais vraiment pas à quoi elle sert. Elisabeth dit que "
"tu as trouvé une sorte de porte derrière laquelle ils détenaient Chrissy. "
"Cette carte permet peut-être de l'ouvrir. Tiens, prends-la."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:160 dialog/ccatech.msg:109 dialog/cctech1.msg:109
#: dialog/cctech2.msg:109 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:110 dialog/mcbaltha.msg:163
#: dialog/ockerith.msg:104 dialog/rcmodjes.msg:129 dialog/vcandy.msg:204
msgid "What can I help you with?"
msgstr "En quoi puis-je t'être utile ?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:161
msgid ""
"Just the problems with the NCR, but I think the deal you offered will solve "
"that."
msgstr ""
"Juste les problèmes avec la RNC, mais je pense que le marché que tu as "
"offert va permettre d'y remédier."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:162
msgid "You've done it, friend! We're no longer under Darion's yoke. Thank you!"
msgstr "Tu as réussi ! Nous ne sommes plus sous le joug de Darion. Merci !"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:163
msgid ""
"Now that Darion's gone we don't have any way to get food. We will surely "
"perish! Thanks a lot."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que Darion est parti, nous n'avons plus de moyens d'obtenir de la "
"nourriture. Nous allons certainement mourir ! Vraiment merci."

