msgid "Uhhh...? Was this your first time?"
msgstr ""
"Tu sais, j'en ai eu des mauvaises baises, mais celle-là, c'était la pire de "
"toutes."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:125
msgid "He has cuts and bruises all over his body."
msgstr "Il a des coupures et des bleus sur tout le corps."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:150
msgid "You see a slender, primitive woman."
msgstr "Tu vois une femme mince à l'apparence primitive."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:175
msgid "She looks like she's been beaten."
msgstr "On dirait qu'elle a été battue."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:225
msgid "He doesn't look very healthy."
msgstr "Il n'a pas l'air en bonne santé."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:250
msgid "You see a woman captive."
msgstr "Tu vois une femme prisonnière."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:275
msgid "She's filthy and seems to be malnourished."
msgstr "Elle est sale et semble sous-alimentée."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:300
msgid "No hurt, please!"
msgstr "Pas faire mal, pitié."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:301
msgid "We leave now?"
msgstr "Nous partir maintenant ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:302
msgid "No talk. Must run."
msgstr "Pas parler. Courir."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:303
msgid "Thank you for help."
msgstr "Merci de ton aide."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:304
msgid "Thank you very much!"
msgstr "Merci beaucoup."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:305
msgid "You are a saint."
msgstr "Tu es un ange."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:306
msgid "What are you doing? We should go."
msgstr "Que fais-tu ? Il faut partir."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:307
msgid "Please help us escape."
msgstr "Aide-nous à filer d'ici."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:320 dialog/slvcc4.msg:320
msgid "You bad!"
msgstr "Toi méchant !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:321 dialog/slvcc4.msg:321
msgid "We no talk you."
msgstr "Nous pas parler toi."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:322 dialog/slvcc4.msg:322
msgid "We get free."
msgstr "Nous prendre liberté."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:323 dialog/slvcc4.msg:323
msgid "You no keep us."
msgstr "Toi pas garder nous."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:324 dialog/slvcc4.msg:324
msgid "You slaver!"
msgstr "Toi esclavagiste !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:325 dialog/slvcc4.msg:325
msgid "Why you slavers do this?"
msgstr "Pourquoi faites-vous ça, esclavagistes ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:326 dialog/slvcc4.msg:326
msgid "How could you work for these people?"
msgstr "Comment est-ce possible de travailler pour ces gens ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:327 dialog/dcslave.msg:357 dialog/slvcc4.msg:327
#: dialog/slvcc4.msg:357
msgid "We're not primitives!"
msgstr "On n'est pas des primitifs !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:328 dialog/slvcc4.msg:328
msgid "Don't you have any morals?"
msgstr "Vous n'avez donc aucune morale ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:329 dialog/dcslave.msg:355 dialog/slvcc4.msg:329
#: dialog/slvcc4.msg:355
msgid "What's going to happen to us?"
msgstr "Que va-t-il nous arriver ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:330 dialog/slvcc4.msg:330
msgid "What did we do wrong?"
msgstr "Qu'avons-nous fait de mal ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:331 dialog/slvcc4.msg:331
msgid "Leave us alone, slaver!"
msgstr "Laisse-nous tranquilles, esclavagiste !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:351 dialog/slvcc4.msg:351
msgid "You no slaver."
msgstr "Toi pas esclavagiste."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:352 dialog/slvcc4.msg:352
msgid "You no hurt?"
msgstr "Toi pas faire mal ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:353 dialog/slvcc4.msg:353
msgid "Friend?"
msgstr "Ami ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:354 dialog/slvcc4.msg:354
msgid "You help?"
msgstr "Toi aider ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:356 dialog/slvcc4.msg:356
msgid "Were you captured too?"
msgstr "Toi aussi, tu es en captivité ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:358 dialog/slvcc4.msg:358
msgid "Who do these people think they are?"
msgstr "Pour qui se prennent-ils ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:359 dialog/qcgenprs.msg:144 dialog/slvcc4.msg:359
msgid "Please help us!"
msgstr "Aide-nous, pas pitié !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:360 dialog/rccamint.msg:139 dialog/slvcc4.msg:360
msgid "Get me out of here."
msgstr "Toi pas garder nous ici !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:380
msgid "You no keep us here!"
msgstr "A l'aide !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:381
msgid "No right!"
msgstr "Pas juste !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:382
msgid "We no bad!"
msgstr "Nous pas méchants !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:383
msgid "We help?"
msgstr "Nous aider ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:384 dialog/qcgenprs.msg:124 dialog/qcgenprs.msg:151
msgid "Free us!"
msgstr "Libère-nous !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:385
msgid "No like."
msgstr "Pas aimer."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:386
msgid "Bad place."
msgstr "Endroit mauvais."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:387
msgid "Why bad people do this?"
msgstr "Méchants pourquoi faire ça ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:388
msgid "We no slave!"
msgstr "Nous pas esclaves !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:389
msgid "We do nothing wrong."
msgstr "Nous rien faire de mal."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:390
msgid "Let go!"
msgstr "Partir !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:391
msgid "What go on?"
msgstr "Quoi arriver ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:392
msgid "Big noise?"
msgstr "Grand bruit ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:393
msgid "Who fight?"
msgstr "Qui se battre ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:394
msgid "What happen?"
msgstr "Quoi se passer ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:395
msgid "Something happen?"
msgstr "Quelque chose se passer ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:396
msgid "Someone help us!"
msgstr "A l'aide !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:397
msgid "Hey! Can't anyone hear me?"
msgstr "Hé ! Est-ce que quelqu'un m'entend ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:398
msgid "This is wrong!"
msgstr "C'est pas bien !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:399
msgid "We didn't do anything!"
msgstr "On n'a rien fait !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:400
msgid "Let us out of here!"
msgstr "On veut sortir d'ici !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:401
msgid "Someone get us out!"
msgstr "Quelqu'un peut-il nous sortir d'ici ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:402
msgid "What did we do?"
msgstr "Qu'avons-nous fait ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:403
msgid "We didn't do anything."
msgstr "On n'a rien fait ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:404
msgid "We don't deserve this."
msgstr "On ne mérite pas ça."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:405
msgid "Those bastards!"
msgstr "Ces salauds !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:406 dialog/echomles.msg:104 dialog/qcgenprs.msg:150
msgid "Help us!"
msgstr "Aide-nous !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:407
msgid "Let me out!"
msgstr "Je veux sortir d'ici !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:408
msgid "We're not slaves!"
msgstr "Nous ne sommes pas des esclaves !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:409
msgid "We're not primitives! Let us out of here!"
msgstr "On n'est pas des primitifs ! Laissez-nous sortir !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:410
msgid "What's happening?"
msgstr "Que se passe-t-il ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:411
msgid "Is someone here to save us?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il quelqu'un pour nous sauver ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:412
msgid "Over here!"
msgstr "Par ici !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:413
msgid "Help! Don't leave us!"
msgstr "A l'aide ! Ne nous laisse pas !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:414
msgid "What was all that shooting?"
msgstr "C'était quoi, ces coups de feu ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:421 dialog/mcprotec.msg:153 dialog/wcdobbs.msg:104
msgid "Ug!"
msgstr "Argh !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:422
msgid "Don't stop!"
msgstr "Ne vous arrêtez pas !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:424
msgid "I'm heading as far away from this place as possible."
msgstr "Je m'en vais aussi loin que possible d'ici."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:425
msgid "Keep moving!"
msgstr "Ne vous arrêtez pas !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:426
msgid "Freedom! Freedom at last!"
msgstr "Libre ! Libre enfin !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:440
msgid "What loud gun noise? What you want?"
msgstr "Quoi gros bruit de revolver ? Quoi toi vouloir ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:441
msgid "Hey! What was all that gunfire? Are the slavers dead?"
msgstr "Hé ! C'était quoi ces coups de feu ? Les esclaves sont-ils morts ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:442
msgid "Hey! What was all that gunfire? What's going on?"
msgstr "Hé ! C'était quoi ces coups de feu ? Que se passe-t-il ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:443
msgid "That was Metzger's nightcap."
msgstr "C'était le dernier petit coup de Metzger avant le coucher."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:444
msgid "Oh, nothing. Just checking up on you. Bye."
msgstr "Oh, rien. Je venais voir comment tu allais. Salut."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:445
msgid "You are free to go. Metzger's dead."
msgstr "Tu es libre de partir. Metzger est mort."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:446
msgid "You free."
msgstr "Tu es libre."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:447
msgid " friend. He kill Mezgur. You go now."
msgstr " ami. Lui tuer Mezgur. Toi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:448
msgid " friend. She kill Mezgur. You go now."
msgstr " amie. Elle tuer Mezgur. Toi partir maintenant."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:460
msgid "He dead? Me thank you! We leave fast. Bye. You friend."
msgstr "Lui mort ? Moi merci toi ! Nous partir vite. Adieu. Toi et moi amis."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:461
msgid ""
"What? Metzger's dead? Oh, thank you so much! We better leave before others "
"show up. Thank you again."
msgstr ""
"Quoi ? Metzger est mort ? Oh, merci infiniment ! Oh, nous devons partir "
"avant que les autres arrivent. Merci encore."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:462
msgid "You're welcome. Now get out of here."
msgstr "Il n'y a pas de quoi. Maintenant, allez-vous-en."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:463 dialog/hcguard2.msg:251
msgid "Take care."
msgstr "Fais attention à toi."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:470
msgid ""
"Wait, one more thing. I'm looking for someone specific and I don't see her "
"here. Do you know where other slaves might be held?"
msgstr ""
"Attends, encore une chose. Je suis à la recherche de quelqu'un en "
"particulier et je ne la vois pas ici. Tu sais où les autres esclaves "
"pourraient être ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:471
msgid "Big camp near here. (The tribal points south west) Two moons from here."
msgstr ""
"Grand camp esclavagiste par là. [le tribal te montre la direction du Sud "
"Ouest] A deux lunes d'ici."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:472
msgid ""
"There's a camp about two days travel south west from here. That's where I "
"was first at."
msgstr ""
"Il y a un camp esclavagiste, à peu près 2 jours de voyage depuis ici vers le "
"Sud Ouest. C'est là que j'étais avant."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:473
msgid "Thank you. Now get out of here."
msgstr "Merci. Vous pouvez y aller maintenant."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:474
msgid "Thank you. Take care then."
msgstr "Merci. Prends soin de toi."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:475
msgid "Wait. I look for someone. Where more slaves?"
msgstr "Attends. Moi chercher quelqu'un. Où être autres esclaves ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:476
msgid "Thankee. Go now!"
msgstr "Merciieuh. Moi partir !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:480 dialog/ocdar.msg:104
msgid "What you want?"
msgstr "Quoi toi vouloir ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:482
msgid "Oh, nothing."
msgstr "Oh, rien."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:501
msgid "Never mind. You're free to go. Metzger's dead."
msgstr "Peu importe. Vous êtes libre de partir. Metzger est mort."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:510
msgid "Wha? Free? Bad men gone? We go now! Thank you. You friend! Bye!"
msgstr ""
"Quoi ? Libre ? Méchants partis ? Nous partir maintenant ! Merci ! Adieu !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:511
msgid ""
"Free? What? You killed them all? Thank you so much! We'd better leave while "
"we still can. Thank you again, you're a saint!"
msgstr ""
"Libre ? Quoi ? Tu les as tous tués ? Merci infiniment ! Nous devons partir "
"tant qu'il encore temps. Merci encore, tu es un ange !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:520
msgid "Damn you!"
msgstr "Malédiction !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:521
msgid "Rot in hell!"
msgstr "Va moisir en Enfer !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:522 dialog/ecscaven.msg:105
msgid "You'll pay for this."
msgstr "Tu paieras pour ton geste."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:523
msgid "Why are you even talking to me?"
msgstr "Comment oses-tu me parler ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:525 dialog/hcghoul.msg:172 dialog/kcardin.msg:950
msgid "I don't want to talk to you."
msgstr "Je ne vous adresserai pas la parole."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:526
msgid "How could you?!"
msgstr "Comment as-tu pu ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:527
msgid "I don't ever want to see you again."
msgstr "Je ne veux plus jamais te revoir !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:528
msgid "This isn't going to change things."
msgstr "Ca ne va rien changer."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:529
msgid "I'll be on my way, if you don't mind."
msgstr "Je pars, si personne n'y voit d'inconvénient."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:530
msgid "Please, just let me leave."
msgstr "Laisse-moi partir, s'il te plaît."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:531
msgid "Just let me be on my way."
msgstr "Laisse-moi partir !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:532
msgid "I still don't want to talk to you."
msgstr "Je veux toujours pas te parler."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:534
msgid "No chance."
msgstr "Aucune chance."

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:535
msgid "You think this makes things better?"
msgstr "Tu crois que ça va arranger les choses ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:600
msgid "We go?"
msgstr "Nous partir ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:601
msgid "No hurt?"
msgstr "Pas mal ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:602 dialog/hcprof.msg:127 dialog/hcprof.msg:130
msgid "Go!"
msgstr "Partir !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:603
msgid "Home!"
msgstr "A la maison !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:604
msgid "Free?"
msgstr "Libre ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:607
msgid "Did you say free?"
msgstr "Tu as dit libre ?"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:608 game/cmbatai2.msg:44904 game/combatai.msg:44904
msgid "I'm out of here!"
msgstr "Je m'en vais !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:609
msgid "Let's go!"
msgstr "Allons-y !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:610
msgid "Everyone! We're free!"
msgstr "Que tout le monde m'écoute ! Nous sommes libres !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:611
msgid "Yaaahooo!"
msgstr "Yaaahooo !"

#: dialog/dcslave.msg:700
msgid "You free the slaves from their pens."
msgstr "Tu as libéré les esclaves de leur enclos."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:150
msgid "He seems to be one of Metzger's personal guards."
msgstr "On dirait un des gardes personnels de Metzger."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:201 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:230 dialog/slvcc2.msg:201
#: dialog/slvcc5.msg:201
msgid "Now you die."
msgstr "Maintenant, crève."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:300
msgid "You want to see the boss? Go right in."
msgstr "Tu veux voir le patron ? Vas-y rentre."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:301
msgid "Metzger's the man to talk to, not me."
msgstr "C'est à Metzger qu'il faut parler, pas à moi."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:302 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:434 dialog/tribec6.msg:142
msgid "Go on in."
msgstr "Entre."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:303
msgid "Behave yourself."
msgstr "Conduis-toi bien."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:304
msgid "Metzger's right through this door."
msgstr "Tu trouveras Metzger derrière cette porte."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:305
msgid "Don't piss Metzger off."
msgstr "Ne fais pas chier Metzger."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:306
msgid "We're not selling if that's what you're here for."
msgstr "On ne vend rien, si c'est pour ça que t'es là."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:307
msgid "Still can't get used to a woman slaver."
msgstr "Je peux pas me faire à l'idée d'une femme esclavagiste."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:308 dialog/slvcc2.msg:304 dialog/slvcc5.msg:304
msgid "Nice to have you with us."
msgstr "Content de te compter parmi nous."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:309 dialog/slvcc2.msg:305 dialog/slvcc5.msg:305
msgid "Hi. How's it going?"
msgstr "Salut ! Comment ça va ?"

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:310 dialog/slvcc2.msg:306 dialog/slvcc5.msg:306
msgid "You club any slaves yet?"
msgstr "T'as déjà bastonné un esclave ?"

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:311 dialog/hcsteve.msg:150 dialog/slvcc2.msg:307
#: dialog/slvcc5.msg:307
msgid "Hi again."
msgstr "Rebonjour !"

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:312
msgid "Going to go on another run?"
msgstr "Tu pars à la chasse ?"

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:313 dialog/slvcc2.msg:309 dialog/slvcc5.msg:309
msgid "Things are pretty calm."
msgstr "C'est plutôt calme en ce moment."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:314 dialog/slvcc5.msg:310
msgid "When am I going to see some action?"
msgstr "Quand est-ce qu'il y aura de l'action ?"

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:315
msgid "I miss going on slave runs. Guarding sucks."
msgstr "La chasse aux esclaves me manque. La garde, c'est nul."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:316 dialog/slvcc2.msg:312 dialog/slvcc5.msg:312
msgid "Slave runs are a blast."
msgstr "La chasse aux esclaves, c'est top."

#: dialog/dcslaver.msg:317
msgid "Hey, man, glad to have you with us."
msgstr "Hé. Ca fait plaisir de t'avoir avec nous."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:150
msgid "He looks like he could easily take care of himself in a fight."
msgstr "Il a l'air très fort."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:200
msgid ""
"Ah, fresh meat.... Welcome ta the slaver's guild. The name's Aidan. Ya here "
"on\n"
" business? Ya better be."
msgstr ""
"Salut ! Bienvenue à la Guilde des Esclavagistes. Je m'appelle Aidan. T'es là "
"pour affaires ? T'as intérêt."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:201
msgid "What exactly does your guild do?"
msgstr "Que faites-vous au juste dans cette Guilde ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:202
msgid "Slaver's guild?"
msgstr "La Guilde des Esclavagistes ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:203
msgid "Save guld?"
msgstr "La Guide Eslagiste ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:204
msgid "Aruk kun sung?"
msgstr "Aruk Kum Sung ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:215
msgid ""
"[Aidan looks you up and down.] Well, ya look like you'd fit right in, buddy, "
"but you'll\n"
" have ta talk ta Metzger, of course. Right though that back door."
msgstr ""
"[Aidan te regarde de bas en haut] On dirait que tu pourrais faire l'affaire. "
"Mais tu dois parler à Metzger. Derrière la porte du fond."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:216
msgid ""
"[Aidan looks you up and down.] You don't look like ya could stomach it, pal, "
"but who\n"
" am I ta judge? Ya gotta talk ta Metzger. He's through the back door."
msgstr ""
"[Aidan te regarde de bas en haut] Ben, tu n'as pas tellement le genre, mais "
"si le boulot t'intéresse, va parler à Metzger. Son bureau est juste derrière "
"la porte du fond."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:217
msgid "I said ta talk ta Metzger. You fucking deaf and dumb or just dumb?"
msgstr ""
"Je t'ai dit d'aller parler à Metzger. T'es sourdingue ou t'es juste débile ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:219
msgid "Another question for you then."
msgstr "Alors, j'ai encore une question à te poser."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:220 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:385 dialog/ncpitbos.msg:290
#: dialog/ncpitbos.msg:351
msgid "Thanks, I will."
msgstr "Merci, j'y vais tout de suite."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:221 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:386
msgid "Medger"
msgstr "Medger"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:222 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:387
msgid "Uh... kay."
msgstr "Hum... D'accord."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:240
msgid ""
"Ya gotta be shittin' me! We capture and sell slaves. That's what yer here "
"for, right?\n"
" Ya looking for some action?"
msgstr ""
"Tu rigoles ou quoi ? On capture et on vend des esclaves ici, c'est pour ça "
"qu'on est là. Tu cherches un peu d'action ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:241
msgid ""
"Ya gotta be shittin' me! We capture and sell slaves. If ya ain't here for "
"that, whatta\n"
" want?"
msgstr ""
"Tu rigoles ou quoi ? On capture et on vend des esclaves ici, c'est pour ça "
"qu'on est là. Si c'est pas pour ça que t'es là, que veux-tu ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:242
msgid ""
"So, ya joined up. This should be interesting. If you like action, yer in the "
"right line of work. If ya don't, ya won't last long."
msgstr ""
"Bienvenue au club ! Si tu cherches de l'action, tu fais la queue dans la "
"bonne file. Sinon, tu feras pas long feu."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:243
msgid ""
"I never thought I would see that tat on a woman. It looks good though. "
"Surprised Metzger... fuck it. So what do ya need?"
msgstr ""
"Merde. J'aurais jamais cru voir un tatouage comme ça chez une femme. Mais ça "
"lui va bien... Il sera surpris, Metzger... Tant pis. Alors, que veux-tu ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:244
msgid "What do ya want? Ya lost or somethin'?"
msgstr "Que veux-tu ? Tu cherches ton chemin ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:245
msgid "Hello again. li'l lady. Whatcha need?"
msgstr "Eh bonjour, ma pt'ite. De quoi t'as besoin ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:247
msgid "I'm looking to join."
msgstr "J'aimerais devenir membre."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:248
msgid "Where do you get your slaves?"
msgstr "Où est-ce que vous trouvez les esclaves ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:249
msgid "I'd like to buy some slaves."
msgstr "J'aimerais acheter quelques esclaves."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:250
msgid "Do you know a man named Vic?"
msgstr "Tu connais un gars qui s'appelle Vic ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:251
msgid "I'm looking for a Merchant."
msgstr "Je cherche un marchand."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:252
msgid "You ever heard of Vault 13?"
msgstr "T'as déjà entendu parler de l'Abri 13 ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:254 dialog/scduppo.msg:105 dialog/scduppo.msg:122
msgid "Work."
msgstr "Travail."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:256
msgid "Kill."
msgstr "Tuer."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:270
msgid ""
"Ah, a bloodthirsty one. Well... Talk to the boss. We might have a place for "
"ya. Go through the back door."
msgstr ""
"Ah, on est sanguinaire, hein ? Bon, tu devrais parler au patron. On a peut-"
"être une place pour toi. Juste derrière la porte du fond."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:271
msgid ""
"Metzger's never had a bitch slaver, but if you're really that bloodthirsty, "
"check with him. He's right through that door."
msgstr ""
"Ben, heu... Metzger n'a jamais embauché de femme, mais si tu aimes vraiment "
"le sang, ça vaut la peine d'essayer. Il est juste derrière la porte du fond."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:272
msgid "Okke."
msgstr "D'ac."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:274
msgid "Krook"
msgstr "Grouic."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:280
msgid ""
"Talk ta Metzger about that. He doesn't normally sell to the public. Has his "
"hands full with... bigger customers."
msgstr ""
"Il faut voir avec le patron. D'habitude, Metzger ne traite pas avec les "
"particuliers. Il a assez à faire avec... de plus gros clients."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:282
msgid "Can I ask something else then?"
msgstr "Je peux te poser une autre question ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:284
msgid "What about Vic?"
msgstr "Et Vic ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:290
msgid "Ya don't say. Beat it!"
msgstr "Ouais c'est ça. Dégage !"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:291
msgid "Dumb bitch."
msgstr "Abruti."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:292
msgid "Oook?"
msgstr "Oook ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:300
msgid ""
"Not likely. That dumbass Vic pissed Metzger off about some radio or "
"something. I doubt that he'd sell'm. You'll have to talk ta him yourself."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas. Il a foutu Metzger en rogne à cause d'une radio. Je sais pas "
"s'il voudra le vendre. Il faut que tu lui en parles personnellement."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:301
msgid ""
"Well, I hear he finally fixed the radio. You should ask Metzger. He's not "
"much use now, not very good trade quality."
msgstr ""
"Ben, je sais qu'il a enfin réparé la radio. Tu devrais demander à Metzger. "
"Il n'a plus une grande valeur marchande maintenant."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:303
msgid "Where's Metzger at?"
msgstr "Où est Metzger ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:310
msgid "He's in the back room right through the door over there."
msgstr "Metzger est dans la pièce du fond, juste derrière cette porte."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:311
msgid "You playing with me? He's right back there. Just go through that door."
msgstr ""
"Tu te moques de moi ? Il est juste là derrière. Derrière la porte du fond."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:320
msgid ""
"Damn, you don't know Metzger? What're ya doin' in this town, if not ta see "
"him? He's the head of the Slaver's Guild."
msgstr ""
"Incroyable, tu connais pas Metzger. Que fais-tu en ville si c'est pas pour "
"le voir ? C'est le chef de la Guilde des Esclavagistes."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:321
msgid ""
"How many times do I have to tell ya? He's the slave master. He runs things "
"in this town."
msgstr ""
"Faut te le dire combien de fois ? C'est le Maître des Esclavagistes. Dans "
"cette ville, c'est lui le patron."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:330
msgid ""
"I ain't talkin' about that. Metzger'll string me up. Plus, we wouldn't want "
"any outside competition."
msgstr ""
"Je regrette, je peux pas en parler. Metzger me ferait pendre. On veut pas de "
"concurrence."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:331
msgid "I already said. I ain't gonna talk about that."
msgstr "Je te l'ai dit. Je peux pas en parler."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:332
msgid "Tell me before I blow a hole through your head."
msgstr "Réponds-moi sinon je fais un trou dans ta petite tête."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:333
msgid "I understand. Another question?"
msgstr "Je vois. Une autre question ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:340
msgid ""
"Listen here, ya li'le shit head, don't you dare threaten me or anyone else "
"in our guild, or you're dead. Get that? Dead."
msgstr ""
"Ecoute, petite cervelle... Si tu me menaces encore une fois, moi ou "
"quiconque dans cette Guilde, t'es un être mort. Pigé ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:341
msgid ""
"Listen here, ya li'l cunt. Don't you dare threaten me or anyone else in our "
"guild, or your dead. Get that? Dead."
msgstr ""
"Ecoute, petite pouf. Si tu me menaces encore une fois, moi ou quiconque dans "
"cette Guilde, t'es morte. Pigé ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:342
msgid "Now, young Jet eye, you will die."
msgstr "Maintenant, fini de bluffer, tu vas mourir."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:344
msgid "Sorry, please don't hurt me."
msgstr "Pardon. Ne me fais pas de mal."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:345
msgid "Yeah, whatever. I'll let you live this time."
msgstr "Ouais, c'est bon. Je te laisse la vie, pour cette fois."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:350
msgid ""
"Oh, really? Maybe I should just blow a hole through your head right here 'n "
"now. What do you think, hot shot?"
msgstr ""
"Ah bon ? Je ferais peut-être mieux de t'éclater la cervelle tout de suite. "
"Qu'en penses-tu ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:351
msgid "Take your best shot."
msgstr "Vise bien."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:352
msgid "Don't make me laugh."
msgstr "Ne me fais pas rire."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:353
msgid "I was just joking, man."
msgstr "Je plaisantais, c'est tout."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:354
msgid "I'm sorry. I was just trying to impress you."
msgstr "Pardon. J'essayais simplement de t'impressionner."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:360
msgid "Run along, before I change m'mind."
msgstr "Barre-toi d'ici vite fait avant que je change d'avis !"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:370
msgid ""
"What? Oh, you must be looking for Mom's. You're one building off. She's in "
"the building directly south. S-o-u-t-h. That way. [Aidan points out the "
"door.]"
msgstr ""
"Quoi ? Ah, tu cherches certainement La Mamma. C'est à un bâtiment d'ici. "
"C'est le bâtiment tout au Sud. Au S.U.D. Par là-bas. [Adrian t'indique la "
"porte]"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:371
msgid "Huh? Uh... Oh."
msgstr "Hein ? Heu... Ah !"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:380
msgid ""
"Ya look like ya might fit in, but Metzger's never hired a woman. Not sure "
"why, but I doubt he's gonna start now."
msgstr ""
"Tu pourrais faire l'affaire, on dirait. Mais Metzger n'a jamais embauché de "
"femme. Je sais pas pourquoi, mais à mon avis, c'est pas près de changer."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:381
msgid ""
"Ya don't look the type. Hell, Metzger's never hired a woman before. Not sure "
"why, but I doubt he's starting now."
msgstr ""
"T'as pas vraiment le physique de l'emploi. En plus Metzger n'a jamais "
"embauché de femme. Je sais pas pourquoi, mais à mon avis, c'est pas près de "
"changer."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:382
msgid "I said ta talk ta Metzger."
msgstr "Je t'ai dit d'aller parler à Metzger."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:384 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:401
msgid "Another question."
msgstr "Une autre question."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:400
msgid ""
"Nope, but I'd check with the boss. He's probably been all over the fuckin' "
"place."
msgstr ""
"Non, mais je verrai avec le patron. Il a pas mal bourlingué et il est allé "
"partout."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:410
msgid ""
"Merchant? Oh, you must mean Vic, that guy that sells the old Vault stuff. "
"He's fucked. Metzger pretty pissed with'm."
msgstr ""
"Un marchand ? Ah, tu veux parler de Vic, ce gars qui vend des vieux trucs de "
"l'Abri... Metzger en a ras-le-bol de lui."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:411
msgid ""
"Yeah, Vic... that Merchant guy, right? The one that sells the old Vault "
"stuff. He's fucked. Metzger pretty pissed with'm."
msgstr ""
"Ouais, Vic... le marchand, hein ? Celui qui vend des vieux trucs de l'Abri. "
"Metzger en a ras-le-bol de lui."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:412
msgid "How many times you gonna ask me that? Metzger's got'm."
msgstr "Tu vas me demander ça combien de fois ? C'est Metzger qui le garde. "

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:415
msgid "Is he for sale?"
msgstr "Il est à vendre ? "

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:430
msgid "Hey, boys, look who's back."
msgstr "Hé, les gars ! Visez un peu qui est de retour !"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:431
msgid "Run, it's a slaver! Ah, I crack m'self up."
msgstr "Sauve qui peut, c'est un esclavagiste ! Oh, j'l'adore celle-là."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:432
msgid "Back for some action?"
msgstr "Tu veux un peu d'action."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:433
msgid "You know the way."
msgstr "Tu connais le chemin."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:435
msgid "He's wait'n for ya."
msgstr "Il t'attend."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:437
msgid "I know that ugly face."
msgstr "Je connais cette sale tronche."

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:438
msgid "How's it goin'?"
msgstr "Hé, comment ça va ?"

#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:439
msgid "Yer back. Ya gonna join up?"
msgstr "Tu es de retour. Tu te joins à nous ?"

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:100
msgid "You see a big, primitive looking man."
msgstr "Tu vois un homme grand à l'air primitif."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:120
msgid "You see a strange looking man."
msgstr "Tu vois un homme étrange."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:121
msgid "He seems to be awfully thin."
msgstr "Il est horriblement maigre."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:130
msgid "You see a ragged looking man."
msgstr "Tu vois un homme en haillons."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:141
msgid "He moves with suggesting speed."
msgstr "Ses mouvements témoignent d'une certaine rapidité."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:160
msgid "You see a rather large woman."
msgstr "Tu vois une femme plutôt large."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:201
msgid "Where you at?"
msgstr "Où en es-tu ?"

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:202
msgid "I'm gunna hurt you."
msgstr "Je vais te faire mal."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:210
msgid "I'm going to get your for this!"
msgstr "Tu vas me le payer !"

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:235
msgid "You're slavers aren't you? Oh, god."
msgstr "Oh, mon Dieu, des esclavagistes !"

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:261
msgid "Get ready; I think they're close now."
msgstr "Soyez prêts, je pense qu'ils sont proches maintenant."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:272
msgid "Why they want hurt."
msgstr "Pourquoi eux vouloir mal."

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:315
msgid "No do that!"
msgstr "Pas faire ça !"

#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:323
msgid "Help someone! Please!"
msgstr "De l'aide quelqu'un ! Pitié !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:100
msgid "You see a greasy old coot."
msgstr "Tu vois un vieux type graisseux."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:150
msgid "You see Smitty the mechanic and junkyard owner."
msgstr "Tu vois Smitty, le mécano et le propriétaire du dépotoir."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:151
msgid "You see a greasy old coot with dirty work-clothes on."
msgstr "Tu vois un vieux type graisseux vêtu de vêtements de travail crados."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:200
msgid "You varmint! Git outta here before I hafta learn ya!"
msgstr "Dégage de là ou je vais t'apprendre, moi !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:201
msgid "Git outta my place!"
msgstr "Sors de chez moi !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:202
msgid "Git off my land!"
msgstr "Sors de mon terrain !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:203
msgid "Dang varmint, git outta here."
msgstr "Saloperie, barre-toi de là !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:204
msgid "Go the hell away from me."
msgstr "Ne t'approche pas de moi !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:220
msgid "Hey, git off my land."
msgstr "Hé ! Fous le camp de mon terrain !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:221
msgid "You there, dumbass, git outta here."
msgstr "Eh, toi, l'andouille, dégage d'ici !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:222
msgid "Git, go on, git!"
msgstr "Allez, allez, casse-toi !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:223
msgid "I ain't got time for your type."
msgstr "J'ai pas de temps à perdre avec les spécimens dans ton genre !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:224
msgid "Sorry, I guess I don't speak idjit."
msgstr "Dommage, je parle pas l'imbécile."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:240
msgid "Hello there, young feller. What can old Smitty do ya for?"
msgstr "Bonjour, jeune homme. Que peut faire le vieux Smitty pour toi ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:241
msgid "Hello there, cute-stuff. What can old Smitty do ya for?"
msgstr "Bonjour ma belle. Que peut faire le vieux Smitty pour toi ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:242
msgid "Jumpin' jiminy, what can I do for ya now?"
msgstr "Smitty Les Bons Tuyaux, à votre service !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:243
msgid ""
"Hey there, I really enjoyed my meal from Mom's. Thanks. Now what can old "
"Smitty do for ya?"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour ! J'ai vraiment apprécié le repas de La Mamma. Merci. Que puis-je "
"faire pour toi ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:244
msgid "I was just wondering what you do here?"
msgstr "Je voulais simplement savoir ce que tu faisais ici."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:245
msgid "Say, old timer, I have this thingy here that I picked up in Gecko..."
msgstr "Dis donc mon vieux, j'ai ramassé ce truc à Gecko... "

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:246
msgid "Hey Smitty, I was wondering about that car you had for sale."
msgstr "Hé ! Smitty, qu'est devenue la voiture que tu vendais ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:247
msgid "I brought your meal from Mom's."
msgstr "Je t'ai apporté un repas de chez La Mamma."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:248
msgid "Say, old timer, I have this thingy here that I picked up in Klamath..."
msgstr "Dis donc mon vieux, j'ai ramassé ce truc à Klamath..."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:249
msgid "I was just looking around a bit. See you later, Smitty."
msgstr "Je jetais seulement un coup d'oeil. A plus tard, Smitty."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:260 dialog/dcsmitty.msg:280
msgid "Let old Smitty here take a look at it."
msgstr "Laisse donc Smitty regarder ça."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:261 dialog/dcsmitty.msg:281
msgid "Sure, here it is."
msgstr "Bien sûr. Voilà."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:262 dialog/dcsmitty.msg:282
msgid "On second thought, let me ask you about something else."
msgstr "Réflexion faite, laisse-moi te poser une autre question."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:263 dialog/dcsmitty.msg:283
msgid "Maybe another time. Goodbye, Smitty."
msgstr "Une autre fois, peut-être. Au revoir, Smitty."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:300
msgid ""
"Well now, that looks to me like it's an old fuel cell controller. Hmm, I bet "
"if I used that with the old Highwayman I could get her purring like a kitten."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, à mon avis, ça ressemble à un vieux contrôleur de transmission. "
"Hum, je parie que si je l'utilisais avec la vieille Highwayman, je la ferais "
"ronronner comme un chaton."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:310
msgid ""
"Hmm, that looks jist like a fuel cell regulator. If I had a car that ran, "
"it'd sure improve the mileage on it."
msgstr ""
"Hum, on dirait un régulateur de carburant. Si j'avais une voiture en état de "
"marche, je pourrais améliorer sa consommation avec ça."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:320
msgid ""
"That was mighty darn kind of you. Thanks mucho, compadre. Here's a little "
"something for your trouble. It'll come in handy 'round these parts. (He "
"hands you a stimpak.)"
msgstr ""
"C'était vraiment super sympa de ta part. Merci mucho. Voilà un petit quelque "
"chose pour le dérangement. Ca te rendra service par ici. (Il te tend un "
"Stimpak.)"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:321
msgid "Thanks, Smitty. No problem. See you around."
msgstr "Merci Smitty. Pas de problème. A un de ces jours !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:322
msgid ""
"Well, uhhh... Thanks, but I already headed over to Mom's and got some eats "
"myself, so I won't be needin' that anymore."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, heu... Merci, mais j'ai déjà fait un tour chez La Mamma et j'ai "
"déjà mangé. Je ne veux plus rien."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:323
msgid ""
"Oops, I'm not the usual delivery person. He called in sick today. Can I get "
"some experience points anyway?"
msgstr ""
"Oh, d'habitude, il y a un autre livreur, mais aujourd'hui il est malade. "
"Puis-je avoir des points d'expérience quand même ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:324
msgid ""
"OK, sorry about the mix-up. I hope Mom doesn't fire me! I really need this "
"job."
msgstr ""
"D'accord. Pardon pour la confusion. J'espère que la Mamma ne me mettra pas à "
"la porte ! J'ai vraiment besoin de ce boulot."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:325
msgid ""
"You know we're not doing the free meal after 24 hours thing anymore, right?"
msgstr "On ne fait plus l'offre de repas gratuit après 24 heures tu sais."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:326
msgid "Well, maybe I'll just eat it myself then."
msgstr "Bon, alors je le mangerai tout seul."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:327
msgid "Mom's not gonna be too happy with this."
msgstr "La Mamma ne sera pas très contente."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:330
msgid ""
"Well, you see, I've got this car, a Chrysalis Motors Highwayman. She's a "
"beaut, too. They used to say \"Nothing can stop a Highwayman.\" Built tough, "
"that's what they were."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois cette Chrysalis Motors Highwayman, elle est à moi. C'est une vraie "
"beauté. \"Rien n'arrête une Highwayman !\" disait la pub. Construite pour "
"durer."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:331
msgid "Yeah, so what's that got to do with me?"
msgstr "Ouais, quel rapport avec moi ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:340
msgid ""
"Well, you see, I thought I needed a battery for the thing but all I really "
"need is a fuel cell controller. Them things was always going bad on 'em."
msgstr ""
"Tu vois, je croyais avoir besoin d'une batterie, mais il me faut un "
"contrôleur de transmission en fait. C'est toujours cette pièce qui casse sur "
"ces machines."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:341
msgid "Well, I've got one of those."
msgstr "Ben, moi j'en ai un."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:350
msgid ""
"That right? Here's the deal. You give me $2,000 and I'll sell you the car. "
"Heck I'll even install the fuel cell controller for you. Should run good as "
"new. I'll even charge it up with some extra micro fusion power cells I got."
msgstr ""
"D'accord. Voilà ce qu'on va faire. Je te vends la voiture pour $2000. "
"J'installerai même le contrôleur de transmission. Elle sera comme neuve. Et "
"j'ajouterai aussi quelques cellules à micro fusion."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:351
msgid "That sounds good to me. Here's the money and the part."
msgstr "Ca marche. Tiens, voilà l'argent et la pièce."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:352
msgid ""
"I don't think I want to do that right now. Let me ask you about something "
"else, Smitty."
msgstr ""
"Ca m'intéresse pas pour le moment. J'aimerais te poser une autre question, "
"Smitty."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:353
msgid "Let me think about it. I'll see you around, Smitty."
msgstr "Je vais y réfléchir. A un de ces quatre, Smitty."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:370
msgid "Jist take it easy with her 'til she warms up, now."
msgstr "Vas-y doucement, laisse-lui le temps de se chauffer !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:371
msgid "OK, I will. Thanks, Smitty."
msgstr "D'accord. Merci Smitty."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:380
msgid "Well, a lot an' not so much at the same time."
msgstr "Bon, c'est beaucoup et pas beaucoup en même temps."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:390
msgid ""
"What I'm saying is that havin' a regulator is nice but you need to find a "
"fuel cell controller."
msgstr ""
"Bon, c'est bien d'avoir un Régulateur de carburant, mais il te faut un "
"Contrôleur de transmission."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:391 dialog/tribec1.msg:341
msgid "Why's that?"
msgstr "Pourquoi ça ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:400
msgid ""
"'Cause if'n you had a controller, and $2,000, I could fix this here "
"Chrysalis Motors Highwayman that I got here and you could drive around in "
"style."
msgstr ""
"Parce que si tu avais un contrôleur de transmission et $2 000, je pourrais "
"te réparer la Chrysalis Motors Highwayman que j'ai ici et tu aurais beaucoup "
"de style."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:401
msgid "Really? Where can I find a fuel cell controller?"
msgstr "Ah bon ? Où puis-je trouver un contrôleur de transmission ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:410
msgid ""
"Now that's a silly question. Don't you think if I knew that then I'd be "
"driving around in the car?"
msgstr ""
"Quelle question idiote ! Si je le savais, tu crois pas que je serais déjà en "
"train de conduire cette bagnole ?!"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:411
msgid "Wow. I'll have to look for one of those."
msgstr "Ohhh ! Il faut que je trouve un de ces trucs."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:420
msgid ""
"Be a good idea. If you find one jist come on back here with it. Oh, and don' "
"forget the $2,000, neither."
msgstr ""
"Ca serait bien. Si t'en trouves, reviens vite ici avec. Oh, et n'oublie pas "
"non plus les $2000."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:421
msgid "Sounds like a plan, Smitty. Hey, let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""
"Ca a l'air d'un super plan, Smitty. Hé, j'aimerais te poser une autre "
"question."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:422
msgid "I'm going to go look for one right now. Goodbye."
msgstr "Je vais en chercher un tout de suite. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:430
msgid "Hey there, how's that car runnin' for ya?"
msgstr "Salut ! Elle roule bien cette bagnole ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:431
msgid ""
"Pretty good, Smitty, but I found this part for the car and I don't know what "
"to do with it."
msgstr ""
"Pas mal, Smitty. Mais j'ai trouvé cette pièce pour la voiture et je ne sais "
"pas quoi en faire."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:432
msgid ""
"Great, Smitty, just great. Hey, I brought you a meal. Compliments of Mom."
msgstr ""
"Super Smitty, génial. Hé, je t'ai apporté le repas. Avec les compliments de "
"la Mamma."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:433
msgid "Real good, Smitty, real good. Thanks. See you around. Goodbye."
msgstr ""
"Très bien Smitty, vraiment très bien. Merci. A un de ces jours. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:450
msgid ""
"Well now, that's a fuel cell regulator. That'll give you better mileage per "
"energy cell. I could put that in for you, if you had say $750 for my trouble."
msgstr ""
"Bon, c'est un régulateur de carburant, ça réduit la consommation de "
"carburant par cellule énergétique. Je peux te l'installer si tu as $750 pour "
"le dérangement."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:451
msgid "That sounds like a deal, Smitty. Here's the part and the money."
msgstr "Tope là, Smitty. Voici la pièce et l'argent."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:452
msgid "I'll have to think about it, Smitty. Goodbye for now."
msgstr "Il faut que je réfléchisse, Smitty. A bientôt."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:460
msgid ""
"Mostly I just keep watch over all this old junk. Only got one thing worth "
"doodly-squat."
msgstr ""
"Je surveille ce tas de ferraille. Il y a un seul truc ici qui vaut quelque "
"chose."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:462
msgid "I figured that. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr "J'avais remarqué. J'aimerais te poser une autre question."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:470
msgid ""
"Why, it's none other than this Chrysalis Motors Highwayman. They used ta say "
"that \"Nothing can stop a Highwayman.\" They shore built 'em tough, I'll say "
"that for 'em."
msgstr ""
"Rien d'autre que cette Chrysalis Motors Highwayman. \"Rien n'arrête une "
"Highwayman !\" disait la pub. Construite pour durer."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:471
msgid "Wow, does it run?"
msgstr "Génial ! Est-ce qu'elle roule ?"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:480
msgid "If'n it ran, do you think I'd still be in this shithole of a town?"
msgstr ""
"Si elle roulait, tu crois que je serait encore en train de pourrir dans ce "
"bled ?!"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:481 dialog/qcbird.msg:146
msgid "Uh, yes."
msgstr "Heu, oui."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:482
msgid "I guess not."
msgstr "J'imagine que non."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:490
msgid "Well, you're probably right. I got kinda settled in here."
msgstr "Ouais bon, tu as probablement raison. J'me suis habitué à vivre ici."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:500
msgid "Well, then again, mebbe' I would too. I got all comfortable here."
msgstr "Oui c'est bien possible... Il y a tout le confort dont j'ai besoin ici."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:510
msgid ""
"I wouldn't mind selling the car though. If someone brought me the battery - "
"no strike that, uh, I guess I'd need a fuel cell controller. Yeah, if'n I "
"had one of them, I'd sell the car for $2,000. Even install the controller so "
"it'd run right."
msgstr ""
"J'aimerais bien vendre cette voiture. Si quelqu'un m'apportait la batterie - "
"heu, non oublie ça... J'aurais besoin d'un contrôleur de transmission. "
"Ouais. Si seulement j'en avais un... Je vendrais ma voiture pour $2 000. "
"Pour ce prix, j'installerais même le contrôleur."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:511
msgid ""
"That sounds interesting. I'll have to come back if I ever find a fuel cell "
"controller. Let me ask you something else right now."
msgstr ""
"Ca m'a l'air intéressant. Si je trouve un contrôleur de transmission, je "
"reviens. Mais dis-moi..."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:512
msgid "When I find one, I'll be back. Goodbye, Smitty."
msgstr "Si j'en trouve un, je reviens ici. Au revoir, Smitty."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:520
msgid "There you go. Better'n new. Take it easy with her now."
msgstr "Et voilà. Mieux qu'une neuve. Ne la brusque pas !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:521
msgid "I will. Thanks, Smitty. Goodbye."
msgstr "D'accord. Merci Smitty. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:600
msgid "YOU GET THE HELL AWAY FROM MY CAR!"
msgstr "NE T'APPROCHE PAS DE MA BAGNOLE !"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:650
msgid "Don't let me catch you sneaking around my car like that again."
msgstr "Gare à toi si je te vois encore tourner autour de ma bagnole !!"

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:651
msgid "You won't."
msgstr "C'est bon, j'arrête."

#: dialog/dcsmitty.msg:652
msgid "Uggg-K"
msgstr "Ok."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:100 dialog/kcggcust.msg:103 dialog/vcbarpat.msg:101
msgid "You see a bar patron."
msgstr "Tu vois une cliente du bar."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:101
msgid "You see Leanne."
msgstr "Tu vois Leanne."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:102
msgid "She's very beautiful, but seems to be lost in thought."
msgstr "Elle est vraiment superbe, mais elle semble perdue dans ses pensées."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:104
msgid "Why are you doing this?"
msgstr "Pourquoi fais-tu ça !"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:106 dialog/dcstory2.msg:107 game/cmbatai2.msg:2002
#: game/cmbatai2.msg:2103 game/combatai.msg:2002 game/combatai.msg:2103
msgid "Please stop!"
msgstr "Je t'en prie, arrête !"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:107 dialog/dcstory2.msg:108
msgid "You murderer!"
msgstr "Tu es un assassin !"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:108
msgid "How could you do that to Becky!"
msgstr "Comment as-tu pu faire ça à Babeth !"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:109
msgid "What did she do to you?"
msgstr "Que t'avait-elle fait ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:110
msgid "You'll rot in hell."
msgstr "Tu vas brûler en enfer."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:111
msgid "Sorry, all out of stories."
msgstr "Excuse-moi, je n'ai plus d'histoires."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:112
msgid "Thanks for the drink."
msgstr "Merci pour le verre."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:113
msgid "Pleasure talking to you."
msgstr "Ca a été un plaisir de parler avec toi."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:114
msgid "Thanks for listening."
msgstr "Merci de m'avoir écouté."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:115 dialog/mcslag.msg:302
msgid "Nice to see you again."
msgstr "Ca fait plaisir de te revoir."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:116
msgid "Safe travels."
msgstr "Bon voyage."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:117
msgid ""
"Why hello! Nice to see a new face around here. My name's Leanne. How are "
"you? Care to sit down?"
msgstr ""
"Eh, bonjour ! Ca fait plaisir de voir une nouvelle tête ici. Je m'appelle "
"Leanne. Je t'en prie, assieds-toi !"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:118
msgid "Hello again. Doing well, I hope?"
msgstr "Rebonjour. J'espère que ça va ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:119
msgid "So, tell me what you know about the Master."
msgstr "Bon, dis-moi ce que tu sais à propos du Maître."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:120
msgid "Great. How are things with you?"
msgstr "Formidable. Comment ça va pour toi ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:122
msgid "Can't talk right now. Bye."
msgstr "Je ne peux pas parler pour le moment. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:123
msgid "Igsby?"
msgstr "Igsby ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:124
msgid "Bgy."
msgstr "Bgy."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:131
msgid "Oh, I'm sorry. I don't understand. Perhaps you shouldn't drink so much."
msgstr ""
"Oh, pardon. Je ne comprends pas. Tu ne devrais peut-être pas boire autant."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:132 dialog/dcstory2.msg:132
msgid "Ugra."
msgstr "Ugra."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:133 dialog/dcstory2.msg:133
msgid "Fegi."
msgstr "Fegi."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:134
msgid ""
"Oh, very good. Thanks for asking. Becky has such an interesting family "
"history. Do you have one yourself?"
msgstr ""
"Oh, très bien. Merci de demander. Babeth a une histoire de famille si "
"intéressante. Et toi, en as-tu une ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:135
msgid ""
"Still doing good, thanks. Now where were we? I think you were talking about "
"your family history?"
msgstr ""
"Encore en train de remercier. Bon, où en étions-nous ? Je crois que tu "
"parlais de l'histoire de ta famille ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:136
msgid ""
"Yes. I am the Chosen One. My ancestor saved the world from one called the "
"Master."
msgstr ""
"Oui. Je suis l'Etre Elu. Mon ancêtre a sauvé le monde d'un personnage appelé "
"le Maître."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:137
msgid ""
"Yeah. My ancestor supposedly saved the world from someone called the "
"'Master.'"
msgstr ""
"Ouais. Mon ancêtre a soi-disant sauvé le monde d'un personnage appelé le « "
"Maître »."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:138 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:118 dialog/octhearn.msg:116
#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:116
msgid "I've got to go."
msgstr "Je dois partir."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:139
msgid ""
"Uh, okay. Nice to meet you Chosen One... Actually, I've heard something "
"about a master before..."
msgstr ""
"Euh, Ok. Ravi de te voir, Etre Elu... Vraiment. J'ai entendu parler de "
"quelque chose à propos d'un maître..."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:140
msgid ""
"How interesting. That reminds me of a story I heard a long time ago. "
"Something about a master."
msgstr ""
"C'est intéressant. Ca me rappelle une histoire que j'ai entendue il y a très "
"longtemps. Quelque chose à propos d'un maître."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:141
msgid "Really? What was it?"
msgstr "Vraiment ? Et de quoi s'agissait-il ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:142 dialog/nclloyd.msg:357
msgid "Tell me."
msgstr "Dis-moi."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:144
msgid ""
"Well this might take a bit. Be a gentleman and buy me a drink, wouldn't you "
"please? Not whiskey though, Nuka-Cola please."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, ça va prendre un peu de temps. Sois galant et offre-moi un verre, "
"d'accord ? Pas de whisky, du Nuka-Cola, s'il te plaît."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:145
msgid ""
"Well this might take a bit. Be a doll and buy me a drink, wouldn't you "
"please? Not whiskey though, Nuka-Cola please."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, ça va prendre un peu de temps. Sois gentille et offre-moi un verre, "
"d'accord ? Pas de whisky, du Nuka-Cola, s'il te plaît."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:146
msgid "Shall we get started? I remember it quite well now."
msgstr "Peut-on commencer ? Je m'en rappelle assez bien maintenant."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:148
msgid "Sorry, I can't spare $5 right now."
msgstr "Pardon, mais je ne peux pas dépenser $5 pour le moment."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:149
msgid ""
"Thanks. Now let's see... I remember my mom telling me about this huge "
"migration that happened 70... or was it 80 years ago..."
msgstr ""
"Merci. Bon, maintenant, voyons voir... Ma mère m'a parlé de cette vaste "
"migration qu'il y a eu il y a 70 ans... Ou était-ce 80 ans."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:150
msgid "Please, go on."
msgstr "Elle est très belle, mais elle a l'air d'être perdue dans ses pensées."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:151
msgid ""
"Really big mutants with weapons as tall as you and me came from the south. "
"Mom said it looked like a big migration of some sort."
msgstr ""
"De très grands mutants avec des armes aussi grandes que toi et moi sont "
"venus du Sud. La Mamma disait que c'était comme une vaste migration."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:152
msgid "How many?"
msgstr "Combien ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:153
msgid ""
"Don't know, but there were multiple groups of them. Some would continue "
"north, others headed east. No one knew where they were going."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas, mais il y en avait des tas de groupes. Certains ont continué "
"vers le Nord, d'autres se sont dirigés vers l'Est. Personne ne savait où ils "
"allaient."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:155
msgid "They were quite upset and seemed to be fleeing from something."
msgstr "Ils avaient l'air inquiet et semblaient fuir quelque chose."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:157
msgid ""
"Yeah, there were also others in dirty, tattered purple robes... they kept "
"babbling about how the Master was dead..."
msgstr ""
"Ouais. Et il y en avait d'autres qui portaient des robes violettes en "
"lambeaux... Ils n'arrêtaient pas de parler de la manière dont le Maître "
"était mort..."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:158 dialog/kcsmiley.msg:181 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:157
msgid "Interesting."
msgstr "Intéressant."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:159
msgid "Some of them even committed suicide right here in town!"
msgstr "Certains se sont même suicidés, ici, dans la ville !"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:160 dialog/gcpercy.msg:144 dialog/qccurlng.msg:207
msgid "So?"
msgstr "Et alors ?"

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:161
msgid ""
"Well don't you see. They were talking about the Master, the one your "
"ancestor killed."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, tu ne comprends pas. Ils parlaient du Maître, celui que ton ancêtre "
"a tué."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:163
msgid "Well, it's getting late. Bye."
msgstr "Bon, il se fait tard. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:164 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:204
msgid "My pleasure. Bye."
msgstr "Ce fut un plaisir. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dcstory1.msg:167
msgid "Leanne told you her story about the Master."
msgstr "Leanne t'a raconté son histoire sur le Maître."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:100
msgid "You see bar patron."
msgstr "Tu vois une cliente du bar."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:101
msgid "You see Stacy."
msgstr "Tu vois Stacy."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:102
msgid "She seems to be a little sad."
msgstr "Elle a l'air un peu triste."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:104
msgid "How could you?"
msgstr "Comment as-tu pu ?"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:109
msgid "Poor Mom! You'll pay for that!"
msgstr "Pauvre Mamma ! Tu vas payer pour ça !"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:110
msgid "Mom..."
msgstr "Mamma..."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:111
msgid "But she was so nice to everyone..."
msgstr "Mais elle était si gentille avec tout le monde..."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:112
msgid "Sorry, can't think of anything else interesting."
msgstr "Je regrette, mais je ne vois rien d'autre d'intéressant."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:113
msgid "My brains all dried up."
msgstr "Mon cerveau est desséché."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:114 dialog/scmerk.msg:201
msgid "That's it."
msgstr "Voilà."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:116
msgid "Have you said hi to Mom yet?"
msgstr "Tu as déjà dit bonjour à Mamma ?"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:117
msgid "Oh, hi."
msgstr "Oh, salut."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:118
msgid "Oh, you again."
msgstr "Oh, encore toi."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:119
msgid "Tell me about your cat."
msgstr "Parle-moi de ton chat."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:120
msgid "Why the glum face?"
msgstr "Pourquoi cet air triste ?"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:121
msgid "You come here often?"
msgstr "Tu viens souvent ici ?"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:122
msgid "I'll have to catch you later. Bye."
msgstr "Je t'aurai plus tard. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:123
msgid "Okah?"
msgstr "Ok ?"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:131
msgid "Please don't bother me. I'm really not in the mood right now."
msgstr "Ne me dérange pas. Je ne suis pas d'humeur pour le moment."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:134
msgid ""
"Oh, nothing really. Just sometimes I get thinking about my mom and cat. I "
"miss them so very much."
msgstr ""
"Oh, rien, vraiment. C'est juste que parfois, je me mets à penser à ma maman "
"et à la chatte. Ils me manquent tant."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:135
msgid "Cat?"
msgstr "Une chatte ?"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:136
msgid "Sorry to hear that. Bye."
msgstr "Je regrette d'entendre ça. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:137
msgid ""
"Yeah, Cuddles. She was such a sweet cat. I really don't feel like talking "
"about it... Well, unless you'd like to buy me a drink. That might help."
msgstr ""
"Ouais, Caresses. C'était une gentille chatte. Je n'ai pas vraiment envie "
"d'en parler... Bon, à moins que tu m'offres un verre. Ca pourrait m'aider."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:138
msgid ""
"As I said, I would prefer not to talk about it right now. If you'd like to "
"buy me a drink, it might loosen my tongue."
msgstr ""
"Comme je te l'ai dit, je préfère ne pas en parler pour le moment. Mais si tu "
"m'offres un verre, ça me déliera peut-être la langue."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:139
msgid "Of course I will. I'd love to hear about it."
msgstr "D'accord. J'aimerais vraiment que tu m'en parles."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:141
msgid "Sorry, I can't spare $10 right now."
msgstr "Je regrette, mais je n'ai pas $10 à dépenser pour le moment."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:142
msgid "Obviously."
msgstr "Evidemment."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:143
msgid "Do you think you're funny or something? Get a better line."
msgstr "Tu te trouves drôle ? Trouve autre chose. "

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:144
msgid "So why the glum face?"
msgstr "Alors, pourquoi cet air triste ?"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:146
msgid ""
"I hear there used to be ones that were as big as you and me. They used to "
"eat animals as big as a brahmin. Now that's scary stuff."
msgstr ""
"J'ai entendu dire qu'il y en avait d'aussi grands que toi et moi. Ils "
"mangeaient des animaux aussi grands qu'une Brahmine. Maintenant, ça fait "
"bizarre."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:147
msgid "That's nothing."
msgstr "Ce n'est rien."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:148
msgid "Yeah, it is."
msgstr "Ouais."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:149
msgid ""
"The kind I'm talking about is a small cute animal, bigger than a rat but "
"smaller than a dog. Some are fluffy, like my Cuddles, but others have short "
"hair."
msgstr ""
"Celui dont je parle était un adorable animal, plus grand qu'un rat, mais "
"plus petit qu'un chien. Certains ont beaucoup de poils, comme ma Caresses, "
"d'autres ont les poils ras."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:151
msgid ""
"They like to be pet like a dog does, but cats make this wonderful relaxing "
"sound when you pet them."
msgstr ""
"Ils aiment être caressés comme les chiens, mais les chats font ce doux et "
"merveilleux ronronnement lorsqu'on les caresse."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:152
msgid "Strange."
msgstr "Etrange."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:153
msgid ""
"Cuddles always used to help me go to sleep at night. I think of her every "
"night when I try to go to sleep."
msgstr ""
"Caresses m'aidait à m'endormir le soir. Je pense tous les soirs à elle "
"lorsque j'essaie de m'endormir."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:154
msgid "Sounds nice."
msgstr "Ca a l'air bien."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:156
msgid ""
"I had her when I was a kid, but she disappeared. I didn't know then what "
"happened to her, I was too young."
msgstr ""
"Je l'avais lorsque j'étais enfant, mais elle a disparu. Je n'ai jamais su ce "
"qui lui était arrivé, j'étais trop petite."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:158
msgid ""
"Well, food was awfully scarce back then and people had to eat. It's quite "
"sad really..."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, la nourriture était très rare en ce temps-là et les gens avaient "
"besoin de se nourrir. C'est vraiment triste."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:160
msgid ""
"People would hunt them because they were such easy prey. None of them are "
"around anymore because of it."
msgstr ""
"Les gens les chassaient car c'étaient des proies faciles. C'est pour ça "
"qu'ils ont tous disparu."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:161
msgid "Sick!"
msgstr "Malade !"

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:162
msgid "I can understand that."
msgstr "Je peux comprendre ça."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:163
msgid ""
"Those were the wild ones, but I'm sure that's what happened to mine. Now I "
"know why Mom always kept a close eye on her."
msgstr ""
"Ceux-là étaient sauvages, mais je pense vraiment que c'est ce qui est arrivé "
"à la mienne. Maintenant, je sais pourquoi maman gardait toujours un oeil sur "
"elle."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:164
msgid "How sad."
msgstr "C'est triste."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:167
msgid "It makes me sad to think about it..."
msgstr "Je suis triste rien que d'y penser..."

#: dialog/dcstory2.msg:169
msgid "Stacy told you a sweet story about her darling cat Cuddles."
msgstr ""
"Stacy t'a raconté une belle histoire à propos de Caresses, sa chatte adorée."

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:150
msgid "The thug looks pretty ruthless."
msgstr "Le voyou a l'air assez cruel."

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:151
msgid "Get out of my face."
msgstr "Dégage de là ! "

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:152
msgid "You lookin' for trouble?"
msgstr "Tu cherches les emmerdes ?"

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:153
msgid "Keep right on walking."
msgstr "Continue à marcher."

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:154 dialog/scvortis.msg:203 dialog/shtandi.msg:273
msgid "Not interested."
msgstr "Pas intéressé."

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:200
msgid "Hey punk."
msgstr "Hé, sale crapule !"

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:201
msgid "You want some trouble?"
msgstr "Tu cherches la merde ?"

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:202
msgid "Come here, sissy."
msgstr "Viens ici, femmelette."

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:203
msgid "Don't make me come over there and beat your ass."
msgstr "Je vais venir te botter les fesses, si tu continues !"

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:204
msgid "You talking to me?"
msgstr "C'est à moi que tu parles ?"

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:205 dialog/ecwash.msg:441 game/cmbatai2.msg:32344
#: game/combatai.msg:18141 game/combatai.msg:32344 game/combatai.msg:41721
msgid "You want some of this?"
msgstr "Vous en voulez de ça ?"

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:206
msgid "Hey baby, come here."
msgstr "Hé, mon chou, viens voir ici."

#: dialog/dcthug.msg:207
msgid "Hey, you like what you see?"
msgstr "Hé, ça t'plaît c'que tu vois ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:100
msgid "You see the shop owner."
msgstr "Tu vois le propriétaire du magasin."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:101
msgid "You see Tubby."
msgstr "Tu vois Dodu."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:150
msgid "This is the store owner."
msgstr "Tu vois le propriétaire du magasin."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:151
msgid "This is Tubby, the shop store owner."
msgstr "Voici Dodu, le propriétaire du magasin."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:153
msgid "I would prefer that you take your business elsewhere."
msgstr "J'aimerais mieux que t'ailles faire tes affaires ailleurs."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:154
msgid "You are a business man. Let's conduct business."
msgstr "T'es un homme d'affaires. Alors, parlons affaires."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:155
msgid "Can I ask you something."
msgstr "Je peux te demander quelque chose."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:157
msgid "I am so happy to see you again. What can I do for you today?"
msgstr ""
"Je suis tellement content de te revoir. Je peux faire quelque chose pour toi "
"aujourd'hui ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:159
msgid "Can I ask you something?"
msgstr "Je peux te poser une question."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:160
msgid "Nothing for now. Bye."
msgstr "Rien pour le moment. Salut."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:161
msgid ""
"Hello, sir, and welcome to Tubby's. I am the proprietor. May I help\n"
" you?"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour Monsieur, et bienvenu chez Dodu. Je suis le propriétaire. Je peux "
"vous aider ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:162
msgid "Yes, let's trade."
msgstr "Oui, faisons du business."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:163 dialog/dctubby.msg:167
msgid "I need some information."
msgstr "J'aimerais quelques renseignements."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:165
msgid ""
"Hello, madam. I am called Tubby by my friends, and I welcome you\n"
" to my store. How may I help you?"
msgstr ""
"Bonjour Madame. Mes amis m'appellent Dodu. Je vous souhaite la bienvenue "
"dans mon magasin. Que désirez-vous ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:166
msgid "I want to buy some things."
msgstr "J'ai des choses à acheter."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:169
msgid "I would prefer that you leave, instead."
msgstr "Je préférerais que tu partes."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:172
msgid "Who's in charge of this town?"
msgstr "Qui est responsable de la ville ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:173
msgid "Why is everyone selling drugs?"
msgstr "Pourquoi tout le monde vend-il des stimulants ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:174
msgid "Do you know where the Vault is located?"
msgstr "Sais-tu où se trouve l'Abri ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:175
msgid "I would like to barter after all."
msgstr "Je voudrais faire du troc finalement."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:176 dialog/ocsandy.msg:125
msgid "Never mind. Bye"
msgstr "Tant pis. Au revoir."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:177
msgid ""
"Oh my. I can tell we will have a communication problem. Please nod\n"
" if you would like to trade any goods."
msgstr ""
"Ah, on risque d'avoir quelques problèmes de communication ! Fais *oui* avec "
"la tête si tu veux bien échanger des marchandises."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:178
msgid "[Nod]"
msgstr "[Faire oui de la tête]"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:179
msgid "Byebye."
msgstr "Salut."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:180
msgid ""
"No one, I'm afraid. The Den is an anarchistic place where a kind of\n"
" Darwinian struggle is played out. Only the strongest, fastest or smartest\n"
" will survive here. I'm sure you will find your niche."
msgstr ""
"Personne. La Fosse est un lieu anarchique où se livre une espèce de combat "
"darwinien. Seuls les plus forts, les plus rapides ou les plus intelligents "
"survivent ici. J'ai la certitude que tu trouveras ta place."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:181
msgid "Um, thanks."
msgstr "Hum, merci."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:182
msgid ""
"OK. Drugs are the basis for this town's economic system, just as another \n"
"town may use grain or gold. Redding is another prime example of a town "
"fueled by drugs.\n"
" Damn miners are too high all the time to get any real work done. I have "
"never been there myself,\n"
" but it is a couple days south-east of here if you want to check it out."
msgstr ""
"Alors... Les stimulants sont au centre du système économique de cette ville. "
"D'autres villes ont des céréales ou de l'or. Redding est un autre exemple de "
"ville qui carbure à la drogue. Les gars de la mine sont trop shootés pour "
"faire leur boulot correctement. Je n'y suis jamais allé moi-même, mais c'est "
"à quelques jours d'ici au Sud-Est si tu veux aller voir."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:184
msgid ""
"I have heard of a place called Vault City. But unfortunately, I can't\n"
" help you with directions. You see, very few of us towns can offer "
"acceptable\n"
" exchange for the medical services they provide, so most of us have never "
"been\n"
" there."
msgstr ""
"J'ai entendu parler de la Cité de l'Abri. Malheureusement, je ne sais pas "
"comment on s'y rend. La plupart de nos villes n'offrent rien d'acceptable en "
"échange des services médicaux qu'ils fournissent, alors beaucoup ne sont "
"jamais allés là-bas."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:185
msgid "OK. Thanks."
msgstr "D'accord. Merci."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:186
msgid "That's not the kind of information I would just GIVE away to anyone."
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas le genre de renseignement que je DONNE comme ça à n'importe qui "
"!"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:187
msgid "Would a hundred bucks change your mind?"
msgstr "Une centaine de dollars, ça te ferait changer d'avis ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:188
msgid "How about I give you $50 and you tell me."
msgstr "Je te donne $50 et tu me le dis."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:189
msgid ""
"What do you say you give me the information, or I give you a new hole\n"
" in the head."
msgstr ""
"A toi de voir, tu me donnes ces renseignements ou je fais un trou dans ta "
"jolie tête."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:191
msgid "Well, can I ask you something else, then?"
msgstr "Eh bien, je peux te poser une autre question ?"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:192
msgid ""
"Sure, that kind of money MIGHT help me change my mind. But you ain't got\n"
" it!"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr. Cet argent POURRAIT me faire changer d'avis. Mais tu l'as pas !"

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:193
msgid "I must have dropped it somewhere. I'm gonna go look for it."
msgstr "J'ai dû le laisser tomber quelque part. Je vais le chercher."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:194
msgid "I don't think that's going to be enough."
msgstr "Je ne crois pas que ça sera assez."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:500
msgid "Sure Petey. I'll be there in a second."
msgstr "Bien sûr, Pierrot. Je suis à toi dans une seconde."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:501
msgid "Hold on, Petey!"
msgstr "Attends, Pierrot."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:502
msgid "I'm comin', I'm comin'."
msgstr "Je viens, je viens."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:510
msgid "Here you go, Petey."
msgstr "Et voilà, Pierrot."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:511
msgid "You know, Petey, you should kick this shit."
msgstr "Tu sais, Pierrot, tu devrais arrêter les stimulants."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:512
msgid "Take this and get the hell outta here, Petey."
msgstr "Tiens Pierrot, prends ça et fiche-moi le camp d'ici."

#: dialog/dctubby.msg:520 dialog/scvortis.msg:172
msgid "Pleasure doing business."
msgstr "C'est un plaisir de faire des affaires."

#: dialog/dctubfri.msg:110
msgid "You see a Jet whore."
msgstr "Tu vois une prostituée fidèle au Jet."

#: dialog/dctubfri.msg:111
msgid "You see one of Tubby's Jet whores."
msgstr "Tu vois une prostituée fidèle au Jet, c'est une des filles de Dodu."

#: dialog/dctubfri.msg:150
msgid "He seems to be a friend of Tubby's."
msgstr "On dirait un ami de Dodu."

#: dialog/dctubfri.msg:160
msgid "She seems to be extremely doped up."
msgstr "Elle a l'air complètement défaite."

#: dialog/dctubfri.msg:161
